-- # Class: AdjustableDate Description: A class for defining a date that shall be subject to adjustment if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day in the specified business centers, together with the convention for adjusting the date.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: unadjustedDate Description: A date subject to adjustment. While in FpML this date is required, this cardinality constraint has been relaxed as part of the CDM in order to support the FRA representation, which effective and termination dates are specified in FpML as adjusted dates.
--     * Slot: adjustedDate Description: The date once the adjustment has been performed. (Note that this date may change if the business center holidays change).
--     * Slot: dateAdjustments_id Description: The business day convention and financial business centers used for adjusting the date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business date in the specified business centers.
--     * Slot: dateAdjustmentsReference_id Description: A pointer style reference to date adjustments defined elsewhere in the document.
-- # Class: AdjustableDates Description: A class for defining a series of dates that shall be subject to adjustment if they would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day in the specified business centers, together with the convention for adjusting the dates.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: dateAdjustments_id Description: The business day convention and financial business centers used for adjusting the date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business date in the specified business centers.
-- # Class: AdjustableOrAdjustedDate Description: A class for defining a date that shall be subject to adjustment if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day in the specified business centers, together with the convention for adjusting the date.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: unadjustedDate Description: A date subject to adjustment.
--     * Slot: adjustedDate Description: The date once the adjustment has been performed. (Note that this date may change if the business center holidays change).
--     * Slot: dateAdjustments_id Description: The business day convention and financial business centers used for adjusting the date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business date in the specified business centers.
-- # Class: AdjustableOrAdjustedOrRelativeDate Description: This Rosetta class specifies the date as either an unadjusted, adjusted or relative date. It supplements the features of the AdjustableOrAdjustedDate to support the credit default swap option premium, which uses the relative date construct.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: unadjustedDate Description: A date subject to adjustment.
--     * Slot: adjustedDate Description: The date once the adjustment has been performed. (Note that this date may change if the business center holidays change).
--     * Slot: dateAdjustments_id Description: The business day convention and financial business centers used for adjusting the date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business date in the specified business centers.
--     * Slot: relativeDate_id Description: A date specified as some offset to another date (the anchor date).
-- # Class: AdjustableOrRelativeDate Description: A class giving the choice between defining a date as an explicit date together with applicable adjustments or as relative to some other (anchor) date.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: adjustableDate_id Description: A date that shall be subject to adjustment if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day in the specified business centers, together with the convention for adjusting the date.
--     * Slot: relativeDate_id Description: A date specified as some offset to another date (the anchor date).
-- # Class: AdjustableOrRelativeDates Description: A class giving the choice between defining a series of dates as an explicit list of dates together with applicable adjustments or as relative to some other series of (anchor) dates.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: adjustableDates_id Description: A series of dates that shall be subject to adjustment if they would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day in the specified business centers, together with the convention for adjusting the date.
--     * Slot: relativeDates_id Description: A series of dates specified as some offset to another series of dates (the anchor dates).
-- # Class: AdjustableRelativeOrPeriodicDates Description: A class giving the choice between defining a series of dates as an explicit list of dates together with applicable adjustments or as relative to some other series of (anchor) dates, or as a calculation period schedule.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: adjustableDates_id Description: A series of dates that shall be subject to adjustment if they would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day in the specified business centers, together with the convention for adjusting the date.
--     * Slot: relativeDates_id Description: A series of dates specified as some offset to another series of dates (the anchor dates).
--     * Slot: periodicDates_id Description: A calculation period schedule.
-- # Class: AdjustedRelativeDateOffset Description: A type defining a date (referred to as the derived date) as a relative offset from another date (referred to as the anchor date) plus optional date adjustments.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: businessDayConvention Description: The convention for adjusting a date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day, as specified by an ISDA convention (e.g. Following, Precedent).
--     * Slot: dateRelativeTo Description: Specifies the anchor as an href attribute. The href attribute value is a pointer style reference to the element or component elsewhere in the document where the anchor date is defined.
--     * Slot: adjustedDate Description: The date once the adjustment has been performed. (Note that this date may change if the business center holidays change).
--     * Slot: dayType Description: In the case of an offset specified as a number of days, this element defines whether consideration is given as to whether a day is a good business day or not. If a day type of business days is specified then non-business days are ignored when calculating the offset. The financial business centers to use for determination of business days are implied by the context in which this element is used. This element must only be included when the offset is specified as a number of days. If the offset is zero days then the dayType element should not be included.
--     * Slot: periodMultiplier Description: A time period multiplier, e.g. 1, 2 or 3 etc. A negative value can be used when specifying an offset relative to another date, e.g. -2 days.
--     * Slot: period Description: A time period, e.g. a day, week, month or year of the stream. If the periodMultiplier value is 0 (zero) then period must contain the value D (day).
--     * Slot: relativeDateAdjustments_id Description: The business day convention and financial business centers used for adjusting the relative date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business date in the specified business centers.
--     * Slot: businessCenters_id
--     * Slot: businessCentersReference_id Description: A pointer style reference to a set of financial business centers defined elsewhere in the document. This set of business centers is used to determine whether a particular day is a business day or not.
-- # Class: AveragingSchedule Description: Class to representing a method for generating a series of dates.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: startDate Description: Date on which this period begins.
--     * Slot: endDate Description: Date on which this period ends.
--     * Slot: averagingPeriodFrequency_id Description: The frequency at which averaging period occurs with the regular part of the valuation schedule and their roll date convention.
-- # Class: BusinessCenterTime Description: A class for defining a time with respect to a business day calendar location. For example, 11:00:00 GBLO.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: hourMinuteTime Description: A time specified in hh:mm:ss format where the second component must be '00', e.g. 11am would be represented as 11:00:00.
--     * Slot: businessCenter Description: A code identifying a business day calendar location. A business day calendar location is drawn from the list identified by the business day calendar location enumeration.
-- # Class: BusinessCenters Description: A class for specifying the business day calendar location used in determining whether a day is a business day or not, either by specifying this business center by reference to an enumerated list that is maintained by the FpML standard, or by reference to such specification when it exists elsewhere as part of the instance document. This class corresponds to the FpML BusinessCentersOrReference.model.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: businessCentersReference_id Description: A reference to a financial business center location specified elsewhere in the instance document.
-- # Class: BusinessDateRange Description: A class defining a range of contiguous business days by defining an unadjusted first date, an unadjusted last date and a business day convention and business centers for adjusting the first and last dates if they would otherwise fall on a non business day in the specified business centers. The days between the first and last date must also be good business days in the specified centers to be counted in the range.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: businessDayConvention Description: The convention for adjusting a date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day, as specified by an ISDA convention (e.g. Following, Precedent).
--     * Slot: startDate Description: The first date of a date range.
--     * Slot: endDate Description: The last date of a date range.
--     * Slot: businessCenters_id Description: The business center(s), specified either explicitly or by reference to those specified somewhere else in the instance document.
-- # Class: BusinessDayAdjustments Description: A class defining the business day convention and financial business centers used for adjusting any relevant date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day in the specified business center.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: businessDayConvention Description: The convention for adjusting a date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day.
--     * Slot: businessCenters_id Description: The business center(s), specified either explicitly or by reference to those specified somewhere else in the instance document.
-- # Class: CalculationFrequency Description: Represents the parameters for describing how often something (such as collateral interest) is to be calculated.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: monthOfYear Description: Specifies the month of the year if used.
--     * Slot: dayOfMonth Description: Specifies the day of the month if used.
--     * Slot: dayOfWeek Description: Specifies the day of the week if used.
--     * Slot: weekOfMonth Description: Specifies the week of the month if used.
--     * Slot: offsetDays Description: Specifies how many days from the trigger event should the payment occur.
--     * Slot: period_id Description: Specifies the time period at which calculation is performed, e.g. 1 month.
--     * Slot: dateLocation_id Description: Specifies where is the time measured.
-- # Class: CalculationPeriodFrequency Description: A class to specify the frequency at which calculation period end dates occur within the regular part of the calculation period schedule and their roll date convention.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: rollConvention Description: The roll convention specifies the period term as part of a periodic schedule, i.e. the calculation period end date within the regular part of the calculation period. The value could be a rule, e.g. IMM Settlement Dates, which is the 3rd Wednesday of the month, or it could be a specific day of the month, such as the first day of the applicable month. It is used in conjunction with a frequency and the regular period start date of a calculation period.
--     * Slot: balanceOfFirstPeriod Description: Indicates, when true, that that the first Calculation Period should run from the Effective Date to the end of the calendar period in which the Effective Date falls, e.g. Jan 15 - Jan 31 if the calculation periods are one month long and Effective Date is Jan 15. If false, the first Calculation Period should run from the Effective Date for one whole period, e.g. Jan 15 to Feb 14 if the calculation periods are one month long and Effective Date is Jan 15. Mostly used in Commmodity Swaps.
--     * Slot: periodMultiplier Description: A time period multiplier, e.g. 1, 2, or 3. If the period value is T (Term) then period multiplier must contain the value 1.
--     * Slot: period Description: A time period, e.g. a day, week, month, year or term of the stream.
-- # Class: CustomisableOffset Description: A class to specify an offset either as a normalized [multiplier, period, dayType] or as a custom provision of type string.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: customProvision
--     * Slot: offset_id
-- # Class: DateList Description: List of dates.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: DateRange Description: A class defining a contiguous series of calendar dates. The date range is defined as all the dates between and including the start and the end date. The start date must fall on or before the end date.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: startDate Description: The first date of a date range.
--     * Slot: endDate Description: The last date of a date range.
-- # Class: DateTimeList Description: List of dateTimes.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: DirectOrRelativeTime Description: Represents a time definition that can be either an absolute (direct) time or a time calculated relative to another referenced time. Either one directTime or one relativeTime should be provided
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: directTime_id Description: An absolute time value expressed in a specific time zone.
--     * Slot: relativeTime_id Description: A time value calculated relative to another reference time.
-- # Class: Frequency Description: A class for defining a date frequency, e.g. one day, three months, through the combination of an integer value and a standardized period value that is specified as part of an enumeration.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: periodMultiplier Description: A time period multiplier, e.g. 1, 2, or 3. If the period value is T (Term) then period multiplier must contain the value 1.
--     * Slot: period Description: A time period, e.g. a day, week, month, year or term of the stream.
-- # Class: Offset Description: A class defining an offset used in calculating a new date relative to a reference date, e.g. calendar days, business days, commodity Business days, etc.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: dayType Description: In the case of an offset specified as a number of days, this element defines whether consideration is given as to whether a day is a good business day or not. If a day type of business days is specified then non-business days are ignored when calculating the offset. The financial business centers to use for determination of business days are implied by the context in which this element is used. This element must only be included when the offset is specified as a number of days. If the offset is zero days then the dayType element should not be included.
--     * Slot: periodMultiplier Description: A time period multiplier, e.g. 1, 2 or 3 etc. A negative value can be used when specifying an offset relative to another date, e.g. -2 days.
--     * Slot: period Description: A time period, e.g. a day, week, month or year of the stream. If the periodMultiplier value is 0 (zero) then period must contain the value D (day).
-- # Class: Period Description: A class to define recurring periods or time offsets.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: periodMultiplier Description: A time period multiplier, e.g. 1, 2 or 3 etc. A negative value can be used when specifying an offset relative to another date, e.g. -2 days.
--     * Slot: period Description: A time period, e.g. a day, week, month or year of the stream. If the periodMultiplier value is 0 (zero) then period must contain the value D (day).
-- # Class: PeriodBound Description: Indicator to specify if the period bound is defined as a period and whether the bound is inclusive.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: inclusive Description: Specifies whether the period bound is inclusive, e.g. for a lower bound, false would indicate greater than, whereas true would indicate greater than or equal to.
--     * Slot: period_id Description: Specifies the period is to be used as the bound, e.g. 5Y.
-- # Class: PeriodRange Description: Indicates The period range defined as either a lower and upper period bound, or both.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: lowerBound_id Description: Specifies the lower bound of a period range, e.g. greater than or equal to 5Y.
--     * Slot: upperBound_id Description: Specifies the upper bound of a period range, e.g. less than to 10Y.
-- # Class: PeriodicDates Description: A class for specifying a calculation period schedule.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: dayType Description: Denotes the enumerated values to specify the day type classification used in counting the number of days between two dates.
--     * Slot: startDate_id Description: The start date of the calculation period. FpML specifies that for interest rate swaps this date must only be specified if it is not equal to the effective date. It is always specified in the case of equity swaps and credit default swaps with periodic payments. This date may be subject to adjustment in accordance with a business day convention.
--     * Slot: endDate_id Description: The end date of the calculation period. FpML specifies that for interest rate swaps this date must only be specified if it is not equal to the termination date. It is always specified in the case of equity swaps with periodic payments. This date may be subject to adjustment in accordance with a business day convention.
--     * Slot: periodFrequency_id Description: The frequency at which calculation period end dates occur with the regular part of the calculation period schedule and their roll date convention.
--     * Slot: periodDatesAdjustments_id Description: The specification of the business day convention and financial business centers used for adjusting any calculation period date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day in the specified business center.
-- # Class: RelativeDateOffset Description: A class defining a date (referred to as the derived date) as a relative offset from another date (referred to as the anchor date). If the anchor date is itself an adjustable date then the offset is assumed to be calculated from the adjusted anchor date. A number of different scenarios can be supported, namely; 1) the derived date may simply be a number of calendar periods (days, weeks, months or years) preceding or following the anchor date; 2) the unadjusted derived date may be a number of calendar periods (days, weeks, months or years) preceding or following the anchor date with the resulting unadjusted derived date subject to adjustment in accordance with a specified business day convention, i.e. the derived date must fall on a good business day; 3) the derived date may be a number of business days preceding or following the anchor date. Note that the businessDayConvention specifies any required adjustment to the unadjusted derived date. A negative or positive value in the periodMultiplier indicates whether the unadjusted derived precedes or follows the anchor date. The businessDayConvention should contain a value NONE if the day type element contains a value of Business (since specifying a negative or positive business days offset would already guarantee that the derived date would fall on a good business day in the specified business centers).
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: businessDayConvention Description: The convention for adjusting a date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day, as specified by an ISDA convention (e.g. Following, Precedent).
--     * Slot: dateRelativeTo Description: Specifies the anchor as an href attribute. The href attribute value is a pointer style reference to the element or component elsewhere in the document where the anchor date is defined.
--     * Slot: adjustedDate Description: The date once the adjustment has been performed. (Note that this date may change if the business center holidays change).
--     * Slot: dayType Description: In the case of an offset specified as a number of days, this element defines whether consideration is given as to whether a day is a good business day or not. If a day type of business days is specified then non-business days are ignored when calculating the offset. The financial business centers to use for determination of business days are implied by the context in which this element is used. This element must only be included when the offset is specified as a number of days. If the offset is zero days then the dayType element should not be included.
--     * Slot: periodMultiplier Description: A time period multiplier, e.g. 1, 2 or 3 etc. A negative value can be used when specifying an offset relative to another date, e.g. -2 days.
--     * Slot: period Description: A time period, e.g. a day, week, month or year of the stream. If the periodMultiplier value is 0 (zero) then period must contain the value D (day).
--     * Slot: businessCenters_id
--     * Slot: businessCentersReference_id Description: A pointer style reference to a set of financial business centers defined elsewhere in the document. This set of business centers is used to determine whether a particular day is a business day or not.
-- # Class: RelativeDates Description: A class describing a set of dates defined as relative to another set of dates.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: periodSkip Description: The number of periods in the referenced date schedule that are between each date in the relative date schedule. Thus a skip of 2 would mean that dates are relative to every second date in the referenced schedule. If present this should have a value greater than 1.
--     * Slot: businessDayConvention Description: The convention for adjusting a date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day, as specified by an ISDA convention (e.g. Following, Precedent).
--     * Slot: dateRelativeTo Description: Specifies the anchor as an href attribute. The href attribute value is a pointer style reference to the element or component elsewhere in the document where the anchor date is defined.
--     * Slot: adjustedDate Description: The date once the adjustment has been performed. (Note that this date may change if the business center holidays change).
--     * Slot: dayType Description: In the case of an offset specified as a number of days, this element defines whether consideration is given as to whether a day is a good business day or not. If a day type of business days is specified then non-business days are ignored when calculating the offset. The financial business centers to use for determination of business days are implied by the context in which this element is used. This element must only be included when the offset is specified as a number of days. If the offset is zero days then the dayType element should not be included.
--     * Slot: periodMultiplier Description: A time period multiplier, e.g. 1, 2 or 3 etc. A negative value can be used when specifying an offset relative to another date, e.g. -2 days.
--     * Slot: period Description: A time period, e.g. a day, week, month or year of the stream. If the periodMultiplier value is 0 (zero) then period must contain the value D (day).
--     * Slot: scheduleBounds_id Description: The first and last dates of a schedule. This can be used to restrict the range of values in a reference series of dates.
--     * Slot: businessCenters_id
--     * Slot: businessCentersReference_id Description: A pointer style reference to a set of financial business centers defined elsewhere in the document. This set of business centers is used to determine whether a particular day is a business day or not.
-- # Class: RelativeTime Description: Defines a time value calculated relative to a reference time. The final value is derived by applying any offset and rounding rules inherited from RelativeTimeOffset to the reference time.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: offsetTimeUnit Description: The unit of time for the offset (e.g., seconds, minutes, hours, days).
--     * Slot: offsetMultiplier Description: A time offset multiplier, e.g. 1, 2 or 3 etc. A negative value can be used when specifying a negative offset, e.g. -2 hours.
--     * Slot: timeRelativeTo_id Description: The reference time zone or base time from which the relative time is calculated.
--     * Slot: rounding_id Description: Optional rules that define how the calculated time should be rounded after the offset has been applied.
-- # Class: RelativeTimeOffset Description: Describes how a time is offset from a reference point, including the unit, magnitude, and rounding behavior.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: offsetTimeUnit Description: The unit of time for the offset (e.g., seconds, minutes, hours, days).
--     * Slot: offsetMultiplier Description: A time offset multiplier, e.g. 1, 2 or 3 etc. A negative value can be used when specifying a negative offset, e.g. -2 hours.
--     * Slot: rounding_id Description: Optional rules that define how the calculated time should be rounded after the offset has been applied.
-- # Class: TimeRounding Description: Specifies how a calculated time should be rounded, including both the direction of rounding and the unit to which the time is rounded. Rounding is applied after all offsets have been calculated.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: roundingDirection Description: The direction in which rounding is performed (e.g., up, down, or to the nearest value).
--     * Slot: roundToUnit Description: The time unit to which the value should be rounded (e.g., minute, hour, day).
-- # Class: TimeZone Description: The time alongside with the timezone location information. This class makes use of the FpML TimezoneLocation construct.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: time Description: The observation time.
--     * Slot: location Description: FpML specifies the timezoneLocationScheme by reference to the Time Zone Database (a.k.a. tz database) maintained by IANA, the Internet Assigned Numbers Authority.
-- # Class: AveragingCalculationMethod Description: Defines the ways in which multiple values can be aggregated into a single value.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isWeighted Description: Identifies whether the average values will be weighted or unweighted.
--     * Slot: calculationMethod Description: Identifies which of the Pythagorean means is being used to compute an average value.
-- # Class: DatedValue Description: Defines a date and value pair. This definition is used for varying rate or amount schedules, e.g. a notional amortisation or a step-up coupon schedule.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: date Description: The date on which the associated step value becomes effective. This day may be subject to adjustment in accordance with a business day convention.
--     * Slot: value Description: The rate of amount which becomes effective on the associated step date. A rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
-- # Class: Measure Description: Defines a concrete measure as a single number associated to a unit. It extends MeasureBase by requiring a single value attribute to be present. A measure may be unit-less so the unit attribute is still optional.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value Description: The value attribute must be present in a concrete measure.
--     * Slot: unit_id Description: Qualifies the unit by which the amount is measured. Optional because a measure may be unit-less (e.g. when representing a ratio between amounts in the same unit).
-- # Class: MeasureBase Description: Provides an abstract type to define a measure as a single number or a schedule associated to a unit. This type is abstract because all its attributes are optional. The types that extend it can specify further existence constraints.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value Description: The initial rate or amount, as the case may be. An initial rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
--     * Slot: unit_id Description: Qualifies the unit by which the amount is measured. Optional because a measure may be unit-less (e.g. when representing a ratio between amounts in the same unit).
-- # Class: MoneyBound Description: The money bound is defined as a money amount and whether the bound is inclusive.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: inclusive Description: Whether the money amount bound is inclusive, e.g. for a lower bound, false would indicate greater than, whereas true would indicate greater than or equal to.
--     * Slot: money_id Description: The money amount to be used as the bound, e.g. 1,000 USD.
-- # Class: MoneyRange Description: The money range defined as either a lower and upper money bound, or both.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: lowerBound_id Description: The lower bound of a money range, e.g. greater than or equal to 1,000 USD.
--     * Slot: upperBound_id Description: The upper bound of a money range, e.g. less than 10,000 USD.
-- # Class: NonNegativeDatedValue Description: Defines a date and value pair where the value is non-negative. This definition is used for varying rate or amount schedules, e.g. a notional amortisation or a step-up coupon schedule.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: date Description: The date on which the associated step value becomes effective. This day may be subject to adjustment in accordance with a business day convention.
--     * Slot: value Description: requires the rate of amount which becomes effective on the associated step date to be non-negative. A rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
-- # Class: NonNegativeMeasure Description: Defines a concrete non-negative measure as a number associated to a unit. It extends Measure by requiring the value attribute to be non-negative. A measure may be unit-less so the unit attribute is still optional.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value Description: The value attribute must be present in a concrete measure and non-negative.
--     * Slot: unit_id Description: Qualifies the unit by which the amount is measured. Optional because a measure may be unit-less (e.g. when representing a ratio between amounts in the same unit).
-- # Class: NonNegativeQuantity Description: Specifies a quantity as a non-negative number, which condition is enforced through a data rule that only applies to the extending class.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value Description: For a non-negative quantity, the value attribute must be positive.
--     * Slot: multiplier_id Description: Defines an optional measure that the quantity should be multiplied by to derive a total quantity. Requires that the multiplier must be positive. This number is associated to an optional unit. For example in the case of the Coal (API2) CIF ARA (ARGUS-McCloskey) Futures Contract on the CME, where the unit would be contracts, the multiplier value would 1,000 and the mulitiplier unit would be 1,000 MT (Metric Tons).
--     * Slot: frequency_id Description: Defines the frequency to be used when defining a quantity. For example a quantity may be specified as a number of barrels of oil per day, which needs multiplying by the number of days in the relevant period to get the total quantity as a number of barrels.
--     * Slot: total_id Description: Specifies the total quantity when the quantity itself is specified with a frequency.
--     * Slot: unit_id Description: Requires that a unit of amount must be specified for any quantity.
-- # Class: NonNegativeQuantitySchedule Description: Specifies a quantity schedule where all the values must be non-negative.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value Description: For a non-negative quantity schedule, all amount attribute must be positive.
--     * Slot: multiplier_id Description: Defines an optional measure that the quantity should be multiplied by to derive a total quantity. Requires that the multiplier must be positive. This number is associated to an optional unit. For example in the case of the Coal (API2) CIF ARA (ARGUS-McCloskey) Futures Contract on the CME, where the unit would be contracts, the multiplier value would 1,000 and the mulitiplier unit would be 1,000 MT (Metric Tons).
--     * Slot: frequency_id Description: Defines the frequency to be used when defining a quantity. For example a quantity may be specified as a number of barrels of oil per day, which needs multiplying by the number of days in the relevant period to get the total quantity as a number of barrels.
--     * Slot: total_id Description: For a non-negative quantity schedule, all amount attribute must be positive.
--     * Slot: unit_id Description: Requires that a unit of amount must be specified for any quantity.
-- # Class: NonNegativeSchedule Description: Specifies a schedule whose values are non-negative.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value Description: The non-negative initial rate or amount, as the case may be. An initial rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
-- # Class: NumberBound Description: The number bound is defined as a number and whether the bound is inclusive.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: number Description: The number to be used as the bound, e.g. 5.
--     * Slot: inclusive Description: Whether the number bound is inclusive, e.g. for a lower bound, false would indicate greater than, whereas true would indicate greater than or equal to.
-- # Class: NumberRange Description: The number range defined as either a lower and upper number bound, or both.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: lowerBound_id Description: The lower bound of a number range, e.g. greater than or equal to 5.
--     * Slot: upperBound_id Description: The upper bound of a number range, e.g. less than 10.
-- # Class: Quantity Description: Specifies a quantity as a single value to be associated to a financial product, for example a transfer amount resulting from a trade. This data type extends QuantitySchedule and requires that only the single value exists.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value Description: Requires the single rate or amount, as the case may be, to be present. An initial rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
--     * Slot: multiplier_id Description: Defines an optional measure that the quantity should be multiplied by to derive a total quantity. Requires that the multiplier must be positive. This number is associated to an optional unit. For example in the case of the Coal (API2) CIF ARA (ARGUS-McCloskey) Futures Contract on the CME, where the unit would be contracts, the multiplier value would 1,000 and the mulitiplier unit would be 1,000 MT (Metric Tons).
--     * Slot: frequency_id Description: Defines the frequency to be used when defining a quantity. For example a quantity may be specified as a number of barrels of oil per day, which needs multiplying by the number of days in the relevant period to get the total quantity as a number of barrels.
--     * Slot: total_id Description: Specifies the total quantity when the quantity itself is specified with a frequency.
--     * Slot: unit_id Description: Requires that a unit of amount must be specified for any quantity.
-- # Class: QuantitySchedule Description: Specifies a quantity schedule to be associated to a financial product to represent a trade amount. This data type extends MeasureBase with several unit or multiplier attributes that are used to define financial quantities. This data type is generically based on a schedule and can also be used to represent a quantity as a single value.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value Description: The initial rate or amount, as the case may be. An initial rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
--     * Slot: multiplier_id Description: Defines an optional measure that the quantity should be multiplied by to derive a total quantity. Requires that the multiplier must be positive. This number is associated to an optional unit. For example in the case of the Coal (API2) CIF ARA (ARGUS-McCloskey) Futures Contract on the CME, where the unit would be contracts, the multiplier value would 1,000 and the mulitiplier unit would be 1,000 MT (Metric Tons).
--     * Slot: frequency_id Description: Defines the frequency to be used when defining a quantity. For example a quantity may be specified as a number of barrels of oil per day, which needs multiplying by the number of days in the relevant period to get the total quantity as a number of barrels.
--     * Slot: total_id Description: Specifies the total quantity when the quantity itself is specified with a frequency.
--     * Slot: unit_id Description: Requires that a unit of amount must be specified for any quantity.
-- # Class: Rounding Description: Defines rounding rules and precision to be used in the rounding of a number.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: roundingDirection Description: Specifies the rounding rule as up, down, or nearest.
--     * Slot: precision Description: Specifies the rounding precision in terms of a number of decimal places when the number is evaluated in decimal form (not percentage), e.g. 0.09876543 rounded to the nearest 5 decimal places is 0.0987654.
-- # Class: Schedule Description: Specifies an amount or quantity, either as a single value or as a schedule of dated values. This can be used where the applicable quantity changes over time, with each dated value becoming effective from its associated step date.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value Description: The initial rate or amount, as the case may be. An initial rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
-- # Class: ScheduleWithInitialValue Description: A class defining a schedule of rates or amounts in terms of an initial value and then a series of step date and value pairs. On each step date the rate or amount changes to the new step value. The series of step date and value pairs are optional. If not specified, this implies that the initial value remains unchanged over time.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value Description: The initial rate or amount must be specified, as the case may be. An initial rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
-- # Class: UnitType Description: Defines the unit to be used for price, quantity, or other purposes
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: capacityUnit Description: Provides an enumerated value for a capacity unit, generally used in the context of defining quantities for commodities.
--     * Slot: weatherUnit Description: Provides an enumerated values for a weather unit, generally used in the context of defining quantities for commodities.
--     * Slot: financialUnit Description: Provides an enumerated value for financial units, generally used in the context of defining quantities for securities.
--     * Slot: currency Description: Defines the currency to be used as a unit for a price, quantity, or other purpose.
-- # Class: Asset Description: An Asset is defined as something that can be owned and transferred in the financial markets. As a choice data type, one and only one of the attributes must be used.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: Cash_id Description: An Asset that consists solely of a monetary holding in a currency.
--     * Slot: Commodity_id Description: An Asset comprised of raw or refined materials or agricultural products, eg gold, oil or wheat.
--     * Slot: DigitalAsset_id Description: An Asset that exists only in digital form, eg Bitcoin or Ethereum; excludes the digital representation of other Assets.
--     * Slot: Instrument_id Description: An asset that is issued by one party to one or more others; Instrument is also a choice data type.
-- # Class: AssetBase Description: The base data type to specify common attributes for all Assets.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: AssetIdentifier Description: The unique identifier for an Asset, specified using an Asset Identifier Type enumerator.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: identifier Description: The identifier value.
--     * Slot: identifierType Description: Defines the symbology source of the Asset Identifier, eg CUSIP, ISIN, etc.
-- # Class: AssetType Description: Represents a class to allow specification of the asset product type.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Represents a filter based on the type of collateral asset.
--     * Slot: securityType Description: Represents a filter based on the type of security.
--     * Slot: fundType Description: Represents a filter based on the type of fund.
--     * Slot: debtType_id Description: Represents a filter based on the type of bond.
--     * Slot: equityType_id Description: Represents a filter based on the type of equity.
-- # Class: Cash Description: An Asset that consists solely of a monetary holding in a currency. The currency of the Cash asset is held in the string Identifier (from AssetBase) and the AssetIdTypeEnum must be set to define that a CurrencyCode is set. The function SetCashCurrency can be used to create (or update) a Cash object and the function GetCashCurrency can be used to retrieve the currency of a Cash object.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: CollateralGuarantorType Description: Specifies the origin of entity guaranteeing the collateral.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: guarantorType Description: Specifies the origin of entity guaranteeing the collateral.
-- # Class: CollateralIssuerType Description: Represents a class to allow specification of the type of entity issuing the collateral.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: issuerType Description: Specifies the origin of entity issuing the collateral.
--     * Slot: supraNationalType Description: Specifies debt issued by international organisations and multilateral banks.
--     * Slot: quasiGovernmentType_id Description: Specifies debt issues by institutions or bodies, typically constituted by statute, with a function mandated by the government and subject to government supervision inclusive of profit- and non-profit making bodies. Includes the US Agencies and GSEs and the EU concept of public sector entities. Excluding any entities which are also Regional Government.
--     * Slot: regionalGovernmentType_id Description: Specifies Regional government, local authority or municipal.
--     * Slot: specialPurposeVehicleType_id Description: Specifies a subsidiary company that is formed to undertake a specific business purpose of acquisition and financing of specific assets on a potentially limited recourse basis dependent of how it is designed. E.g. asset backed securities, including securitisations.
-- # Class: CollateralTaxonomy Description: Specifies the collateral taxonomy, which is composed of a taxonomy value and a taxonomy source.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: taxonomySource Description: Specifies the taxonomy source.
--     * Slot: taxonomyValue_id Description: Specifies the taxonomy value.
-- # Class: CollateralTaxonomyValue Description: Specifies the collateral taxonomy value, either as a specified enumeration or as a string.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: Commodity Description: Identifies a specific commodity by referencing a product identifier or by a product definition.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: description Description: Provides additional information about the commodity underlier.
--     * Slot: priceQuoteType Description: Describes the required quote type of the underlying price that will be observed. Example values include 'Bid, 'Ask', 'Settlement' (for a futures contract) and 'WeightedAverage' (for some published prices and indices).
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: commodityProductDefinition_id Description: Specifies the commodity underlier in the event that no ISDA Commodity Reference Benchmark exists.
--     * Slot: deliveryDateReference_id Description: Specifies the parameters for identifying the relevant contract date when the commodity reference price is a futures contract.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: CommodityProductDefinition Description: Specifies the commodity underlier in the event that no ISDA Commodity Reference Price exists.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: commodityInfoPublisher Description: Specifies the publication where the commodity prices can be found.
--     * Slot: exchangeId Description: Identifies the exchange from which the reference price should be sourced, using the scheme at the following url: http://www.fpml.org/coding-scheme/external/exchange-id-MIC-1-0
--     * Slot: referenceFramework_id Description: Specifies the type of commodity.
--     * Slot: priceSource_id Description: Specifies a publication that provides the commodity price, including, where applicable the details of where in the publication the price is published. Applicable when the commodity reference price is not a futures contract
-- # Class: CommodityReferenceFramework Description: Specifies the type of commodity.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: commodityName Description: Identifies the commodity more specifically. Where possible, this should follow the naming convention used in the 2005 ISDA Commodity Definitions SubAnnex A, including the subCommodity and additional qualifiers, but should be limited to 256 characters or less.
--     * Slot: capacityUnit Description: Provides an enumerated value for a capacity unit, generally used in the context of defining quantities for commodities.
--     * Slot: weatherUnit Description: Provides an enumerated values for a weather unit, generally used in the context of defining quantities for commodities.
--     * Slot: currency Description: Defines the currency in which the commodity is priced.
-- # Class: DebtEconomics Description: Specifies selected economics of a debt security.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: seniority Description: Specifies the order of repayment in the event of a sale or bankruptcy of the issuer or a related party (eg guarantor).
--     * Slot: interest Description: Specifies the general rule for periodic interest rate payment.
--     * Slot: principal Description: Specifies the general rule for repayment of principal.
--     * Slot: secured_id Description: Specifies the type of secured debt.
--     * Slot: redemption_id Description: Specifies the general rule for redemption of a debt security.
-- # Class: DebtRedemption Description: Specifies the redemption features and whether the redemption right is exercised at the discretion of the issuer or the holder.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: redemptionType Description: Specifies the contractual redemption or conversion features associated with a debt security.
--     * Slot: putCall Description: Specifies the embedded option feature of a debt security.
--     * Slot: party Description: Specifies whether the debt security is redeemed at the election of the Issuer/Holder.
-- # Class: DebtType Description: Specifies the type of debt security.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: DeliveryDateParameters Description: Specifies a specific date or the parameters for identifying the relevant contract date when the commodity reference price is a futures contract.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: deliveryNearby_id Description: Provides a container for the parametric representation that specifies which nearby contract date would be used as a refrence for a price.
--     * Slot: deliveryDate_id Description: Specifies the specific contract date for the contract that should be referenced for a price.
--     * Slot: deliveryDateRollConvention_id Description: Specifies, for a Commodity Transaction that references a listed future, the day on which the specified future will roll to the next nearby month prior to the expiration of the referenced future. If the future will not roll at all - i.e. the price will be taken from the expiring contract, 0 days should be specified here. If the future will roll to the next nearby on the last trading day - i.e. the price will be taken from the next nearby on the last trading day, then 1 business day should be specified and so on.
--     * Slot: deliveryDateExpirationConvention_id Description: Specifies, for a Commodity Transaction that references a listed future, the day on which the specified future will expire ahead of the actual expiration of the referenced future. For example: Z21 Contract expires on 19Nov21, with an adjust of 2D the 'expire' will be 16Nov21. DeliveryDateRollConvention takes precedence. Example: Pricing on the Z21 Contract with NearbyContractDay and a deliveryDateRoll of 10D, Sampling of the F22 Contract will occur on 8Nov21 through the last Date of the Z21 Contract. With an ExpConvention of 5D, the last sampling date on the F22 contract will be 12Nov21.
-- # Class: DigitalAsset Description: An Asset that exists only in digital form, eg Bitcoin or Ethereum, that is not backed by other Assets; excludes the digital representation of other Assets, eg coins or Tokenised assets.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: EquityType
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: equityType
--     * Slot: depositaryReceipt
-- # Class: Instrument Description: A type of Asset that is issued by one party to one or more others.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: ListedDerivative_id Description: A securitized derivative on another asset that is created by an exchange.
--     * Slot: Loan_id Description: An Asset that represents a loan or borrow obligation.
--     * Slot: Security_id Description: An Asset that is issued by a party to be held by or transferred to others.
-- # Class: InstrumentBase Description: Defines the common attributes for all Instrument data types.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: ListedDerivative Description: A securitized derivative on another asset.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: deliveryTerm Description: Also called contract month or delivery month. However, it's not always a month. It is usually expressed using a code, e.g. Z23 would be the Dec 2023 contract, (Z = December). For crude oil, the corresponding contract might be called CLZ23. Optional as this can be uniquely identified in the identifier.
--     * Slot: optionType Description: The type of option, ie Put or Call. Left empty if it is a Future.
--     * Slot: strike Description: Specifies the strike of the option.
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: Loan Description: Identifies a loan by referencing an asset identifier and through an optional set of attributes.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: lien Description: Specifies the seniority level of the lien.
--     * Slot: facilityType Description: Specifies the type of loan facility (letter of credit, revolving, ...).
--     * Slot: creditAgreementDate Description: Specifies the credit agreement date is the closing date (the date where the agreement has been signed) for the loans in the credit agreement. Funding of the facilities occurs on (or sometimes a little after) the Credit Agreement date. This underlier attribute is used to help identify which of the company's outstanding loans are being referenced by knowing to which credit agreement it belongs. ISDA Standards Terms Supplement term: Date of Original Credit Agreement.
--     * Slot: tranche Description: Denotes the loan tranche that is subject to the derivative transaction. It will typically be referenced as the Bloomberg tranche number. ISDA Standards Terms Supplement term: Bloomberg Tranche Number.
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: PriceSource Description: Specifies a publication that provides the commodity price, including, where applicable, the details of where in the publication the price is published.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: pricePublisher Description: Defines a publication in which the price can be found. (e.g Gas Daily, Platts Bloomberg. Commodity publishers can be found at this URL: http://www.fpml.org/coding-scheme/commodity-information-provider>
--     * Slot: priceSourceLocation Description: Specifies the location of the price which may be a specific page, electornic screen name, or a code (e.g. a RIC code) where the price can be found.
--     * Slot: priceSourceHeading Description: Specifies the heading or field name for the price on a given page or screen, where applicable.
--     * Slot: priceSourceTime Description: Specifies the time at which the price should be observed.
-- # Class: ProductIdentifier Description: Comprises an identifier and a source. The associated metadata key denotes the ability to associate a hash value to the ProductIdentifier instantiations for the purpose of model cross-referencing, in support of functionality such as the event effect and the lineage.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: source Description: Defines the source of the identifier.
--     * Slot: identifier Description: Provides an identifier associated with a specific product. The identifier is unique within the public source specified in the source attribute.
-- # Class: ProductTaxonomy Description: Specifies the product taxonomy, which is composed of a taxonomy value and a taxonomy source.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: primaryAssetClass Description: Classifies the most important risk class of the trade.
--     * Slot: source Description: The source of the taxonomy that defines the rules for classifying the object. The taxonomy source is taken from a enumerated list of taxonomy names. Optional as the taxonomy source may not be provided.
--     * Slot: calculated Description: Specifies whether the taxonomy has been derived from the model features using a CDM qualification function that determines the product type based on the model features.
--     * Slot: value_id Description: The value according to that taxonomy. Optional as it may not be possible to classify the object in that taxonomy.
-- # Class: QuasiGovernmentIssuerType Description: Represents a class to allow specification of different types of Quasi Government collateral.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: sovereignEntity Description: True if sovereign entity (e.g. not separate legal personality from sovereign) or false if non-sovereign entity (e.g. separate legal personality from sovereign).
--     * Slot: sovereignRecourse Description: Applies to non-sovereign entity (e.g. separate legal personality from sovereign). True if entity has recourse to sovereign (e.g. debt guaranteed by government). False if entity does not have recourse to sovereign.
-- # Class: RegionalGovernmentIssuerType Description: Represents a class to allow specification of different type of Regional government collateral.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: sovereignRecourse Description: Applies to regional governments, local authorities or municipals. True if entity has recourse to sovereign (e.g. debt guaranteed by government). False if entity does not have recourse to sovereign.
-- # Class: SecuredDebt
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: securedType Description: Specifies the type of secured debt product.
--     * Slot: assetBacked Description: Specifies the type of Asset Backed Security.
--     * Slot: collateralizedObligation Description: Specifies the type of Collateralized Obligation.
--     * Slot: coveredBond Description: Specifies the type of Covered Bond.
--     * Slot: propertyType Description: Specifies the type of property when the security is linked to a property asset.
-- # Class: Security Description: Identifies a security by referencing an identifier and by specifying the sector.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: securityType Description: Identifies the type of security using an enumerated list.
--     * Slot: fundType Description: Identifies the type of fund.
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: debtType_id Description: Identifies the type of debt and selected debt economics.
--     * Slot: equityType_id Description: Identifies the type of equity.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: SpecialPurposeVehicleIssuerType Description: Represents a class to allow specification of different types of special purpose vehicle (SPV) collateral.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: creditRisk Description: Indicates tranched or untranched credit risk.
-- # Class: Taxonomy Description: Defines the taxonomy of an object by combining a taxonomy source (i.e. the rules to classify the object) and a value (i.e. the output of those rules on the object).
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: source Description: The source of the taxonomy that defines the rules for classifying the object. The taxonomy source is taken from a enumerated list of taxonomy names. Optional as the taxonomy source may not be provided.
--     * Slot: calculated Description: Specifies whether the taxonomy has been derived from the model features using a CDM qualification function that determines the product type based on the model features.
--     * Slot: value_id Description: The value according to that taxonomy. Optional as it may not be possible to classify the object in that taxonomy.
-- # Class: TaxonomyClassification
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: description Description: A description of the class.
--     * Slot: className Description: The name defined by the classification system for a specific attribute in the taxonomy
--     * Slot: value Description: The value set by the taxonomy that is specific to the className attribute.
--     * Slot: ordinal Description: In the case of multi-layered hierarchical classification systems such as commodity classification, the layer the value and className occupy in the classification hierarchy, where 1 represents the top-layer.
-- # Class: TaxonomyValue Description: Defines a taxonomy value as either a simple string or a more granular expression with class names and values for each class.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: name Description: Specifies the taxonomy value as a simple string, which may be associated to an external scheme.
-- # Class: NotDomesticCurrency Description: A class to specify the ISDA 2003 Term: Not Domestic Currency.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: applicable Description: Indicates whether the Not Domestic Currency provision is applicable.
--     * Slot: currency Description: An explicit specification of the domestic currency. The list of valid currencies is not presently positioned as an enumeration as part of the CDM because that scope is limited to the values specified by ISDA and FpML. As a result, implementers have to make reference to the relevant standard, such as the ISO 4217 standard for currency codes.
-- # Class: Obligations Description: A class to specify the underlying obligations of the reference entity on which protection is purchased or sold through the Credit Default Swap.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: category Description: Used in both obligations and deliverable obligations to represent a class or type of securities which apply. ISDA 2003 Term: Obligation Category/Deliverable Obligation Category.
--     * Slot: notSubordinated Description: An obligation and deliverable obligation characteristic. An obligation that ranks at least equal with the most senior Reference Obligation in priority of payment or, if no Reference Obligation is specified in the related Confirmation, the obligations of the Reference Entity that are senior. ISDA 2003 Term: Not Subordinated.
--     * Slot: notSovereignLender Description: An obligation and deliverable obligation characteristic. Any obligation that is not primarily (majority) owed to a Sovereign or Supranational Organisation. ISDA 2003 Term: Not Sovereign Lender.
--     * Slot: notDomesticLaw Description: An obligation and deliverable obligation characteristic. If the reference entity is a Sovereign, this means any obligation that is not subject to the laws of the reference entity. If the reference entity is not a sovereign, this means any obligation that is not subject to the laws of the jurisdiction of the reference entity. ISDA 2003 Term: Not Domestic Law.
--     * Slot: listed Description: An obligation and deliverable obligation characteristic. Indicates whether or not the obligation is quoted, listed or ordinarily purchased and sold on an exchange. ISDA 2003 Term: Listed.
--     * Slot: notDomesticIssuance Description: An obligation and deliverable obligation characteristic. Any obligation other than an obligation that was intended to be offered for sale primarily in the domestic market of the relevant Reference Entity. This specifies that the obligation must be an internationally recognised bond. ISDA 2003 Term: Not Domestic Issuance.
--     * Slot: fullFaithAndCreditObLiability Description: An obligation and deliverable obligation characteristic. Defined in the ISDA published additional provisions for U.S. Municipal as Reference Entity. ISDA 2003 Term: Full Faith and Credit Obligation Liability.
--     * Slot: generalFundObligationLiability Description: An obligation and deliverable obligation characteristic. Defined in the ISDA published additional provisions for U.S. Municipal as Reference Entity. ISDA 2003 Term: General Fund Obligation Liability.
--     * Slot: revenueObligationLiability Description: An obligation and deliverable obligation characteristic. Defined in the ISDA published additional provisions for U.S. Municipal as Reference Entity. ISDA 2003 Term: Revenue Obligation Liability.
--     * Slot: notContingent Description: OTE: Only allowed as an obligation characteristic under ISDA Credit 1999. In essence Not Contingent means the repayment of principal cannot be dependent on a formula/index, i.e. to prevent the risk of being delivered an instrument that may never pay any element of principal, and to ensure that the obligation is interest bearing (on a regular schedule). ISDA 2003 Term: Not Contingent.
--     * Slot: excluded Description: A free format string to specify any excluded obligations or deliverable obligations, as the case may be, of the reference entity or excluded types of obligations or deliverable obligations. ISDA 2003 Term: Excluded Obligations/Excluded Deliverable Obligations.
--     * Slot: othReferenceEntityObligations Description: This element is used to specify any other obligations of a reference entity in both obligations and deliverable obligations. The obligations can be specified free-form. ISDA 2003 Term: Other Obligations of a Reference Entity.
--     * Slot: designatedPriority Description: Applies to Loan CDS, to indicate what lien level is appropriate for a deliverable obligation. Applies to European Loan CDS, to indicate the Ranking of the obligation. Example: a 2nd lien Loan CDS would imply that the deliverable obligations are 1st or 2nd lien loans.
--     * Slot: cashSettlementOnly Description: An obligation and deliverable obligation characteristic. Defined in the ISDA published Standard Terms Supplement for use with CDS Transactions on Leveraged Loans. ISDA 2003 Term: Cash Settlement Only.
--     * Slot: deliveryOfCommitments Description: An obligation and deliverable obligation characteristic. Defined in the ISDA published Standard Terms Supplement for use with CDS Transactions on Leveraged Loans. ISDA 2003 Term: Delivery of Commitments.
--     * Slot: continuity Description: An obligation and deliverable obligation characteristic. Defined in the ISDA published Standard Terms Supplement for use with CDS Transactions on Leveraged Loans. ISDA 2003 Term: Continuity.
--     * Slot: specifiedCurrency_id Description: An obligation and deliverable obligation characteristic. The currency or currencies in which an obligation or deliverable obligation must be payable. ISDA 2003 Term: Specified Currency.
--     * Slot: notDomesticCurrency_id Description: An obligation and deliverable obligation characteristic. Any obligation that is payable in any currency other than the domestic currency. Domestic currency is either the currency so specified or, if no currency is specified, the currency of (a) the reference entity, if the reference entity is a sovereign, or (b) the jurisdiction in which the relevant reference entity is organised, if the reference entity is not a sovereign. ISDA 2003 Term: Not Domestic Currency.
-- # Class: SpecifiedCurrency
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: applicable Description: Indicates whether the specified currency provision is applicable.
--     * Slot: currency Description: The currency in which the specified currency is denominated. The list of valid currencies is not presently positioned as an enumeration as part of the CDM because that scope is limited to the values specified by ISDA and FpML. As a result, implementers have to make reference to the relevant standard, such as the ISO 4217 standard for currency codes.
-- # Class: CodeList Description: A type hold a list of codes for business data validation
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: identification_id Description: Identification information about the code list
-- # Class: CodeListIdentification Description: A type to identify the version of a codelist
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: description Description: A description of the code list, e.g. A list of codes identifying business centers
--     * Slot: version Description: The the most recent version of the codelist, eg. 9-1
--     * Slot: publicationDate Description: The most recent date the code list was published, e.g. 2021-10-05
--     * Slot: shortName Description: A short name (without whitespace) for the code list, e.g. businessCenterScheme
--     * Slot: codeShortId Description: The name of the code list, e.g. business-center
--     * Slot: canonicalUri Description: Canonical URI which uniquely identifies all versions (collectively) of the referenced code list. Must be an absolute URI. Must not be used as a de facto location URI.
--     * Slot: canonicalVersionUri Description: Canonical URI which uniquely identifies a specific version of the referenced code list. Must be an absolute URI. Must not be used as a de facto location URI.
--     * Slot: locationUri Description: Suggested retrieval location for this version, in genericode format. An application must signal an error to the user if a document retrieved using a LocationUri is not in genericode format.
-- # Class: CodeValue Description: A type to hold the value of the code in a codelist
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: description Description: A description of the meaning of the code, e.g. New York City, USA
--     * Slot: source Description: Where the code was defined,e.g. ISDA, FpML, Bloomberg
--     * Slot: value Description: The value of the code, e.g. USNY
--     * Slot: effectiveDate Description: When the code became/becomes effective
--     * Slot: deprecatedDate Description: When the code ceased to be valid for new uses
-- # Class: AssignedIdentifier Description: A class to specify the identifier value and its associated version.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: version Description: The identifier version, which is specified as an integer and is meant to be incremented each time the transaction terms (whether contract or event) change. This version is made option to support the use case where the identifier is referenced without the version. The constraint that a contract and a lifecycle event need to have an associated version is enforced through data rules.
--     * Slot: identifier Description: The identifier value.
-- # Class: IdentifiedList Description: Attaches an identifier to a collection of objects, when those objects themselves can each be represented by an identifier. One use case is the representation of package transactions, where each component is a separate trade with its own identifier, and those trades are linked together as a package with its own identifier. The data type has been named generically rather than referring to 'packages' as it may have a number of other uses.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: listId_id Description: The identifier for the list. In the case of a package transaction, this would be the package identifier. This attribute is mandatory to allow the list itself to be identified.
--     * Slot: price_id Description: The price of the package.
-- # Class: Identifier Description: A class to specify a generic identifier, applicable to CDM artefacts such as executions, contracts, lifecycle events and legal documents. An issuer can be associated with the actual identifier value as a way to properly qualify it.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: issuer Description: The identifier issuer, when specified explicitly alongside the identifier value (instead of being specified by reference to a party).
--     * Slot: issuerReference_id Description: The identifier issuer, when specified by reference to a party specified as part of the transaction.
-- # Class: LocationIdentifier Description: Specifies a location identifier. An issuer and an identifier type can be associated with the actual identifier value as a way to properly qualify it.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: locationIdentifierType Description: Specifies the nature of a location identifier.
--     * Slot: issuer Description: The identifier issuer, when specified explicitly alongside the identifier value (instead of being specified by reference to a party).
--     * Slot: issuerReference_id Description: The identifier issuer, when specified by reference to a party specified as part of the transaction.
-- # Class: Account Description: A class to specify an account as an account number alongside, optionally. an account name, an account type, an account beneficiary and a servicing party.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: accountNumber Description: The account number.
--     * Slot: accountName Description: The name by which the account is known.
--     * Slot: accountType Description: The type of account, e.g. client, house.
--     * Slot: partyReference_id Description: A reference to the party to which the account refers to.
--     * Slot: accountBeneficiary_id Description: A reference to the party beneficiary of the account.
--     * Slot: servicingParty_id Description: The reference to the legal entity that services the account, i.e. in the books of which the account is held.
-- # Class: Address Description: A class to specify a post or street address.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: city Description: The city component of the postal address.
--     * Slot: state Description: A country subdivision used in postal addresses in some countries. For example, US states, Canadian provinces, Swiss cantons, ...
--     * Slot: country Description: The ISO 3166 standard code for the country within which the postal address is located.
--     * Slot: postalCode Description: The code, required for computerized mail sorting systems, that is allocated to a physical address by a national postal authority.
-- # Class: AncillaryEntity Description: Holds an identifier for an ancillary entity, either identified directly via its ancillary role or directly as a legal entity.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: ancillaryParty Description: Identifies a party via its ancillary role on a transaction (e.g. CCP or DCO through which the trade should be cleared.)
--     * Slot: legalEntity_id
-- # Class: AncillaryParty Description: Defines an ancillary role enumerated value with an associated party reference. The product is agnostic to the actual parties involved in the transaction, with the party references abstracted away from the product definition and replaced by the AncillaryRoleEnum. The AncillaryRoleEnum can then be positioned in the product and this AncillaryParty type, which is positioned outside of the product definition, allows the AncillaryRoleEnum to be associated with an actual party reference.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: role Description: Specifies the AncillaryRoleEnum that is associated to the party reference. An ancillary party is any involved party that is not one of the two principal parties to the transaction.
--     * Slot: onBehalfOf Description: Optionally specifies the counterparty that the ancillary party is acting on behalf of.
-- # Class: AssetAncillaryPartyRole
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: role Description: The party role.
--     * Slot: partyReference_id Description: A reference to the party to which the role refers to.
-- # Class: AssetPartyRole
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: role Description: The party role.
--     * Slot: partyReference_id Description: A reference to the party to which the role refers to.
-- # Class: BusinessUnit Description: A class to specify an organizational unit.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: name Description: A name used to describe the organizational unit
--     * Slot: identifier_id Description: An identifier used to uniquely identify the organizational unit
--     * Slot: contactInformation_id Description: The contact information for such business unit, when different from the contact information associated with the party.
-- # Class: BuyerSeller Description: This class corresponds to the FpML BuyerSeller.model construct.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: buyer Description: Buyer party that can be resolved as one of the two principal parties to the transaction. The party that buys this instrument, i.e. pays for this instrument and receives the rights defined by it. ISDA 2002 Equity Definitions section 1.18: `Buyer` means the party specified as such in the related Confirmation. | ISDA 2006 Definitions article 12.1 (b)(i) relating to a Swaption: 'Buyer' means the party that will, on each Premium Payment Date, pay to Seller the Premium | ISDA 2006 Definitions article 12.1 (b)(ii) relating to Swap Transactions with applicable Early Termination: the party specified as such in the related Confirmation, or the Exercising Party if neither party is specified | ISDA 2006 Definitions article 12.1 (b)(iii) relating to any other Option Transaction: the party specified as such in the related Confirmation. | ISDA 2014 Credit Definition article 1.4: `Buyer` means the Fixed Rate Payer.
--     * Slot: seller Description: Seller party that can be resolved as one of the two principal parties to the transaction. The party that sells ('writes') this instrument, i.e. that grants the rights defined by this instrument and in return receives a payment for it. ISDA 2002 Equity Definitions section 1.19: `Seller` means the party specified as such in the related Confirmation. | ISDA 2006 Definitions article 12.1 (a)(i) relating to a Swaption: 'Seller' means the party the party specified as such or as writer in the related Confirmation | ISDA 2006 Definitions article 12.1 (a)(ii) relating to Swap Transactions with applicable Early Termination: the party specified as such or as writer in the related Confirmation or, if neither party is specified as such, the Non-exercising Party | ISDA 2006 Definitions article 12.1 (a)(iii) relating to any other Option Transaction: the party specified as such in the related Confirmation. | ISDA 2014 Credit Definition article 1.4: `Seller` means the Floating Rate Payer.
-- # Class: ContactInformation Description: A class to specify contact information associated with a party: telephone, postal/street address, email and web page.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: Counterparty Description: Defines a counterparty enumerated value, e.g. Party1 or Party2, with an associated party reference. The product is agnostic to the actual parties to the transaction, with the party references abstracted away from the product definition and replaced by the CounterpartyEnum (e.g. values Party1 or Party2). The CounterpartyEnum can then be positioned in the product (e.g. to specify which counterparty is the payer, receiver etc) and this Counterparty type, which is positioned outside of the product definition, allows the CounterpartyEnum to be associated with an actual party reference.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: role Description: Specifies the CounterpartyEnum, e.g. either Party1 or Party2, that is associated to the partyReference.
--     * Slot: partyReference_id Description: Specifies the party that is associated to the counterparty.
-- # Class: EntityIdentifier Description: Comprises an identifier and a source. The associated metadata key denotes the ability to associate a hash value to the EntityIdentifier instantiations for the purpose of model cross-referencing, in support of functionality such as the event effect and the lineage.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: identifier Description: Provides an identifier associated with a legal entity.
--     * Slot: identifierType Description: Defines the source of the identifier.
-- # Class: LegalEntity Description: A class to specify a legal entity, with a required name and an optional entity identifier (such as the LEI).
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: name Description: The legal entity name.
-- # Class: NaturalPerson Description: A class to represent the attributes that are specific to a natural person.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: honorific Description: An honorific title, such as Mr., Ms., Dr. etc.
--     * Slot: firstName Description: The natural person's first name. It is optional in FpML.
--     * Slot: surname Description: The natural person's surname.
--     * Slot: suffix Description: Name suffix, such as Jr., III, etc.
--     * Slot: dateOfBirth Description: The natural person's date of birth.
--     * Slot: contactInformation_id Description: The contact information for such person, when different from the contact information associated with the party.
-- # Class: NaturalPersonRole Description: A class to specify the role(s) that natural person(s) may have in relation to the contract.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: personReference_id Description: A reference to the natural person to whom the role refers to.
-- # Class: Party Description: A class to specify a party, without a qualification as to whether this party is a legal entity or a natural person, although the model provides the ability to associate a person (or set of persons) to a party, which use case would imply that such party would be a legal entity (even if not formally specified as such).
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: name Description: The party name.
--     * Slot: account_id Description: The account that might be associated with the party. At most one account can be specified, as it is expected that this information is used in the context of a contract or legal document where only one account per party can be associated with such object.
--     * Slot: contactInformation_id Description: The postal/street address, telephone number, email address and/or web page. If the contact information is specific to the associated business unit(s) or person (s), it should be associated with those.
-- # Class: PartyIdentifier Description: Comprises an identifier and a source. The associated metadata key denotes the ability to associate a hash value to the PartyIdentifier instantiations for the purpose of model cross-referencing, in support of functionality such as the event effect and the lineage.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: identifier Description: Provides an identifier associated with a party. The identifier is unique within the public source specified in the source attribute.
--     * Slot: identifierType Description: Defines the source of the identifier.
-- # Class: PartyReferencePayerReceiver Description: Specifies the parties responsible for making and receiving payments defined by this structure.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: payerPartyReference_id Description: The party responsible for making the payments defined by this structure.
--     * Slot: payerAccountReference_id Description: A reference to the account responsible for making the payments defined by this structure.
--     * Slot: receiverPartyReference_id Description: The party that receives the payments corresponding to this structure.
--     * Slot: receiverAccountReference_id Description: A reference to the account that receives the payments corresponding to this structure.
-- # Class: PartyRole Description: A class to specify the role(s) that party(ies) may have in relation to the execution, contract or other legal agreement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: role Description: The party role.
--     * Slot: partyReference_id Description: A reference to the party to which the role refers to.
--     * Slot: ownershipPartyReference_id Description: A reference to the party that has ownership of this party role information. FpML specifies that For shared trade information, this attribute will reference the originator of the data (for example, an execution facility or clearing house).
-- # Class: PayerReceiver Description: Specifies the parties responsible for making and receiving payments defined by this structure.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: payer Description: Specifies the counterparty responsible for making the payments defined by this structure. The party is one of the two principal parties to the transaction.
--     * Slot: receiver Description: Specifies the party that receives the payments corresponding to this structure. The party is one of the two counterparties to the transaction.
-- # Class: PersonIdentifier Description: Comprises an identifier and a source. The associated metadata key denotes the ability to associate a hash value to the PersonIdentifier instantiations for the purpose of model cross-referencing, in support of functionality such as the event effect and the lineage.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: identifier Description: Provides an identifier associated with a person. The identifier is unique within the public source specified in the source attribute.
--     * Slot: identifierType Description: Defines the source of the identifier.
--     * Slot: country Description: The ISO 3166 standard code for the country issuing the identifier.
-- # Class: ReferenceBank Description: A class to describe an institution (party) identified by means of a coding scheme and an optional name.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: referenceBankId Description: An institution (party) identifier, e.g. a bank identifier code (BIC). FpML specifies a referenceBankIdScheme.
--     * Slot: referenceBankName Description: The name of the institution (party). A free format string. FpML does not define usage rules for the element.
-- # Class: ReferenceBanks Description: A class defining the list of reference institutions polled for relevant rates or prices when determining the cash settlement amount for a product where cash settlement is applicable.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: RelatedParty
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: role Description: The category of the relationship. The related party performs the role specified in this field for the base party. For example, if the role is ,Guarantor, the related party acts as a guarantor for the base party.
--     * Slot: partyReference_id Description: Reference to a party.
--     * Slot: accountReference_id Description: Reference to an account.
-- # Class: TelephoneNumber Description: A class to specify a telephone number as a type of phone number (e.g. work, personal, ...) alongside with the actual number.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: telephoneNumberType Description: The type of telephone number, e.g. work, mobile.
--     * Slot: number Description: The actual telephone number.
-- # Class: AccrualFactor Description: The accrual rate and related terms, to adjust the price of an underlier impacted by a Corporate Action when economic impact consists in freezing the underlier price to the last fixing then applying accruals per each remaining underlier price fixing date required i.e. for each fixing date, adjustedPrice = lastFixingPrice x accrualFactor, where: accrualFactor = (1 + accrualRateValue x DCF).
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value_id Description: The rate to be applied to the last fixing price, for price accrual calculation purposes. DatedValue may be used for the purpose of representing Price series if such calculation is required for multiple dates.
--     * Slot: calculationTerms_id Description: Describes the input terms involved in the calculation of the accrual factor.
-- # Class: AccrualFactorCalculationTerms Description: Describes the input terms involved in the calculation of the accrual factor. Optionnally, long and short stub interpolation rates can be specified.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: tenorTillMaturity Description: The duration between last fixing date and the payment date of accruals, calculated in accordance with the appropriate DayCountFraction.
--     * Slot: dayCountFraction Description: The enumerated values to specify the day count fraction.
--     * Slot: interpolationTerms_id Description: Describes the rate, tenor, period duration for the short and long stubs, when the accrualRate optionnaly results from an interpolation method.
-- # Class: AdjustmentFactor Description: Describes the terms involved for adjusting the price of the underlier impacted by a Corporate Action.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value Description: The multiplier value applied to the price of the underlier impacted by a Corporate Action.
--     * Slot: calculationTerms_id Description: Describes the input terms involved in the calculation of the adjustment factor applied to the price of the underlier impacted by a Corporate Action.
-- # Class: AdjustmentFactorCalculationTerms Description: Describes the input terms involved in the calculation of the adjustment factor applied to the price of the underlier impacted by a Corporate Action.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: shareForShareRatio Description: Multiple value, say 'M/N' where 'M' is the number of shares after the event and 'N' is the number of shares prior to the event.
--     * Slot: shareForRightsRatio Description: Multiple value, say 'M/N' where 'M' is the number of rights after the event, and 'N' of shares prior to the event.
--     * Slot: dividendRatio Description: Multiplier value (e.g. 85 %, etc.) to calculate net dividend amount, given gross amount before taking into account the relevant fiscal features.
--     * Slot: bespokeCalculationFormula Description: To describe the formula used to calculate the Adjustment Factor.
--     * Slot: rightsSubscriptionPrice_id Description: The price to pay per each right.
--     * Slot: spinOff_id Description: Defines the underlier for both the Parent Company and the Child Compagny involved in Spin Off corporate action, as well as the respective price observation for each.
--     * Slot: merger_id Description: Defines the underlier for both the Purchaser Company and the Acquired Compagny involved in Spin Off corporate action, as well as the respective price observation for each.
--     * Slot: accrualFactor_id Description: The accrual rate and related terms, to adjust the price of an underlier impacted by a Corporate Action when economic impact consists in freezing the underlier price to last fixing and applying accruals for each remaining underlier price fixing date required i.e. for each, adjustedPrice = lastFixingPrice x (1 + accrualRate x DCF).
--     * Slot: lastFixingPriceBeforeAdjustment_id Description: The last fixing price of the Underlier affected by the CorporateAction, before any adjustment with regards to the CorporateAction.
--     * Slot: dividendObservation_id Description: To record observations of dividends.
-- # Class: AgreementEvent Description: An agreement event represents a life cycle event of a legal document. The combination of legal term amendments, contracting party changes or agreement status changes that are represented by an amendment agreement that includes a change to the overall Legal agreement representation through a change in contractual parties or terms.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: eventQualifier Description: The CDM event qualifier, which corresponds to the outcome of the isEvent qualification logic which qualifies the lifecycle event as a function of its features (e.g. PartialTermination, ClearingSubmission, Novation, ...).
--     * Slot: eventDate Description: Specifies the date of the agreement event.
--     * Slot: effectiveDate Description: Specifies the effective date of the agreement event.
-- # Class: AgreementEventInstruction Description: Specifies the date of the event and the effective date of the event.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: eventDate Description: Specifies the date of the agreement event.
--     * Slot: effectiveDate Description: Specifies the effective date of the agreement event.
-- # Class: AgreementInstruction Description: Instruction to a function that will be used to perform an agreement event
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: before_id Description: Specifies the Legal Agreement that will be acted upon by the primitive event function.
-- # Class: AgreementPrimitiveInstruction Description: Instruction to a function that will be used to capture terms or Party changes to an agreement triggered by an amendment.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: termsChange_id Description: A printive instruction set that details all associated terms changes that are defined within the instruction
--     * Slot: partyChange_id Description: A primitive Instruction set to capture any Party changes applicable to the agreement.
-- # Class: AgreementTermsChangeInstruction Description: A primitive instruction set that details all associated terms changes that are defined within the instruction.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: vmCSATermsChange_id Description: Specifies instructions describing a terms change to a Variation Margin agreement as represented by a set of agreement instructions.
--     * Slot: imCSATermsChange_id Description: Specifies instructions describing a terms change to a Initial Margin agreement as represented by a set of agreement instructions.
--     * Slot: legacyCSATermsChange_id Description: Specifies instructions describing a terms change to a Legacy CSA agreement as represented by a set of agreement instructions.
-- # Class: BillingInstruction Description: Specifies the instructions for creation of a Security Lending billing invoice.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: billingStartDate Description: The starting date of the period described by this invoice
--     * Slot: billingEndDate Description: The ending date of the period described by this invoice
--     * Slot: sendingParty_id Description: The party issuing the invoice
--     * Slot: receivingParty_id Description: The party receiving the invoice
-- # Class: BillingRecord Description: Specifies individual records within a billing invoice.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: recordStartDate Description: The starting date of the period described by this record
--     * Slot: recordEndDate Description: The ending date of the period described by this record
--     * Slot: tradeState_id Description: The trade for the individual billing record.
--     * Slot: recordTransfer_id Description: The settlement terms for the billing record
--     * Slot: minimumFee_id Description: Indicates the minimum fee amount applied to the billing record, if any.
-- # Class: BillingRecordInstruction Description: Specifies the instructions for creation of a billing record.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: recordStartDate Description: The starting date of the period described by this record
--     * Slot: recordEndDate Description: The ending date of the period described by this record
--     * Slot: settlementDate Description: The date for settlement of the transfer.
--     * Slot: tradeState_id Description: The trade for the individual billing record.
-- # Class: BillingSummary Description: Specifies individual summaries within a billing invoice.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: summaryAmountType Description: The account level for the billing summary.
--     * Slot: summaryTransfer_id Description: The settlement terms for the billing summary
-- # Class: BillingSummaryInstruction Description: Specifies the instructions for creation of a billing summary.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: summaryAmountType Description: The account level for the billing summary.
-- # Class: BusinessEvent Description: A business event represents a life cycle event of a trade. The combination of the state changes results in a qualifiable life cycle event. An example of a Business Event is a PartialTermination which is a defined by a quantity change primitive event.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: eventQualifier Description: The CDM event qualifier, which corresponds to the outcome of the isEvent qualification logic which qualifies the lifecycle event as a function of its features (e.g. PartialTermination, ClearingSubmission, Novation, ...).
--     * Slot: intent Description: The intent attribute is meant to be specified when the event qualification cannot be programmatically inferred from the event features. As a result it is only associated with those primitives that can give way to such ambiguity, the quantityChange being one of those. An example of such is a reduction in the trade notional, which could be interpreted as either a trade correction (unless a maximum period of time post-event is specified as part of the qualification), a partial termination or a portfolio rebalancing in the case of an equity swap. On the other hand, an event such as the exercise is not expected to have an associated intent as there should not be ambiguity.
--     * Slot: corporateActionIntent
--     * Slot: eventDate Description: Specifies the date on which the event is taking place. This date is equal to the trade date in the case of a simple execution. However it can be different from the trade date, for example in the case of a partial termination.
--     * Slot: effectiveDate Description: The date on which the event contractually takes effect, when different from the event date.
--     * Slot: eventTime_id Description: The time and zone of the date in which the event is taking place.
--     * Slot: effectiveTime_id Description: The time and zone of the date in which the event contractually takes effect.
--     * Slot: packageInformation_id Description: Specifies the package information in case the business event represents several trades executed as a package (hence this attribute is optional). The package information is only instantiated once at the business event level to preserve referential integrity, whereas individual trades make reference to it to identify that they are part of a package.
-- # Class: CalculateResetInstruction Description: Defines the information needed to create a Reset Instruction for the Reset Business Event.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: rateRecordDate Description: Specifies the 'Rate Record Day' for a Fallback rate. Fallback rate fixing processes typically set the fixing rate in arrears, i.e., the Fallback Rate corresponding to a Rate Record Date is set at the end of the interest accural period. When this applies, Reset->resetDate occurs at the end of the interest period, and the Reset->rateRecordDate occurs near the start of the interest period. The Reset->rateRecordDate and Reset->observations->observationIdentifier->observationDate will differ if a Fallback rate is unavailable on the Rate Record Date, and the latest previous available rate is used as the observation.
--     * Slot: resetDate Description: Specifies the date on which the reset is occuring.
-- # Class: CalculateTransferInstruction Description: Defines the tradeState or payout on which to create a Transfer along with all necessary resets.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: date
--     * Slot: tradeState_id
--     * Slot: payout_id
--     * Slot: payerReceiver_id
--     * Slot: quantity_id Description: Specifies quantity amount returned if not the full amount from the TradeState, e.g. partial return
-- # Class: ClearingInstruction Description: All information required to perform the clear life cycle event; the clearing party (CCP), the two parties facing each other on the alpha contract, and optionally the parties acting as clearing members.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isOpenOffer Description: Open Offer
--     * Slot: alphaContract_id Description: The contract that will be submitted to the clearing house for clearing. The contract should indicate that it should be cleared by assigning a clearing organisation as a party role.
--     * Slot: clearingParty_id Description: The Central Counter party (CCP) that the contract will be submitted to for clearing.
--     * Slot: party1_id Description: First party facing the CCP if it is clearing for its own account.
--     * Slot: party2_id Description: Second party facing the CCP if it is clearing for its own account.
--     * Slot: clearerParty1_id Description: Optional party facing the CCP, acting as clearing member for party1.
--     * Slot: clearerParty2_id Description: Optional party facing the CCP, acting as clearing member for party2.
-- # Class: ClosedState Description: A class to qualify the closed state of an execution or a contract through the combination or a state (e.g. terminated, novated) and a set of dates: activity date, effective date and, when relevant, last payment date.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: state Description: The qualification of what gave way to the contract or execution closure, e.g. allocation, termination, ...
--     * Slot: activityDate Description: The activity date on which the closing state took place, i.e. either the event date of the closing event (e.g. option exercise, contract early termination) or the contractual termination date.
--     * Slot: effectiveDate Description: The date on which the closing event contractually takes effect, when different from the activity date. When an explicit event effective date attribute is associated with the closing event, it will be that date. In the case of a cancellation event, it will be the date on which the cancelled event took place.
--     * Slot: lastPaymentDate Description: The date associated with the last payment in relation to the artefact (e.g. contract) to which this closed state applies. As an example, in the case of an early termination event, it would be the settlement date of the associated fee, if applicable.
-- # Class: CollateralBalance Description: Represents common attributes to define a collateral balance recorded by the principal as held or posted.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: collateralBalanceStatus Description: Defines the collateral balance breakdown of settlement status.
--     * Slot: haircutIndicator Description: Indicates if the collateral balance amount is based on pre or post haircut, if a haircut is associated with the collateral asset
--     * Slot: amountBaseCurrency_id Description: Specifies the collateral balance amount in base currency determined within a collateral legal agreement, or defined for reporting purposes.
--     * Slot: payerReceiver_id Description: Specifies each of the parties in the collateral balance and its perspective with regards to the direction of the collateral balance, posted or received.
-- # Class: CollateralPortfolio Description: Represents common attributes to define the details of collateral assets, to be used in margin call messaging and contribute to collateral balances e.g securities in a collateral account.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: portfolioIdentifier_id Description: Specifies a unique identifier for a set of collateral positions in a portfolio.
--     * Slot: legalAgreement_id Description: The specification of a legal agreement between two parties governing the collateral relationship such as Credit Support Agreement or Collateral Transfer Agreement etc. (NB: this can be provided by reference to a global key for each LegalAgreement object).
-- # Class: CollateralPosition Description: Specifies the individual components of collateral positions.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: collateralPositionStatus Description: Indicates the collateral positions settlement status.
--     * Slot: treatment_id Description: Specifies if there is any treatment to be applied to collateral, such as percentage discount which will impact collateral value.
--     * Slot: product_id Description: The product underlying the position.
--     * Slot: asset_id Description: The asset that underlies the position.
--     * Slot: cashBalance_id Description: The aggregate cost of proceeds.
--     * Slot: tradeReference_id Description: Reference to the Contract, in case product is contractual and the contract has been formed.
-- # Class: ContingentTransfer Description: Specifies a transfer created from a trade contingent upon a specific, uncertain event on a contract. Extends PayoutTransferBase because a Contingent Transfer originates from a Payout.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: transferType Description: Specifies the type of Contingent Transfer.
--     * Slot: corporateActionTransferType Description: A transfer corresponding to a corporate action event
--     * Slot: payerReceiver_id Description: Specifies who pays/receives the transfer, through a normalised Party1 / Party2 enumerator, for use before the transfer is resolved to actual parties.
--     * Slot: payoutReference_id Description: Represents the origin to the transfer as a reference for lineage purposes, whether it originated from trade level settlement terms or from payment terms on an economic payout.
--     * Slot: quantity_id Description: Represents the amount of the asset to be transferred. The cashflow amount is always a positive number, as the cashflow direction is implied by the payer/receiver attribute.
--     * Slot: asset_id Description: Represents the object that is subject to the transfer, it could be an asset or a reference.
--     * Slot: settlementDate_id Description: Represents the date on which the transfer to due.
--     * Slot: paymentDiscounting_id Description: FpML specifies the FpML PaymentDiscounting.model group for representing the discounting elements that can be associated with a payment.
--     * Slot: partyReferencePayerReceiver_id Description: Represents the resolved parties to the transfer and their role.
-- # Class: ContractDetails Description: Defines specific attributes that relate to contractual details of trades.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: governingLaw Description: Represents the law governing the trade and associated contractual product terms.
-- # Class: ContractFormationInstruction Description: Specifies instructions to create a fully formed contract, with optional legal agreements.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: CorporateAction Description: Specifies the relevant data regarding a corporate action
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: corporateActionType Description: The type of corporate action taking place.
--     * Slot: exDate Description: The date on which the corporate action is known to have taken place.
--     * Slot: payDate Description: The date on which resulting from the corporate action are delivered.
--     * Slot: recordDate Description: The date on which the account phyical balance and related underlier ownership is recorded by the custodian.
--     * Slot: announcementDate Description: The date on which the corporate action is announced by the issuer.
--     * Slot: bespokeEventDescription Description: Corporate action triggered by the occurrence of an event which description is seperatly agreed between the parties and/or described in any referenced agreement (for instance bespoke term described in any string type objects present in most root attributes of Agreement type).
--     * Slot: underlier_id Description: The underlier impacted by the corporate action.
--     * Slot: adjustmentFactor_id Description: Specifies any additional details e.g. further descriptions depending on the particular type of Corporate Action, adjustmentFactor, calculations
--     * Slot: informationSource_id Description: A class defining the source of data used in an Observation for any purposes. The data is either sourced from a Provider, or from a Party.
--     * Slot: dividendObservation_id Description: To record observations of dividends.
-- # Class: CounterpartyPositionBusinessEvent Description: A business event represents a life cycle event of a position. The combination of the state changes results in a qualifiable life cycle event.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: intent Description: The intent attribute is meant to be specified when the event qualification cannot be programmatically inferred from the event features. As a result it is only associated with those primitives that can give way to such ambiguity, the quantityChange being one of those.
--     * Slot: corporateActionIntent Description: The intent of a corporate action on the position.
--     * Slot: eventDate Description: Specifies the date on which the event is taking place. This date is equal to the trade date in the case of a simple execution. However it can be different from the trade date, for example in the case of a partial termination.
--     * Slot: effectiveDate Description: The date on which the event contractually takes effect, when different from the event date.
--     * Slot: packageInformation_id Description: Specifies the package information in case the business event represents several trades executed as a package (hence this attribute is optional). The package information is only instantiated once at the business event level to preserve referential integrity, whereas individual trades make reference to it to identify that they are part of a package.
-- # Class: CounterpartyPositionState Description: Defines the fundamental financial information that can be changed by a Primitive Event and by extension any business or life-cycle event. Each PositionState specifies where a Position is in its life-cycle. PositionState is a root type and as such, can be created independently to any other CDM data type, but can also be used as part of the CDM Event Model.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: counterpartyPosition_id Description: Represents the Position that has been effected by a business or life-cycle event.
--     * Slot: state_id Description: Represents the State of the Position through its life-cycle.
-- # Class: CreditEvent Description: Specifies the relevant data regarding a credit event.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: creditEventType Description: The type of credit event taking place.
--     * Slot: eventDeterminationDate Description: The date in which the credit event is determined by the Credit Derivatives Determinations Comitee.
--     * Slot: auctionDate Description: The date on which the auction is scheduled to occur.
--     * Slot: recoveryPercent Description: The percentage of the original value of the asset affected by the credit event that can be recovered.
--     * Slot: finalPrice_id Description: The final price resulting from the auction.
--     * Slot: referenceInformation_id Description: The reference entity, part of a credit basket, impacted by the credit event.
-- # Class: ExecutionDetails Description: Defines specific attributes that relate to trade executions.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: executionType Description: Identifies the type of execution, e.g. via voice, electronically...
--     * Slot: executionVenue_id Description: Represents the venue on which a trade was executed.
--     * Slot: packageReference_id Description: A reference to the package linking the trade with other trades, in case the trade was executed as part of a package (hence this attribute is optional).
-- # Class: ExecutionInstruction Description: Specifies instructions for execution of a transaction, consisting of a product, price, quantity, parties, trade identifier, execution details, and settlement terms.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: tradeDate Description: Denotes the trade/execution date.
--     * Slot: product_id Description: Defines the financial product to be executed and contract formed.
--     * Slot: executionDetails_id Description: Specifies the type and venue of execution, e.g. via voice, or electronically.
--     * Slot: tradeTime_id Description: Denotes the trade time and timezone as agreed by the parties to the trade.
--     * Slot: collateral_id Description: Detail the collateral requirement anticipated with the transaction.
--     * Slot: lotIdentifier_id Description: Lot Identifier associated with the transaction.
-- # Class: ExerciseInstruction Description: Specifies the information required to communicate the choices made by the exercising party, in a financial product endowing the party with at least one option.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: exerciseQuantity_id Description: Contains instructions for exercising the option including a quantity change, and optionally a transfer.
--     * Slot: exerciseOption_id Description: The Payout being exercised on the trade.
--     * Slot: exerciseDate_id Description: Specifies the date on which an option contained within the financial product would be exercised. The date may be omitted if the contractual product allows for only a single date of exercise (European exercise).
--     * Slot: exerciseTime_id Description: Specifies the time at which an option contained within the financial product woulld be exercised. The time may be omitted if the contractual product allows for only a single time of exercise (European exercise).
-- # Class: Exposure Description: Represents the current mark to market value or IM calculation value of the trade portfolio as recorded by the principle (in base currency).
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: calculationDateTime Description: Indicates the date when the exposure is calculated if different from valuation date.
--     * Slot: valuationDateTime Description: Indicates the valuation date of the exposure underlying the calculation.
--     * Slot: tradePortfolio_id Description: Represents a Portfolio that describes all the positions held at a given time, in various states which can be either traded, settled, etc., with lineage information to the previous state.
--     * Slot: aggregateValue_id Description: Represents the aggregate value of the portfolio in base currency.
-- # Class: IndexTransitionInstruction Description: Defines the information needed to create a Index Transition Business Event.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: effectiveDate Description: Specifies the effective date of the index transition event. This is first date on which the floating rate calculation will use the new floating rate index and adjusted spread in the floating rate calculation.
--     * Slot: cashTransfer_id Description: Specifies the cash transfer that can optionally be tied to an index transition event.
-- # Class: Instruction Description: Instruction to a function that will be used to perform a business event
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: primitiveInstruction_id Description: Specifies the primitive instructions that will be used to call primitive event functions.
--     * Slot: before_id Description: Specifies the trade state that will be acted on by the primitive event functions.
-- # Class: Lineage Description: A class to provide lineage information across lifecycle events through a pointer or set of pointers into the event(s), contract(s) and, possibly, payout components that the event is dependent on or relates to. As an example, if an contractFormation event is corrected, the correction event will have a lineage into the initial event, which takes the form of a globalKey into that initial contract formation event. Two referencing mechanisms are provided as part of the CDM: either the globalKey, which corresponds to the hash value of the CDM class which is referred to, or a reference qualifier which is meant to provide support for the ingestion of xml documents with id/href mechanisms. The CDM recommends the use of the globalKey and provides a default implementation which is accessible in the generated code through org.finos.cdm.globalKey.GlobalKeyHashCalculator. If implementers want to use an alternative hashing mechanism, the API in which they need to plug it is com.rosetta.model.lib.HashFunction.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: MarginCallBase Description: Represents common attributes required for Issuance and Response to a Margin Call action as a result of a demand for delivery or return of collateral determined under a legal agreement such as a credit support document or equivalent.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: regMarginType Description: Identifies margin type and if related regulatory mandate
--     * Slot: regIMRole Description: Indicates the role of the party in an regulatory initial margin call instruction (i.e Pledgor party or Secured party).
--     * Slot: instructionType_id Description: Identifies the enumeration values to specify the call notification type, direction, specific action type.
--     * Slot: clearingBroker_id Description: Indicates the name of the Clearing Broker FCM/DCM.
--     * Slot: callIdentifier_id Description: Represents a unique Identifier for a margin call message, that can be referenced throughout all points of the process.
--     * Slot: callAgreementType_id Description: Specifies the legal agreement type the margin call is generated from and governed by.
--     * Slot: agreementMinimumTransferAmount_id Description: Specifies the collateral legal agreement minimum transfer amount in base currency.
--     * Slot: agreementThreshold_id Description: Specifies the collateral legal agreement threshold amount in base currency.
--     * Slot: agreementRounding_id Description: Specifies the collateral legal agreement rounding in base currency.
--     * Slot: baseCurrencyExposure_id Description: Represents the current mark to market value or IM calculation value of the trade portfolio as recorded by the principle (in base currency), to be referenced in a margin call.
--     * Slot: collateralPortfolio_id Description: Represents attributes to define the details of collateral assets within a collateral portfolio to be used in margin call messaging and contribute to collateral balances e.g securities in a collateral account recorded by the principal as held or posted.
--     * Slot: independentAmountBalance_id Description: Represents additional credit support amount over and above mark to market value.
-- # Class: MarginCallExposure Description: Represents attributes required for mark to market value or IM calculation value of the trade portfolio as recorded by the principle (in base currency).
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: regMarginType Description: Identifies margin type and if related regulatory mandate
--     * Slot: regIMRole Description: Indicates the role of the party in an regulatory initial margin call instruction (i.e Pledgor party or Secured party).
--     * Slot: overallExposure_id Description: Represents the whole overall mark to market value or IM calculation value of the trade portfolio as recorded by the principle (in base currency).
--     * Slot: simmIMExposure_id Description: Represents Initial Margin (IM) exposure derived from ISDA SIMM calculation.
--     * Slot: scheduleGridIMExposure_id Description: Represents Initial Margin (IM) exposure derived from schedule or Grid calculation.
--     * Slot: instructionType_id Description: Identifies the enumeration values to specify the call notification type, direction, specific action type.
--     * Slot: clearingBroker_id Description: Indicates the name of the Clearing Broker FCM/DCM.
--     * Slot: callIdentifier_id Description: Represents a unique Identifier for a margin call message, that can be referenced throughout all points of the process.
--     * Slot: callAgreementType_id Description: Specifies the legal agreement type the margin call is generated from and governed by.
--     * Slot: agreementMinimumTransferAmount_id Description: Specifies the collateral legal agreement minimum transfer amount in base currency.
--     * Slot: agreementThreshold_id Description: Specifies the collateral legal agreement threshold amount in base currency.
--     * Slot: agreementRounding_id Description: Specifies the collateral legal agreement rounding in base currency.
--     * Slot: baseCurrencyExposure_id Description: Represents the current mark to market value or IM calculation value of the trade portfolio as recorded by the principle (in base currency), to be referenced in a margin call.
--     * Slot: collateralPortfolio_id Description: Represents attributes to define the details of collateral assets within a collateral portfolio to be used in margin call messaging and contribute to collateral balances e.g securities in a collateral account recorded by the principal as held or posted.
--     * Slot: independentAmountBalance_id Description: Represents additional credit support amount over and above mark to market value.
-- # Class: MarginCallInstructionType Description: Represents enumeration values to specify the call notification type, direction, specific action type.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: callType Description: Indicates the status of the call message type, such as expected call, notification of a call or an actionable margin call.
--     * Slot: visibilityIndicator Description: Indicates the choice if the call instruction is visible or not to the other party.
-- # Class: MarginCallIssuance Description: Represents common attributes required for a Margin Call Issuance under a legal agreement such as a credit support document or equivalent.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: regMarginType Description: Identifies margin type and if related regulatory mandate
--     * Slot: regIMRole Description: Indicates the role of the party in an regulatory initial margin call instruction (i.e Pledgor party or Secured party).
--     * Slot: callAmountInBaseCurrency_id Description: Specifies the amount of margin being called for which accounts for margin calculation inclusive of exposure, independent amount,threshold,collateral balance, MTA, rounding increments (in base currency detailed in supporting collateral agreement).
--     * Slot: instructionType_id Description: Identifies the enumeration values to specify the call notification type, direction, specific action type.
--     * Slot: clearingBroker_id Description: Indicates the name of the Clearing Broker FCM/DCM.
--     * Slot: callIdentifier_id Description: Represents a unique Identifier for a margin call message, that can be referenced throughout all points of the process.
--     * Slot: callAgreementType_id Description: Specifies the legal agreement type the margin call is generated from and governed by.
--     * Slot: agreementMinimumTransferAmount_id Description: Specifies the collateral legal agreement minimum transfer amount in base currency.
--     * Slot: agreementThreshold_id Description: Specifies the collateral legal agreement threshold amount in base currency.
--     * Slot: agreementRounding_id Description: Specifies the collateral legal agreement rounding in base currency.
--     * Slot: baseCurrencyExposure_id Description: Represents the current mark to market value or IM calculation value of the trade portfolio as recorded by the principle (in base currency), to be referenced in a margin call.
--     * Slot: collateralPortfolio_id Description: Represents attributes to define the details of collateral assets within a collateral portfolio to be used in margin call messaging and contribute to collateral balances e.g securities in a collateral account recorded by the principal as held or posted.
--     * Slot: independentAmountBalance_id Description: Represents additional credit support amount over and above mark to market value.
-- # Class: MarginCallResponse Description: Represents common attributes required for a Margin Call Response under a legal agreement such as a credit support document or equivalent.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: marginResponseType Description: Indicates the response type, such as, is the margin call response a 'full' 'part' agreement or 'dispute'.
--     * Slot: regMarginType Description: Identifies margin type and if related regulatory mandate
--     * Slot: regIMRole Description: Indicates the role of the party in an regulatory initial margin call instruction (i.e Pledgor party or Secured party).
--     * Slot: agreedAmountBaseCurrency_id Description: Indicates the amount that posting entity agrees to remit in response to margin call (in base currency).
--     * Slot: instructionType_id Description: Identifies the enumeration values to specify the call notification type, direction, specific action type.
--     * Slot: clearingBroker_id Description: Indicates the name of the Clearing Broker FCM/DCM.
--     * Slot: callIdentifier_id Description: Represents a unique Identifier for a margin call message, that can be referenced throughout all points of the process.
--     * Slot: callAgreementType_id Description: Specifies the legal agreement type the margin call is generated from and governed by.
--     * Slot: agreementMinimumTransferAmount_id Description: Specifies the collateral legal agreement minimum transfer amount in base currency.
--     * Slot: agreementThreshold_id Description: Specifies the collateral legal agreement threshold amount in base currency.
--     * Slot: agreementRounding_id Description: Specifies the collateral legal agreement rounding in base currency.
--     * Slot: baseCurrencyExposure_id Description: Represents the current mark to market value or IM calculation value of the trade portfolio as recorded by the principle (in base currency), to be referenced in a margin call.
--     * Slot: collateralPortfolio_id Description: Represents attributes to define the details of collateral assets within a collateral portfolio to be used in margin call messaging and contribute to collateral balances e.g securities in a collateral account recorded by the principal as held or posted.
--     * Slot: independentAmountBalance_id Description: Represents additional credit support amount over and above mark to market value.
-- # Class: MarginCallResponseAction Description: Specifies the margin call action details, including collateral to be moved and its direction.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: marginCallAction Description: Specifies the margin call action details, specified as either Delivery or Return.
-- # Class: Merger Description: Defines the underlier for both the Purchaser Company and the Acquired Compagny involved in Merger corporate action, as well as th respective price observation for each.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: purchaserSecurity_id Description: Defines the underlier for the Purchaser Company involved in Merger corporate action.
--     * Slot: purchaserSecurityPrice_id Description: The price observation that relates to underlier for the Purchaser Company.
--     * Slot: acquiredSecurity_id Description: Defines the underlier for the Acquired Company involved in Merger corporate action.
--     * Slot: acquiredSecurityPrice_id Description: The price observation that relates to underlier for the Acquired Company.
-- # Class: ObservationEvent Description: Specifies the necessary information to create any observation event.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: creditEvent_id Description: Specifies the necessary information to create a credit event.
--     * Slot: corporateAction_id Description: Specifies the necessary information to create a corporate action.
-- # Class: ObservationInstruction Description: Specifies inputs needed to process an observation.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: observationEvent_id Description: Contains all information related to an observation.
-- # Class: PartyChangeInstruction Description: Specifies instruction to change the party on a trade. This primitive instruction is used in a number of scenarios including: clearing, allocation and novation. The instrution must include a trade identifier, because a change of party effectively results in a different trade.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: counterparty_id Description: The new counterparty who is stepping into the trade. The stepping out counterparty is inferred based on the counterparty role that is being updated.
--     * Slot: ancillaryParty_id Description: Specifies an ancillary party to be added onto the new transaction, e.g. the original executing party in an allocation.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: Specifies an additional party roles to be added on to the new transaction.
-- # Class: PayoutTransferBase Description: Defines a transfer of an Asset associated with an economic payout - either a payout's own scheduled terms or an outcome contingent on some other event. Carries a reference back to that Payout, and allows the transfer's payer/receiver to be expressed as a generic, unresolved Party1 / Party2 enumerator, since a transfer generated directly from a payout's terms may not yet be tied to resolved parties.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: payerReceiver_id Description: Specifies who pays/receives the transfer, through a normalised Party1 / Party2 enumerator, for use before the transfer is resolved to actual parties.
--     * Slot: payoutReference_id Description: Represents the origin to the transfer as a reference for lineage purposes, whether it originated from trade level settlement terms or from payment terms on an economic payout.
--     * Slot: quantity_id Description: Represents the amount of the asset to be transferred. The cashflow amount is always a positive number, as the cashflow direction is implied by the payer/receiver attribute.
--     * Slot: asset_id Description: Represents the object that is subject to the transfer, it could be an asset or a reference.
--     * Slot: settlementDate_id Description: Represents the date on which the transfer to due.
--     * Slot: paymentDiscounting_id Description: FpML specifies the FpML PaymentDiscounting.model group for representing the discounting elements that can be associated with a payment.
--     * Slot: partyReferencePayerReceiver_id Description: Represents the resolved parties to the transfer and their role.
-- # Class: PositionIdentifier Description: Defines a position identifier as a special case of the generic identifier type, that also includes the position identifier class.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: identifierType Description: The enumerated classification of the identifier. Optional as a position identifier may be party-specific, in which case it may not correspond to any established classification.
--     * Slot: issuer Description: The identifier issuer, when specified explicitly alongside the identifier value (instead of being specified by reference to a party).
--     * Slot: issuerReference_id Description: The identifier issuer, when specified by reference to a party specified as part of the transaction.
-- # Class: PrimitiveInstruction Description: A Primitive Instruction describes the inputs required to pass into the corresponding PrimitiveEvent function.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: contractFormation_id Description: Specifies instructions describing an contract formation primitive event.
--     * Slot: execution_id Description: Specifies instructions describing an execution primitive event.
--     * Slot: exercise_id Description: Specifies instructions describing an exercise primitive event.
--     * Slot: partyChange_id Description: Specifies instructions describing a party change primitive event.
--     * Slot: quantityChange_id Description: Specifies instructions describing an quantity change primitive event.
--     * Slot: reset_id Description: Specifies instructions describing a reset event.
--     * Slot: split_id Description: Specifies instructions to split a trade into multiple branches.
--     * Slot: termsChange_id Description: Specifies instructions describing a terms change primitive event.
--     * Slot: transfer_id Description: Specifies instructions describing a transfer primitive event.
--     * Slot: indexTransition_id Description: Specifies inputs needed to process a Index Transition business event.
--     * Slot: stockSplit_id Description: Specifies inputs needed to process a Stock Split business event.
--     * Slot: observation_id Description: Specifies inputs needed to process an observation.
--     * Slot: valuation_id Description: Specifies inputs needed to process an update of a valuation.
-- # Class: QuantityChangeInstruction Description: Instructions required to create a Quantity Change Primitive Event, which can be either an increase, a decrease or a replacement. An increase adds a new trade lot to the original trade, whereas a decrease subtracts from an existing trade lot's quantity. A replacement updates the quantity of an existing trade lot to the new value.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: direction Description: Direction of the quantity change specified as either an increase, decrease or replacement.
-- # Class: Reset Description: Defines the reset value or fixing value produced in cashflow calculations, during the life-cycle of a financial instrument. The reset process defined in Create_Reset function joins product definition details with observations to compute the reset value.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: resetDate Description: Specifies the date on which the reset occurred.
--     * Slot: rateRecordDate Description: Specifies the 'Rate Record Day' for a Fallback rate. Fallback rate fixing processes typically set the fixing rate in arrears, i.e., the Fallback Rate corresponding to a Rate Record Date is set at the end of the interest accural period. When this applies, Reset->resetDate occurs at the end of the interest period, and the Reset->rateRecordDate occurs near the start of the interest period. The Reset->rateRecordDate and Reset->observations->observationIdentifier->observationDate will differ if a Fallback rate is unavailable on the Rate Record Date, and the latest previous available rate is used as the observation.
--     * Slot: resetValue_id Description: Specifies the reset or fixing value. The fixing value could be a cash price, interest rate, or other value.
--     * Slot: averagingMethodology_id Description: Identifies the aggregation method to use in the case where multiple observations are used to compute the reset value and the method is not defined in a payout.
-- # Class: ResetInstruction Description: Defines the information needed to execute a Reset Business Event.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: ReturnInstruction Description: Specifies the information required to create the return of a Security Finance Transaction.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: ScheduledTransfer Description: A scheduled transfer built into the contract. Extends PayoutTransferBase because a Scheduled Transfer originates from a Payout.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: transferType Description: Specifies the type of Scheduled Transfer.
--     * Slot: payerReceiver_id Description: Specifies who pays/receives the transfer, through a normalised Party1 / Party2 enumerator, for use before the transfer is resolved to actual parties.
--     * Slot: payoutReference_id Description: Represents the origin to the transfer as a reference for lineage purposes, whether it originated from trade level settlement terms or from payment terms on an economic payout.
--     * Slot: quantity_id Description: Represents the amount of the asset to be transferred. The cashflow amount is always a positive number, as the cashflow direction is implied by the payer/receiver attribute.
--     * Slot: asset_id Description: Represents the object that is subject to the transfer, it could be an asset or a reference.
--     * Slot: settlementDate_id Description: Represents the date on which the transfer to due.
--     * Slot: paymentDiscounting_id Description: FpML specifies the FpML PaymentDiscounting.model group for representing the discounting elements that can be associated with a payment.
--     * Slot: partyReferencePayerReceiver_id Description: Represents the resolved parties to the transfer and their role.
-- # Class: SecurityLendingInvoice Description: Specifies the information required for inclusion in a securities lending billing invoice.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: billingStartDate Description: The starting date of the period described by this invoice
--     * Slot: billingEndDate Description: The ending date of the period described by this invoice
--     * Slot: sendingParty_id Description: The party issuing the invoice
--     * Slot: receivingParty_id Description: The party receiving the invoice
-- # Class: SpinOff Description: Defines the underlier for both the Parent Company and the Child Compagny involved in Spin Off corporate action, as well as th respective price observation for each.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: parentSecurity_id Description: Defines the underlier for the Parent Company involved in Spin Off corporate action.
--     * Slot: parentSecurityPrice_id Description: The price observation that relates to underlier for the Parent Company.
--     * Slot: childSecurity_id Description: Defines the underlier for the Child Company involved in Spin Off corporate action.
--     * Slot: childSecurityPrice_id Description: The price observation that relates to underlier for the Child Company.
-- # Class: SplitInstruction Description: Specifies instructions for a split, consisting of a breakdown of instructions to be applied to each branch of the split. This instruction can be used to duplicate a trade, as in a clearing scenario, or to split a trade into smaller quantities (in which case each breakdown instruction needs to include a quantity change), as in an allocation.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: State Description: Defines the state of a trade at a point in the Trade's life cycle. Trades have many state dimensions, all of which are represented here. For example, states useful for position keeping are represented alongside those needed for regulatory reporting.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: positionState Description: Identifies the state of the position, to distinguish if just executed, formed, already settled, closed, etc.
--     * Slot: closedState_id Description: Represents the qualification of what led to the trade's closure alongside the dates on which this closure took effect.
-- # Class: StockSplitInstruction Description: Data required to perform a stock split business event.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: adjustmentRatio Description: The number that denotes the cumulative quantity of post-split shares issued to shareholders versus the quantity of pre-split shares previously issued to shareholders. This number will be multiplied by existing shares in an equity derivative contract or other positions to determine the post-split number of shares. With regard to any reference to price, the pre-split reference price will be divided by this number to determine the post-split reference price.
--     * Slot: effectiveDate Description: The effective date of the stock split, also known as the ex-date. This is the date on which the additional shares are paid to the shareholders, or in the case of a reverse stock split, the number shares held by each shareholder is proportionally reduced. Equity derivative transactions can be amended in firms' internal systems on such date. In most markets, the listed stock price is reduced (or increased for a reverse stock split) to account for the split on the same date, but in some markets the price adjustment occurs on a later date. In either case, equity derivative transactions should be amended on the date that the stocks are paid to the shareholders (or consolidated).
-- # Class: TermsChangeInstruction Description: Specifies instructions for terms change consisting of the new transaction terms, and the renegotiation fee.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: adjustment
--     * Slot: product_id Description: product to be changed
-- # Class: Trade Description: Defines the output of a financial transaction between parties - a Business Event. A Trade impacts the financial position (i.e. the balance sheet) of involved parties.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: tradeDate Description: Specifies the date which the trade was agreed.
--     * Slot: adjustment Description: Specifies the conditions that govern the adjustment to the quantity of a product being traded: e.g. execution, portfolio rebalancing etc. It is typically used in the context of Equity Swaps.
--     * Slot: tradeTime_id Description: Denotes the trade time and timezone as agreed by the parties to the trade.
--     * Slot: executionDetails_id Description: Represents information specific to trades that arose from executions.
--     * Slot: contractDetails_id Description: Represents information specific to trades involving contractual products.
--     * Slot: collateral_id Description: Represents the collateral obligations of a party.
--     * Slot: product_id Description: The underlying product to be included in a contract or execution.
-- # Class: TradeIdentifier Description: Defines a trade identifier as a special case of the generic identifier type, that also includes the trade identifier class.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: identifierType Description: The enumerated classification of the identifier. Optional as a trade identifier may be party-specific, in which case it may not correspond to any established classification.
--     * Slot: issuer Description: The identifier issuer, when specified explicitly alongside the identifier value (instead of being specified by reference to a party).
--     * Slot: issuerReference_id Description: The identifier issuer, when specified by reference to a party specified as part of the transaction.
-- # Class: TradePricingReport Description: The attributes that are specific for consensus based pricing reporting.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: discountingIndex Description: It specifies the interest payable on collateral delivered under a CSA covering the trade.
--     * Slot: trade_id Description: Represents the cosensus based pricing parameters on a trade basis.
--     * Slot: pricingTime_id Description: The regional exchange close time for the underlying contract,including time zone, at which the trades should be priced. This provides an indication for which regional snapshot should be used for pricing primarily for Global markets where there are multiple regional close times.
-- # Class: TradeState Description: Defines the fundamental financial information that can be changed by a Primitive Event and by extension any business or life-cycle event. Each TradeState specifies where a Trade is in its life-cycle. TradeState is a root type and as such, can be created independently to any other CDM data type, but can also be used as part of the CDM Event Model.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: trade_id Description: Represents the Trade that has been effected by a business or life-cycle event.
--     * Slot: state_id Description: Represents the State of the Trade through its life-cycle.
-- # Class: Transfer Description: The type of transfer.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: ScheduledTransfer_id Description: A transfer created from a scheduled event on a contract, e.g. Coupon, Dividend Return, Fixed Rate Return
--     * Slot: UnscheduledTransfer_id Description: An ad-hoc transfer instigated by a party to the contract e.g. Recall, Return.
--     * Slot: ContingentTransfer_id Description: A transfer created from a contingent event on a contract, e.g. Corporate Action, Credit Event or Exercise
-- # Class: TransferBase Description: Defines the transfer of an Asset (eg cash, securities or commodities) between two parties on a date.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: quantity_id Description: Represents the amount of the asset to be transferred. The cashflow amount is always a positive number, as the cashflow direction is implied by the payer/receiver attribute.
--     * Slot: asset_id Description: Represents the object that is subject to the transfer, it could be an asset or a reference.
--     * Slot: settlementDate_id Description: Represents the date on which the transfer to due.
--     * Slot: paymentDiscounting_id Description: FpML specifies the FpML PaymentDiscounting.model group for representing the discounting elements that can be associated with a payment.
--     * Slot: partyReferencePayerReceiver_id Description: Represents the resolved parties to the transfer and their role.
-- # Class: TransferInstruction Description: Defines the payout on which to create a Transfer along with all necessary resets.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: TransferState Description: Defines the fundamental financial information associated with a Transfer event. Each TransferState specifies where a Transfer is in its life-cycle. TransferState is a root type and as such, can be created independently to any other CDM data type, but can also be used as part of the CDM Event Model.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: transferStatus Description: Represents the State of the Transfer through its life-cycle.
--     * Slot: transfer_id Description: Represents the Transfer that has been effected by a business or life-cycle event.
-- # Class: UnscheduledTransfer Description: An ad-hoc transfer instigated by a party to the contract. Extends TransferBase rather than PayoutTransferBase because an Unscheduled Transfer is not derived from a Payout's terms - it is initiated by a party against a known counterparty, so it will always have a resolved payer/receiver.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: transferType Description: Specifies the type of unscheduled transfer.
--     * Slot: quantity_id Description: Represents the amount of the asset to be transferred. The cashflow amount is always a positive number, as the cashflow direction is implied by the payer/receiver attribute.
--     * Slot: asset_id Description: Represents the object that is subject to the transfer, it could be an asset or a reference.
--     * Slot: settlementDate_id Description: Represents the date on which the transfer to due.
--     * Slot: paymentDiscounting_id Description: FpML specifies the FpML PaymentDiscounting.model group for representing the discounting elements that can be associated with a payment.
--     * Slot: partyReferencePayerReceiver_id Description: Represents the resolved parties to the transfer and their role.
-- # Class: Valuation Description: Defines the value of an investment, asset, or security
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: timestamp Description: Date and time of the last valuation marked to market, provided by the central counterparty (CCP) or calculated using the current or last available market price of the inputs.
--     * Slot: source Description: Source of the valuation of the transaction by the valuation party.
--     * Slot: method Description: Method used for the valuation of the transaction by the valuation party.
--     * Slot: scope Description: Defines the scope of the valuation, what it applies to e.g. the collateral or the trade
--     * Slot: delta Description: The ratio of the change in the price of a derivative transaction to the change in the price of the underlying. This field is applicable only to options and swaptions.
--     * Slot: valuationTiming Description: Denotes when the valuation was sourced during a business day.
--     * Slot: amount_id Description: Current value of the outstanding contract
--     * Slot: priceComponent_id Description: Denotes the price used to compute the valuation.
-- # Class: ValuationInstruction Description: Specifies inputs needed to process a valuation.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: replace Description: Specifies whether the previous valuation tracks in the valuation history are removed (True) or kept (False).
-- # Class: AssetFloatingRateIndex Description: Specification of an interest rate index which can change over time, e.g. the SONIA (Sterling Overnight Index Average) in the UK.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: floatingRateIndex Description: The reference index that is used to specify the floating interest rate.
--     * Slot: name Description: A description of the Index.
--     * Slot: assetClass Description: The Asset Class of the Index.
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: indexTenor_id Description: The ISDA Designated Maturity, i.e. the floating rate tenor.
--     * Slot: provider_id Description: The organisation that creates or maintains the Index.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: AssetSettlementRateOption Description: Defines the settlement rate option to use for fixing in case of cash settlement. Currently only applicable to foreign exchange fixing in case of cross-currency settlement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: settlementRateOption Description: The rate source for the conversion to the settlement currency. This source is specified through a scheme that reflects the terms of the Annex A to the 1998 FX and Currency Option Definitions.
--     * Slot: priceSourceDisruption_id Description: An attribute defining the parameters to get a new quote when a settlement rate option is disrupted.
-- # Class: Basket Description: Defines a custom basket by referencing an identifier and its constituents.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: BasketConstituent Description: Identifies the constituents of the basket
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: observable_id Description: Specifies the object to be observed for a price, it could be an asset or a reference, within the context of a Basket
-- # Class: CalculationAgent Description: A class defining the ISDA calculation agent responsible for performing duties as defined in the applicable product definitions.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: calculationAgentParty Description: Specifies the party which is the ISDA Calculation Agent for the trade. If more than one party is referenced then the parties are assumed to be co-calculation agents, i.e. they have joint responsibility.
--     * Slot: calculationAgentPartyEnum Description: Specifies the ISDA calculation agent responsible for performing duties as defined in the applicable product definitions. For example, the Calculation Agent may be defined as being the Non-exercising Party.
--     * Slot: calculationAgentBusinessCenter Description: The city in which the office through which ISDA Calculation Agent is acting for purposes of the transaction is located The short-form confirm for a trade that is executed under a Sovereign or Asia Pacific Master Confirmation Agreement ( MCA ), does not need to specify the Calculation Agent. However, the confirm does need to specify the Calculation Agent City. This is due to the fact that the MCA sets the value for Calculation Agent but does not set the value for Calculation Agent City.
-- # Class: CashCollateralValuationMethod Description: This type is a generic structure that can represent the parameters of several mid-market valuation and replacement value methods described in the 2021 ISDA Definitions.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: applicableCsa Description: This may be used to specify what type of CSA (credit support annex/agreement) is to be used for cash settlement purposes.
--     * Slot: cashCollateralCurrency Description: This may be used to indicate the currency of cash collateral for cash settlement purposes.
--     * Slot: cashCollateralInterestRate Description: This may be used to indicate the interest rate to be used for cash collateral for cash settlement purposes.
--     * Slot: agreedDiscountRate Description: This may be used to indicate the discount rate to be used for cash collateral for cash settlement purposes.
--     * Slot: prescribedDocumentationAdjustment Description: This may be used to indicate that 'prescribed documentation adjustment' is applicable.
-- # Class: CreditIndex Description: Specification of an index based on credit risk, typically composed using corporate debt instruments in a region or industry sector, e.g. the iTraxx indices.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: indexSeries Description: A CDS index series identifier, e.g. 1, 2, 3 etc.
--     * Slot: indexAnnexVersion Description: A CDS index series version identifier, e.g. 1, 2, 3 etc.
--     * Slot: indexAnnexDate Description: A CDS index series annex date.
--     * Slot: indexAnnexSource Description: A CDS index series annex source.
--     * Slot: indexFactor Description: Index Factor is the index version factor or percent, expressed as an absolute decimal value between 0 and 1, that multiplied by the original notional amount yields the notional amount covered by the seller of protection.
--     * Slot: seniority Description: Seniority of debt instruments comprising the index.
--     * Slot: name Description: A description of the Index.
--     * Slot: assetClass Description: The Asset Class of the Index.
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: tranche_id Description: This element contains CDS tranche terms.
--     * Slot: settledEntityMatrix_id Description: Used to specify the Relevant Settled Entity Matrix when there are settled entities at the time of the trade.
--     * Slot: provider_id Description: The organisation that creates or maintains the Index.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: CreditNotation Description: Represents a class to specify the credit notation as the combination of agency, notation, scale and debt type qualifications.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: agency Description: Specifies The credit agency to which the other variables (notation, scale, debt type) refer to.
--     * Slot: notation Description: Specifies The credit rating notation. As it varies among credit rating agencies, FpML doesn't specify a default scheme.
--     * Slot: scale Description: Specifies the credit rating scale, with a typical distinction between short term, long term. FpML doesn't specify a default scheme, which is hence not specified as an enumeration as part of the CDM.
--     * Slot: outlook Description: Assesses the potential direction of a long-term credit rating over the intermediate term, which is generally up to two years for investment grade and generally up to one year for speculative grade.
--     * Slot: creditWatch Description: Indicates the potential direction of a short-term or long-term rating. It focuses on identifiable events and short-term trends that cause ratings to be placed under special surveillance.
--     * Slot: debt_id Description: Specifies the credit rating debt type (e.g. long term, high yield, deposits, ...) associated with the credit rating notation and scale.
-- # Class: CreditNotations Description: Represents the credit rating notation higher level construct, which provides the ability to specify multiple rating notations.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: creditNotation_id Description: Specifies only one credit notation is determined.
--     * Slot: creditNotations_id Description: Specifies if several credit notations exist, alongside an 'any' or 'all' or all condition.
-- # Class: CreditRatingDebt Description: Specifies the credit rating debt type(s) associated with the credit rating notation and scale. When several debt types are specified, they must be qualified through an 'any' or 'all'.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: debtType Description: Specifies when there is only one debt type. FpML doesn't specify values in relation to the associated scheme, which is hence not specified as an enumeration as part of the CDM.
--     * Slot: debtTypes_id Description: Specifies if there are several debt types, alongside an 'any' or 'all' or all condition. As an example, Baa1 rating is required for any long term debt and deposit.
-- # Class: DividendApplicability Description: The parameters which define whether dividends are applicable
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: optionsExchangeDividends Description: If present and true, then options exchange dividends are applicable.
--     * Slot: additionalDividends Description: If present and true, then additional dividends are applicable.
--     * Slot: allDividends Description: Represents the European Master Confirmation value of 'All Dividends' which, when applicable, signifies that, for a given Ex-Date, the daily observed Share Price for that day is adjusted (reduced) by the cash dividend and/or the cash value of any non cash dividend per Share (including Extraordinary Dividends) declared by the Issuer. All Dividends in accordance with the ISDA 2002 Equity Derivatives Definitions.
-- # Class: EquityIndex Description: Specification of an index based on equity securities, e.g. the S&P 500.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: name Description: A description of the Index.
--     * Slot: assetClass Description: The Asset Class of the Index.
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: provider_id Description: The organisation that creates or maintains the Index.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: FallbackReferencePrice Description: The method, prioritised by the order it is listed in this element, to get a replacement rate for the disrupted settlement rate option.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: fallbackSurveyValuationPostponement Description: Request rate quotes from the market. This element is set as type Empty in FpML. When present, the FpML synonym is mapped to a value True in the CDM.
--     * Slot: valuationPostponement_id Description: Specifies how long to wait to get a quote from a settlement rate option upon a price source disruption.
--     * Slot: calculationAgentDetermination_id Description: The calculation agent will decide the rate.
-- # Class: ForeignExchangeRateIndex Description: Specification of a rate based on the exchange of a pair of cash assets in specific currencies, e.g. USD versus GBP.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: name Description: A description of the Index.
--     * Slot: assetClass Description: The Asset Class of the Index.
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: quotedCurrencyPair_id Description: Describes the composition of a rate that has been quoted or is to be quoted.
--     * Slot: primaryFxSpotRateSource_id Description: Specifies the primary source from which a rate should be observed.
--     * Slot: secondaryFxSpotRateSource_id Description: Specifies an alternative, or secondary, source from which a rate should be observed.
--     * Slot: provider_id Description: The organisation that creates or maintains the Index.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: FxInformationSource Description: Information source specific to Foreign Exchange products.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: sourceProvider Description: An information source for obtaining a market data point. For example Bloomberg, Reuters, Telerate, etc.
--     * Slot: sourcePage Description: A specific page for the source for obtaining a market data point. In FpML, this is specified as a scheme, rateSourcePageScheme, for which no coding Scheme or URI is specified.
--     * Slot: sourcePageHeading Description: The heading for the source on a given source page.
--     * Slot: fixingTime_id Description: The time that the fixing will be taken along with a business center to define the time zone.
-- # Class: FxRate Description: A class describing the rate of a currency conversion: pair of currency, quotation mode and exchange rate.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: rate Description: The rate of exchange between the two currencies of the leg of a deal. Must be specified with a quote basis.
--     * Slot: quotedCurrencyPair_id Description: Defines the two currencies for an FX trade and the quotation relationship between the two currencies.
-- # Class: FxRateSourceFixing Description: Describes a rate source to be fixed and the date the fixing occurs
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: settlementRateSource_id
--     * Slot: fixingDate_id Description: The date on which the fixing is scheduled to occur.
-- # Class: FxSettlementRateSource Description: The source of the Foreign Exchange settlement rate.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: settlementRateOption Description: Indicates that an officially defined rate settlement rate option will be the used for the fixing.
--     * Slot: nonstandardSettlementRate_id Description: Indicates that a non-standard rate source will be used for the fixing.
-- # Class: FxSpotRateSource Description: A class defining the rate source and fixing time for an FX rate.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: primarySource_id Description: The primary source for where the rate observation will occur. Will typically be either a page or a reference bank published rate.
--     * Slot: secondarySource_id Description: An alternative, or secondary, source for where the rate observation will occur. Will typically be either a page or a reference bank published rate.
-- # Class: Index Description: An Index is an Observable which is computed based on the prices, rates or valuations of a number of assets that are tracked in a standardized way. Examples include equity market indices as well as indices on interest rates, inflation and credit instruments.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: CreditIndex_id Description: An index based on credit risk, typically composed using corporate debt instruments in a region or industry sector, e.g. the iTraxx indices.
--     * Slot: EquityIndex_id Description: An index based on equity securities, e.g. the S&P 500.
--     * Slot: InterestRateIndex_id Description: An index based in interest rates or inflation rates in a certain market.
--     * Slot: ForeignExchangeRateIndex_id Description: A rate based on the exchange of a pair of cash assets in specific currencies, e.g. USD versus GBP.
--     * Slot: OtherIndex_id Description: An index created by a market participant which doesn't align with the other index types.
-- # Class: IndexBase Description: Identifies an index by referencing an identifier.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: name Description: A description of the Index.
--     * Slot: assetClass Description: The Asset Class of the Index.
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: provider_id Description: The organisation that creates or maintains the Index.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: InflationIndex Description: Specification of an index that measures inflation in a specific market, e.g. the US Consumer Price Index.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: inflationRateIndex Description: The reference index that is used to specify the inflation interest rate.
--     * Slot: name Description: A description of the Index.
--     * Slot: assetClass Description: The Asset Class of the Index.
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: indexTenor_id Description: The ISDA Designated Maturity, i.e. the floating rate tenor.
--     * Slot: provider_id Description: The organisation that creates or maintains the Index.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: InformationSource Description: A class defining the source for a piece of information (e.g. a rate fix or an FX fixing). The attribute names have been adjusted from FpML to address the fact that the information is not limited to rates.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: sourceProvider Description: An information source for obtaining a market data point. For example Bloomberg, Reuters, Telerate, etc.
--     * Slot: sourcePage Description: A specific page for the source for obtaining a market data point. In FpML, this is specified as a scheme, rateSourcePageScheme, for which no coding Scheme or URI is specified.
--     * Slot: sourcePageHeading Description: The heading for the source on a given source page.
-- # Class: InterestRateIndex Description: An index based in interest rates or inflation rates in a certain market.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: FloatingRateIndex_id Description: An interest rate index which can change over time, e.g. the SONIA (Sterling Overnight Index Average) in the UK.
--     * Slot: InflationIndex_id Description: An index that measures inflation in a specific market, e.g. the US Consumer Price Index.
-- # Class: MakeWholeAmount Description: A class to specify the amount to be paid by the buyer of the option if the option is exercised prior to the Early Call Date (typically applicable to the convertible bond options).
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: interpolationMethod Description: The type of interpolation method that the calculation agent reserves the right to use.
--     * Slot: earlyCallDate Description: Date prior to which the option buyer will have to pay a Make Whole Amount to the option seller if he/she exercises the option.
--     * Slot: floatingRateIndex
--     * Slot: spread Description: Spread in basis points over the floating rate index.
--     * Slot: side Description: The side (bid/mid/ask) of the measure.
--     * Slot: indexTenor_id Description: The ISDA Designated Maturity, i.e. the tenor of the floating rate.
-- # Class: Money Description: Defines a monetary amount in a specified currency.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value Description: Requires the single rate or amount, as the case may be, to be present. An initial rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
--     * Slot: multiplier_id Description: Defines an optional measure that the quantity should be multiplied by to derive a total quantity. Requires that the multiplier must be positive. This number is associated to an optional unit. For example in the case of the Coal (API2) CIF ARA (ARGUS-McCloskey) Futures Contract on the CME, where the unit would be contracts, the multiplier value would 1,000 and the mulitiplier unit would be 1,000 MT (Metric Tons).
--     * Slot: frequency_id Description: Defines the frequency to be used when defining a quantity. For example a quantity may be specified as a number of barrels of oil per day, which needs multiplying by the number of days in the relevant period to get the total quantity as a number of barrels.
--     * Slot: total_id Description: Specifies the total quantity when the quantity itself is specified with a frequency.
--     * Slot: unit_id Description: Requires that a unit of amount must be specified for any quantity.
-- # Class: MultipleCreditNotations Description: Represetns a class to specify multiple credit notations alongside a conditional 'any' or 'all' qualifier.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: MultipleDebtTypes Description: Represents a class to specify multiple credit debt types alongside a conditional 'any' or 'all' qualifier.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: MultipleValuationDates
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: businessDaysThereafter Description: The number of business days between successive valuation dates when multiple valuation dates are applicable for cash settlement. ISDA 2003 Term: Business Days thereafter.
--     * Slot: numberValuationDates Description: Where multiple valuation dates are specified as being applicable for cash settlement, this element specifies (a) the number of applicable valuation dates, and (b) the number of business days after satisfaction of all conditions to settlement when the first such valuation date occurs, and (c) the number of business days thereafter of each successive valuation date. ISDA 2003 Term: Multiple Valuation Dates.
--     * Slot: businessDays Description: A number of business days. Its precise meaning is dependant on the context in which this element is used. ISDA 2003 Term: Business Day.
-- # Class: Observable Description: Specifies the object to be observed for a price, it could be an asset or a reference.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: Asset_id Description: The object to be observed is an Asset, ie something that can be owned and transferred in the financial markets.
--     * Slot: Basket_id Description: The object to be observed is a Basket, ie a collection of Observables with an identifier and optional weightings.
--     * Slot: Index_id Description: The object to be observed is an Index, ie an observable computed on the prices, rates or valuations of a number of assets.
-- # Class: OtherIndex Description: Specification of a user-defined index that does not meet the criteria of other Index data types.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: description Description: A description that defines the OtherIndex.
--     * Slot: name Description: A description of the Index.
--     * Slot: assetClass Description: The Asset Class of the Index.
--     * Slot: isExchangeListed Description: Defines whether the asset is listed on a public exchange.
--     * Slot: assetType Description: Specifies the type of asset.
--     * Slot: provider_id Description: The organisation that creates or maintains the Index.
--     * Slot: partyRole_id Description: The role of the payer specific to the asset type, i.e. bond, equity.
-- # Class: PerformanceValuationDates Description: Defines how and when a performance type option or performance type swap is to be valued.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: determinationMethod Description: Specifies the method according to which an amount or a date is determined.
--     * Slot: valuationTimeType Description: The time of day at which the calculation agent values the underlying, for example the official closing time of the exchange.
--     * Slot: valuationDates_id Description: 2018 ISDA CDM Equity Confirmation for Security Equity Swap: Pricing Date
--     * Slot: valuationDate_id Description: 2018 ISDA CDM Equity Confirmation for Security Equity Swap: Pricing Date
--     * Slot: valuationTime_id Description: The specific time of day at which the calculation agent values the underlying. The SpecificTime is the only case when the valuationTime (time + business center location e.g. 10:00:00 USNY) should be provided. You should be able to provide just the valuationTime without valuationTimeType, which infer that this is a specific time.
-- # Class: Price Description: Specifies a price as a single value to be associated to a financial product. This data type extends PriceSchedule and requires that only the amount value exists.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: priceType Description: Specifies the price type as an enumeration: interest rate, exchange rate, asset price etc. This attribute is mandatory so that prices can always be clasiffied according to their type. The price type implies some constraints on the price's units.
--     * Slot: priceSubType Description: Allows further classification of the chosen price type.
--     * Slot: priceExpression Description: (Optionally) Specifies whether the price is expressed in absolute or percentage terms.
--     * Slot: arithmeticOperator Description: (Optionally) When the price is to be understood as an operator to apply to an observable, i.e. a spread, multiplier or min/max.
--     * Slot: premiumType Description: (Optionally) Additional attribute that can further define any premium to the price.
--     * Slot: value Description: The initial rate or amount, as the case may be. An initial rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
--     * Slot: perUnitOf_id Description: Provides an attribute to define the unit of the thing being priced. For example, {amount, unitOfAmount, PerUnitOfAmount} = [10, EUR, Shares] = (10.00 EUR/SHARE) * (300,000 SHARES) = EUR 3,000,000.00 (Shares cancel out in the calculation).
--     * Slot: composite_id Description: (Optionally) Specifies the underlying price components if the price can be expressed as a composite: e.g. dirty price = clean price + accrued.
--     * Slot: derivedQuantity_id Description: Specifies the derived quantity associated with the price. For instance when the price is an asset price expressed in a currency, the primary quantity is the asset's quantity while the derived quantity is the corresponding monetary amount in that currency. When the price is an exchange rate, both the primary quantity and the derived quantity are monetary amounts, in the 2 currencies of the exchange rate.
--     * Slot: unit_id Description: Qualifies the unit by which the amount is measured. Optional because a measure may be unit-less (e.g. when representing a ratio between amounts in the same unit).
-- # Class: PriceComposite Description: Defines the inputs required to calculate a price as a simple composite of 2 other values. The inputs consist of 2 numbers and a simple arithmetic operator. This generic data type applies to a variety of use cases where a price is obtained by simple composition, e.g. dirty = clean + accrued (Bond), forward rate = spot rate + forward point (FX) etc.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: baseValue Description: The 1st value in the arithmetic operation, which may be non-commutative in some cases: Subtract, Divide). This 1st operand is called 'baseValue' as it refers to the price anchor in the arithmetic operation: e.g. the clean price (Bond) or the spot rate (FX).
--     * Slot: operand Description: The 2nd value in the arithmetic operation, which may be non-commutative in some cases: Subtract, Divide). The 2nd operand is called 'operand' to distinguish it from the 1st one which is the price anchor.
--     * Slot: arithmeticOperator Description: Specifies the arithmetic operator via an enumeration.
--     * Slot: operandType Description: Optionally qualifies the type of operand: e.g. accrued or forward point.
-- # Class: PriceQuantity Description: Defines a settlement as an exchange between two parties of a specified quantity of an asset (the quantity) against a specified quantity of another asset (the price). The settlement is optional and can be either cash or physical. The quantity can additionally be specified in terms of one or more currency amounts. In the case of non-cash products, the settlement of the price/quantity would not be specified here and instead would be delegated to the product mechanics, as parameterised by the price/quantity values.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: quantity_id Description: Specifies a quantity to be associated with an event, for example a trade amount.
--     * Slot: observable_id Description: Specifies the object to be observed for a price, it could be an asset or an index. The cardinality is optional as some quantity / price cases have no observable (e.g. a fixed rate in a given currency).
--     * Slot: effectiveDate_id Description: Specifies the date at which the price and quantity become effective. This day may be subject to adjustment in accordance with a business day convention, or could be specified as relative to a trade date, for instance. Optional cardinality, as the effective date is usually specified in the product definition, so it may only need to be specified as part of the PriceQuantity in an increase/decrease scenario for an existing trade.
-- # Class: PriceSchedule Description: Specifies the price of a financial instrument in a trade as a schedule of measures. A price generically expresses the value of an exchange as a ratio: it measures the amount of one thing needed to be exchanged for 1 unit of another thing (e.g. cash in a specific currency in exchange for a bond or share). This generic representation can be used to support any type of financial price beyond just cash price: e.g. an interest rate, a foreign exchange rate, etc. This data type is generically based on a schedule and can also be used to represent a price as a single value.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: priceType Description: Specifies the price type as an enumeration: interest rate, exchange rate, asset price etc. This attribute is mandatory so that prices can always be clasiffied according to their type. The price type implies some constraints on the price's units.
--     * Slot: priceSubType Description: Allows further classification of the chosen price type.
--     * Slot: priceExpression Description: (Optionally) Specifies whether the price is expressed in absolute or percentage terms.
--     * Slot: arithmeticOperator Description: (Optionally) When the price is to be understood as an operator to apply to an observable, i.e. a spread, multiplier or min/max.
--     * Slot: premiumType Description: (Optionally) Additional attribute that can further define any premium to the price.
--     * Slot: value Description: The initial rate or amount, as the case may be. An initial rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
--     * Slot: perUnitOf_id Description: Provides an attribute to define the unit of the thing being priced. For example, {amount, unitOfAmount, PerUnitOfAmount} = [10, EUR, Shares] = (10.00 EUR/SHARE) * (300,000 SHARES) = EUR 3,000,000.00 (Shares cancel out in the calculation).
--     * Slot: composite_id Description: (Optionally) Specifies the underlying price components if the price can be expressed as a composite: e.g. dirty price = clean price + accrued.
--     * Slot: derivedQuantity_id Description: Specifies the derived quantity associated with the price. For instance when the price is an asset price expressed in a currency, the primary quantity is the asset's quantity while the derived quantity is the corresponding monetary amount in that currency. When the price is an exchange rate, both the primary quantity and the derived quantity are monetary amounts, in the 2 currencies of the exchange rate.
--     * Slot: unit_id Description: Qualifies the unit by which the amount is measured. Optional because a measure may be unit-less (e.g. when representing a ratio between amounts in the same unit).
-- # Class: PriceSourceDisruption Description: A data defining: the parameters used to get a price quote to replace the settlement rate option that is disrupted.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: fallbackReferencePrice_id Description: The method, prioritised by the order it is listed in this element, to get a replacement rate for the disrupted settlement rate option.
-- # Class: QuotedCurrencyPair Description: A class that describes the composition of a rate that has been quoted or is to be quoted. This includes the two currencies and the quotation relationship between the two currencies and is used as a building block throughout the FX specification.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: currency1 Description: The first currency specified when a pair of currencies is to be evaluated.
--     * Slot: currency2 Description: The second currency specified when a pair of currencies is to be evaluated.
--     * Slot: quoteBasis Description: The method by which the exchange rate is quoted.
-- # Class: RateObservation Description: A class defining parameters associated with an individual observation or fixing. This class forms part of the cashflow representation of a stream.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: resetDate Description: The reset date.
--     * Slot: adjustedFixingDate Description: The adjusted fixing date, i.e. the actual date the rate is observed. The date should already be adjusted for any applicable business day convention.
--     * Slot: observedRate Description: The actual observed rate before any required rate treatment is applied, e.g. before converting a rate quoted on a discount basis to an equivalent yield. An observed rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
--     * Slot: treatedRate Description: The observed rate after any required rate treatment is applied. A treated rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
--     * Slot: observationWeight Description: The number of days weighting to be associated with the rate observation, i.e. the number of days such rate is in effect. This is applicable in the case of a weighted average method of calculation where more than one reset date is established for a single calculation period.
--     * Slot: forecastRate Description: The value representing the forecast rate used to calculate the forecast future value of the accrual period.A value of 1% should be represented as 0.01.
--     * Slot: treatedForecastRate Description: The value representing the forecast rate after applying rate treatment rules. A value of 1% should be represented as 0.01.
--     * Slot: rateReference_id Description: A pointer style reference to a floating rate component defined as part of a stub calculation period amount component. It is only required when it is necessary to distinguish two rate observations for the same fixing date which could occur when linear interpolation of two different rates occurs for a stub calculation period.
-- # Class: ReferenceSwapCurve Description: A complex type used to specify the option and convertible bond option strike when expressed in reference to a swap curve.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: swapUnwindValue_id
--     * Slot: makeWholeAmount_id Description: Amount to be paid by the buyer of the option if the option is exercised prior to the Early Call Date. (The market practice in the convertible bond option space being that the buyer should be penalised if he/she exercises the option early on.)
-- # Class: SingleValuationDate Description: A class to specify the number of business days after satisfaction of all conditions to settlement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: businessDays Description: A number of business days. Its precise meaning is dependant on the context in which this element is used. ISDA 2003 Term: Business Day.
-- # Class: SwapCurveValuation Description: A class to specify a valuation swap curve, which is used as part of the strike construct for the bond and convertible bond options.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: floatingRateIndex
--     * Slot: spread Description: Spread in basis points over the floating rate index.
--     * Slot: side Description: The side (bid/mid/ask) of the measure.
--     * Slot: indexTenor_id Description: The ISDA Designated Maturity, i.e. the tenor of the floating rate.
-- # Class: TransactedPrice Description: A class to represent the transacted price attributes that are positioned as part of the FpML FeeLeg.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: marketFixedRate Description: An optional element that only has meaning in a credit index trade. This element contains the credit spread ('fair value') at which the trade was executed. Unlike the fixedRate of an index, the marketFixedRate varies over the life of the index depending on market conditions. The marketFixedRate is the price of the index as quoted by trading desks.
--     * Slot: initialPoints Description: An optional element that contains the up-front points expressed as a percentage of the notional. An initialPoints value of 5% would be represented as 0.05. The initialPoints element is an alternative to marketFixedRate in quoting the traded level of a trade. When initialPoints is used, the traded level is the sum of fixedRate and initialPoints. The initialPoints is one of the items that are factored into the initialPayment calculation and is payable by the Buyer to the Seller. Note that initialPoints and marketFixedRate may both be present in the same document when both implied values are desired.
--     * Slot: marketPrice Description: An optional element that only has meaning in a credit index trade. This element contains the price at which the trade was executed and is used instead of marketFixedRate on credit trades on certain indicies which are quoted using a price rather than a spread.
--     * Slot: quotationStyle Description: An optional element that contains the up-front points expressed as a percentage of the notional. An initialPoints value of 5% would be represented as 0.05. The initialPoints element is an alternative to marketFixedRate in quoting the traded level of a trade. When initialPoints is used, the traded level is the sum of fixedRate and initialPoints. The initialPoints is one of the items that are factored into the initialPayment calculation and is payable by the Buyer to the Seller. Note that initialPoints and marketFixedRate may both be present in the same document when both implied values are desired.
-- # Class: ValuationDates Description: Defines how and when a performance type option or performance type swap is to be valued, including initial, interim and final valuation dates.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: initialValuationDate_id Description: Specifies the initial valuation dates of the underlyer.
--     * Slot: interimValuationDate_id Description: Specifies the interim valuation dates of the underlyer.
--     * Slot: finalValuationDate_id Description: Specifies the final valuation dates of the underlyer.
-- # Class: ValuationMethod Description: Specifies the parameters required to obtain a valuation, including the source, quotation method (bid, mid etc.) and any applicable quotation amount.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: quotationMethod Description: The type of price quotations to be requested from dealers when determining the market value of the reference obligation for purposes of cash settlement, or which rate quote is to be observed for a fixing. For example, Bid, Offer, Mid-market or Exercising Party Pays. ISDA 2003 Term: Quotation Method. The meaning of Exercising Party Pays is defined in the 2000 ISDA Definitions, Section 17.2. Certain Definitions Relating to Cash Settlement, paragraph (j).
--     * Slot: valuationMethod Description: The ISDA defined methodology for determining the final price of the reference obligation for purposes of cash settlement. (ISDA 2003 Term: Valuation Method). For example, Market, Highest etc.
--     * Slot: valuationSource_id Description: The source for obtaining a valuation. This may come from some information source (e.g. Reuters), from a rate option fixing (e.g. FX fixing for cross-currency settlement), or from a set of reference banks. This is a mandatory attribute as the valuation method relies on one of those sources to be specified.
--     * Slot: quotationAmount_id Description: In the determination of a cash settlement amount, if weighted average quotations are to be obtained, the quotation amount specifies an upper limit to the outstanding principal balance of the reference obligation for which the quote should be obtained. If not specified, the ISDA definitions provide for a fallback amount equal to the floating rate payer calculation amount. ISDA 2003 Term: Quotation Amount.
--     * Slot: minimumQuotationAmount_id Description: In the determination of a cash settlement amount, if weighted average quotations are to be obtained, the minimum quotation amount specifies a minimum intended threshold amount of outstanding principal balance of the reference obligation for which the quote should be obtained. If not specified, the ISDA definitions provide for a fallback amount of the lower of either USD 1,000,000 (or its equivalent in the relevant obligation currency) or the quotation amount. ISDA 2003 Term: Minimum Quotation Amount.
--     * Slot: cashCollateralValuationMethod_id Description: Specifies the parameters representing several mid-market valuation and replacement value methods.
-- # Class: ValuationPostponement Description: Specifies how long to wait to get a quote from a settlement rate option upon a price source disruption.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: maximumDaysOfPostponement Description: The maximum number of days to wait for a quote from the disrupted settlement rate option before proceeding to the next method.
-- # Class: ValuationSource Description: A class describing the method for obtaining a settlement rate, specified through either an information source (page), a settlement rate option (fixing) or by using quotes from reference banks.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: quotedCurrencyPair_id Description: Defines the two currencies for an FX trade and the quotation relationship between the two currencies. This attribute was formerly part of 'fxSettlementTerms', which is now being harmonised into a common 'CashSettlementTerms' that includes a 'ValuationDate'.
--     * Slot: informationSource_id Description: The information source where a published or displayed market rate will be obtained, e.g. Telerate Page 3750.
--     * Slot: settlementRateOption_id Description: The rate option to use for the fixing. Currently only applicable to foreign exchange fixing in case of cross-currency settlement.
--     * Slot: referenceBanks_id Description: A container for a set of reference institutions that may be called upon to provide rate quotations as part of the method to determine the applicable cash settlement amount. If institutions are not specified, it is assumed that reference institutions will be agreed between the parties on the exercise date, or in the case of swap transaction to which mandatory early termination is applicable, the cash settlement valuation date.
--     * Slot: dealerOrCCP_id Description: Holds an identifier for the reference entity that is agreed by both parties as a basis for cash settlement calculations. This could be a dealer from whom quotations are obtained by the calculation agent on the reference obligation for purposes of cash settlement in a credit event. ISDA 2003 Term: Dealer. This could be the clearing organization (CCP, DCO) to which the trade should be cleared, as applicable for cash-settled swaptions.
-- # Class: CalculatedRateDetails Description: Type for reporting details of calculated rates, including the observations that went into the final reported rate.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: aggregateValue Description: The total sum or product of all the individual terms that went into the calculated rate.
--     * Slot: aggregateWeight Description: The total weight of all the terms that went into the calculated rate.
--     * Slot: calculatedRate Description: The resulting calculated weight.
--     * Slot: observations_id Description: The observation dates and weights for each observation date.
-- # Class: CalculatedRateObservationDatesAndWeights Description: Type for reporting the observations dates and the corresponding weights going into a daily calculated rate
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: CalculatedRateObservations Description: Type for reporting observations that went into the final reported rate.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: FallbackRateParameters Description: Defines the structure needed to represent fallback rate parameters. This type is used to represent modular computed rates in interestRatePayouts.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: floatingRateIndex Description: The floating rate index that is used as the basis of the fallback rate.
--     * Slot: effectiveDate Description: The date the fallback rate takes effect.
--     * Slot: spreadAdjustment Description: The economic spread applied to the underlying fallback rate to replicate the original risky rate.
--     * Slot: calculationParameters_id Description: Support for modular calculated rates, such such as lockout compound calculations.
-- # Class: FloatingRateCalculationParameters Description: Defines the structures needed to represent the calculation parameters for daily averaged and compounded modular rates as defined in the 2021 ISDA Definitions in Section 7. This type is used to represent modular computed rates in interestRatePayouts.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: calculationMethod Description: calculation type (averaging or compounding).
--     * Slot: observationShiftCalculation_id Description: any obervation shift parameters if applicable.
--     * Slot: lookbackCalculation_id Description: any lookback parameters if applicable.
--     * Slot: lockoutCalculation_id Description: any lockout parameters if applicable.
--     * Slot: applicableBusinessDays_id Description: the business days that are applicable for the calculation.
--     * Slot: observationParameters_id Description: any applicable observation parameters, such as daily caps or floors.
-- # Class: ObservationParameters Description: Parameters on daily observed computed rates, specifically daily caps and floors. This type is used to represent modular computed rates in interestRatePayouts.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: observationCapRate Description: A daily observation cap rate.
--     * Slot: observationFloorRate Description: A daily observation floor rate.
-- # Class: ObservationShiftCalculation Description: Parameters to describe the observation shift for a daily compounded or averaged floating rate. This type is used to represent modular computed rates in interestRatePayouts.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: offsetDays Description: The number of days of observation shift.
--     * Slot: calculationBase Description: Whether the rate is calculated in advance, in arrears, or relative to a reset date.
--     * Slot: additionalBusinessDays_id Description: Any additional business days that be applicable.
-- # Class: OffsetCalculation Description: Defines business day shifts for daily componded or averaged rates. This type is used for lookback and lockout rates. This type is used to represent modular computed rates in interestRatePayouts.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: offsetDays Description: The number of business days offset.
-- # Class: BusinessDayOffset Description: This allows an offset to be specified as, for instance, N business days, with a business centers specified as included.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: fixingOffsetDefinition Description: Legal text that underlies the Fixing Offset. ISDA Fixing Offset Definition. (e.g. One day that is either a Sydney Business Day or a Melbourne Business Day following the Reset Date)
--     * Slot: fixingOffsetReason Description: Fixing Offset Reason
--     * Slot: periodMultiplier Description: A time period multiplier, e.g. 1, 2 or 3 etc. A negative value can be used when specifying an offset relative to another date, e.g. -2 days.
--     * Slot: period Description: A time period, e.g. a day, week, month or year of the stream. If the periodMultiplier value is 0 (zero) then period must contain the value D (day).
--     * Slot: businessCenters_id Description: The business centers for the offset.
-- # Class: ContractualDefinition
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: publicationDate Description: 2021-06-11
--     * Slot: identifier_id Description: Corresponds to the unique identifier of the Contractual Definition in which the code is published
--     * Slot: contractualDefinitionIdentifier_id Description: Contractual Definition Identifier in which the code is published. Includes Document Type and Document Version
-- # Class: ContractualDefinitionIdentifier
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: contractualDefinitionType Description: e.g. ISDA2021Definitions
--     * Slot: contractualDefinitionVersion Description: e.g. V1
-- # Class: FloatingRateIndexCalculationDefaults Description: This holds the rate calculation defaults applicable for a floating rate index.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: category Description: The ISDA FRO category (e.g. screen rate or calculated rate).
--     * Slot: indexStyle Description: The ISDA FRO style (e.g. term rate, swap rate, etc).
--     * Slot: method Description: The ISDA FRO calculation method (e.g. OIS Compounding).
--     * Slot: dayCountFraction Description: The default day count fraction.
--     * Slot: publicationCalendar Description: Publication Calendar (e.g. EUR-ICESWAP)
--     * Slot: applicableBusinessDays_id Description: The default applicable business days.
-- # Class: FloatingRateIndexDefinition
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: definitionalSource Description: The source of an FRO, particularly if not a Contractual Definition (e.g. the broker rates matrix).
--     * Slot: designatedMaturityApplicable
--     * Slot: inLoan Description: YES / NO to flag FROs identified by the FpML Syndicated Loan WG as having underlying benchmark that may also be referenced in syndicated loans.
--     * Slot: deprecationReason Description: Deprecation and Code Descriptions
--     * Slot: fpmlDescription Description: FpML Description
--     * Slot: fro_id Description: The underlying FRO name and designated maturity.
--     * Slot: calculationDefaults_id Description: Any calculation default values.
--     * Slot: mappings_id Description: Any mappings to other FRos.
--     * Slot: externalMappings_id Description: Any mappings to other codes for this index.
--     * Slot: history_id Description: FRO History
--     * Slot: rounding_id Description: The rounding rules applicable to the floating rate index in case of a calculation.
-- # Class: FloatingRateIndexExternalMap Description: A map for a single FRO to or from an equivalent or similar codes in a different standard such as ISO.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: externalId Description: The FRO name that is being mapped to/from.
--     * Slot: externalStandard Description: The standard/version to which the map applies.
-- # Class: FloatingRateIndexExternalMappings Description: Represents the mappings of FRO codes to other.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isoCode_id
-- # Class: FloatingRateIndexFixingDetails Description: This type holds parameters defining the fixingt time and offset for a floating rate index.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: fixingTime_id Description: Parameters defining the normal fixing time (can vary by index tenor / designated maturity).
--     * Slot: fixingOffset_id Description: Parameters defining the normal fixing offset (can vary by index tenor / designated maturity).
-- # Class: FloatingRateIndexFixingOffset Description: This type holds parameters defining the normal fixing offset for a floating rate index.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: designatedMaturity Description: Allows a reason to be specified for using the alternative fixing offset.
--     * Slot: fixingOffsetDefinition Description: Legal text that underlies the Fixing Offset. ISDA Fixing Offset Definition. (e.g. One day that is either a Sydney Business Day or a Melbourne Business Day following the Reset Date)
--     * Slot: fixingOffsetReason Description: Fixing Offset Reason
--     * Slot: periodMultiplier Description: A time period multiplier, e.g. 1, 2 or 3 etc. A negative value can be used when specifying an offset relative to another date, e.g. -2 days.
--     * Slot: period Description: A time period, e.g. a day, week, month or year of the stream. If the periodMultiplier value is 0 (zero) then period must contain the value D (day).
--     * Slot: businessCenters_id Description: The business centers for the offset.
-- # Class: FloatingRateIndexFixingTime Description: This type holds parameters defining the normal fixing time for a floating rate index.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: designatedMaturity Description: Allows a designed maturity to be specified for the fixing time.
--     * Slot: fixingTimeDefinition Description: Legal text that underlies the Fixing Time. ISDA Fixing Time Definition. (e.g. 09:30, Sydney time).
--     * Slot: fixingReason Description: Fixing Reason
--     * Slot: hourMinuteTime Description: A time specified in hh:mm:ss format where the second component must be '00', e.g. 11am would be represented as 11:00:00.
--     * Slot: businessCenter Description: A code identifying a business day calendar location. A business day calendar location is drawn from the list identified by the business day calendar location enumeration.
-- # Class: FloatingRateIndexIdentification
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: floatingRateIndex Description: The reference index that is used to specify the floating interest rate. The FpML standard maintains the list of such indices, which are positioned as enumeration values as part of the CDM.
--     * Slot: currency Description: FRO currency - 3 character ISO currrency code
--     * Slot: froType Description: FRO type (e.g. OIS)
-- # Class: FloatingRateIndexMap Description: A map for a single FRO to or from an equivalent or similar FRO in a different contractual definitions version.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: contractualDefinitionIdentifier_id Description: Contractual Definition to which the map applies. Includes Document Type and Document Version
--     * Slot: identifier_id Description: Corresponds to the unique identifier of the Contractual Definition to which the map applies
-- # Class: FloatingRateIndexMappings Description: This type defines mappings between FROs in different definitional versions.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: mapsTo_id Description: The successor FRO that this index maps to.
-- # Class: FroHistory Description: FRO History
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: startDate Description: The date the Floating Rate Option was added to the 2006 Definitions or 2021 Floating Rate Matrix. (e.g. 2017/04/06)
--     * Slot: endDate Description: The date the Floating Rate Option was removed from the 2006 Definitions or 2021 Floating Rate Matrix. (e.g. 2014/01/01)
--     * Slot: updateDate Description: The date the Floating Rate Option was last updated in the 2006 Definitions or 2021 Floating Rate Matrix. (e.g. 2021/06/11)
--     * Slot: firstDefinedIn_id Description: The supplement or version the FRO was first added to the 2006 Definitions or 2021 Floating Rate Matrix. (e.g. S52)
--     * Slot: lastUpdatedIn_id Description: The supplement or version the FRO was last updated in the 2006 Definitions or 2021 Floating Rate Matrix. (e.g. FRO-M-V1)
-- # Class: AmountScheduleWithInitialValue Description: A class to specify a currency amount or a currency amount schedule.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: value Description: The initial rate or amount must be specified, as the case may be. An initial rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
-- # Class: AveragingObservationList Description: An unordered list of weighted averaging observations.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: AveragingPeriod Description: Period over which an average value is taken.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: marketDisruption Description: The market disruption event as defined by ISDA 2002 Definitions.
--     * Slot: averagingDateTimes_id Description: An unweighted list of averaging observation date and times.
--     * Slot: averagingObservations_id Description: A weighted list of averaging observation date and times.
-- # Class: CalculationPeriod Description: A data defining: the parameters used in the calculation of a fixed or floating rate calculation period amount. This data forms: part of cashflows representation of a swap stream.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: unadjustedStartDate Description: The calculation start date, unadjusted.
--     * Slot: unadjustedEndDate Description: The calculation end date, unadjusted.
--     * Slot: calculationPeriodNumberOfDays Description: The number of days from the adjusted effective / start date to the adjusted termination / end date calculated in accordance with the applicable day count fraction.
--     * Slot: notionalAmount Description: The amount that a cashflow will accrue interest on.
--     * Slot: fixedRate Description: The calculation period fixed rate. A per annum rate, expressed as a decimal. A fixed rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
--     * Slot: dayCountYearFraction Description: The year fraction value of the calculation period, result of applying the ISDA rules for day count fraction defined in the ISDA Annex.
--     * Slot: forecastRate Description: A value representing the forecast rate used to calculate the forecast future value of the accrual period. This is a calculated rate determined based on averaging the rates in the rateObservation elements, and incorporates all of the rate treatment and averaging rules. A value of 1% should be represented as 0.01.
--     * Slot: adjustedStartDate Description: The calculation period start date, adjusted according to any relevant business day convention.
--     * Slot: adjustedEndDate Description: The calculation period end date, adjusted according to any relevant business day convention.
--     * Slot: fxLinkedNotionalAmount_id Description: The amount that a cashflow will accrue interest on. This is the calculated amount of the FX linked - i.e. the other currency notional amount multiplied by the appropriate FX spot rate.
--     * Slot: floatingRateDefinition_id Description: The floating rate reset information for the calculation period.
--     * Slot: forecastAmount_id Description: The amount representing the forecast of the accrued value of the calculation period. An intermediate value used to generate the forecastPaymentAmount in the PaymentCalculationPeriod.
-- # Class: CalculationPeriodBase Description: The calculation period adjusted start and end dates, which are the baseline arguments needed to compute an interest accrual calculation.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: adjustedStartDate Description: The calculation period start date, adjusted according to any relevant business day convention.
--     * Slot: adjustedEndDate Description: The calculation period end date, adjusted according to any relevant business day convention.
-- # Class: CalculationPeriodData
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: startDate Description: The CDM's startDate attribute; each class's slot_usage gives its meaning.
--     * Slot: endDate Description: The CDM's endDate attribute; each class's slot_usage gives its meaning.
--     * Slot: daysInPeriod
--     * Slot: daysInLeapYearPeriod
--     * Slot: isFirstPeriod
--     * Slot: isLastPeriod
-- # Class: CalculationPeriodDates Description: A data for: defining the parameters used to generate the calculation period dates schedule, including the specification of any initial or final stub calculation periods. A calculation period schedule consists of an optional initial stub calculation period, one or more regular calculation periods and an optional final stub calculation period. In the absence of any initial or final stub calculation periods, the regular part of the calculation period schedule is assumed to be between the effective date and the termination date. No implicit stubs are allowed, i.e. stubs must be explicitly specified using an appropriate combination of firstPeriodStartDate, firstRegularPeriodStartDate and lastRegularPeriodEndDate.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: firstRegularPeriodStartDate Description: The start date of the regular part of the calculation period schedule. It must only be specified if there is an initial stub calculation period. This day may be subject to adjustment in accordance with any adjustments specified in calculationPeriodDatesAdjustments.
--     * Slot: firstCompoundingPeriodEndDate Description: The end date of the initial compounding period when compounding is applicable. It must only be specified when the compoundingMethod element is present and not equal to a value of None. This date may be subject to adjustment in accordance with any adjustments specified in calculationPeriodDatesAdjustments.
--     * Slot: lastRegularPeriodEndDate Description: The end date of the regular part of the calculation period schedule. It must only be specified if there is a final stub calculation period. This day may be subject to adjustment in accordance with any adjustments specified in calculationPeriodDatesAdjustments.
--     * Slot: effectiveDate_id Description: The first day of the terms of the trade. This day may be subject to adjustment in accordance with a business day convention.
--     * Slot: terminationDate_id Description: The last day of the terms of the trade. This date may be subject to adjustments in accordance with the business day convention. It can also be specified in relation to another scheduled date (e.g. the last payment date).
--     * Slot: calculationPeriodDatesAdjustments_id Description: The specification of the business day convention and financial business centers used for adjusting any calculation period date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day in the specified business center.
--     * Slot: firstPeriodStartDate_id Description: The start date of the calculation period. FpML specifies that for interest rate swaps this date must only be specified if it is not equal to the effective date. It is always specified in the case of equity swaps and credit default swaps with periodic payments. This date may be subject to adjustment in accordance with a business day convention.
--     * Slot: calculationPeriodFrequency_id Description: The frequency at which calculation period end dates occur with the regular part of the calculation period schedule and their roll date convention.
-- # Class: DateRelativeToCalculationPeriodDates Description: A data to: provide the ability to point to multiple payment nodes in the document through the unbounded paymentDatesReference.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: DateRelativeToPaymentDates Description: A data to: provide the ability to point to multiple payment nodes in the document through the unbounded paymentDatesReference.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: DateRelativeToValuationDates Description: A data to: provide the ability to point to multiple payment nodes in the document through the unbounded paymentDatesReference.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: FinalCalculationPeriodDateAdjustment Description: A data to: define business date convention adjustment to final payment period per leg.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: businessDayConvention Description: Override business date convention. This takes precedence over leg level information.
--     * Slot: relevantUnderlyingDateReference_id Description: Reference to the unadjusted cancellation effective dates.
--     * Slot: swapStreamReference_id Description: Reference to the leg, where date adjustments may apply.
-- # Class: FxLinkedNotionalAmount Description: A data to: describe the cashflow representation for FX linked notionals.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: resetDate Description: The reset date.
--     * Slot: adjustedFxSpotFixingDate Description: The date on which the FX spot rate is observed. This date should already be adjusted for any applicable business day convention.
--     * Slot: observedFxSpotRate Description: The actual observed FX spot rate.
--     * Slot: notionalAmount Description: The calculation period notional amount.
-- # Class: FxLinkedNotionalSchedule Description: A data to: describe a notional schedule where each notional that applies to a calculation period is calculated with reference to a notional amount or notional amount schedule in a different currency by means of a spot currency exchange rate which is normally observed at the beginning of each period.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: varyingNotionalCurrency Description: The currency of the varying notional amount, i.e. the notional amount being determined periodically based on observation of a spot currency exchange rate. The list of valid currencies is not presently positioned as an enumeration as part of the CDM because that scope is limited to the values specified by ISDA and FpML. As a result, implementers have to make reference to the relevant standard, such as the ISO 4217 standard for currency codes.
--     * Slot: varyingNotionalFixingDates_id Description: The dates on which spot currency exchange rates are observed for purposes of determining the varying notional currency amount that will apply to a calculation period.
--     * Slot: fxSpotRateSource_id Description: The information source and time at which the spot currency exchange rate will be observed.
--     * Slot: fixingTime_id Description: The time at which the spot currency exchange rate will be observed. It is specified as a time in a business day calendar location, e.g. 11:00am London time.
--     * Slot: varyingNotionalInterimExchangePaymentDates_id Description: The dates on which interim exchanges of notional are paid. Interim exchanges will arise as a result of changes in the spot currency exchange amount or changes in the constant notional schedule (e.g. amortisation).
-- # Class: InitialFixingDate Description: A CDM class which purpose is to specify the initial fixing date either alongside the FpML interest rate specification as an offset of another date, or alongside the credit derivative specification as an unadjusted date.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: initialFixingDate
--     * Slot: relativeDateOffset_id
-- # Class: Lag Description: The pricing period per calculation period if the pricing days do not wholly fall within the respective calculation period.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: lagDuration_id Description: Defines the offset of the series of pricing dates relative to the calculation period.
--     * Slot: firstObservationDateOffset_id Description: Defines the offset of the series of pricing dates relative to the calculation period.
-- # Class: ObservationDate Description: Specifies a single date on which market observations take place and specifies optional associated weighting.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: unadjustedDate Description: A date subject to adjustment.
--     * Slot: adjustedDate Description: The date once the adjustment has been performed. (Note that this date may change if the business center holidays change).
--     * Slot: weight Description: Specifies the degree of importance of the observation.
--     * Slot: observationReference Description: Specifies an identification key for the market observation. This attribute can be used as a reference to assign weights to a series of dates defined in a parametricSchedule.
-- # Class: ObservationDates Description: Describes date details for a set of observation dates in parametric or non-parametric form.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: observationSchedule_id Description: Specifies a schedule of dates (non-parametric) on which market observations take place, and allows for the optional definition of weights where applicable. When no weight is specified, then weight of each date is assumed to be 1.0
--     * Slot: periodicSchedule_id Description: Specifies the date range and frequency on which market observations take place. Weights can be assigned to dates in the schedule by assigning the weight and corresponding observationReference in the observationSchedule.
--     * Slot: parametricDates_id Description: Specifies parametric terms to determine which days within a given calculation period the price would be observed. Typically associated with Commodities.
-- # Class: ObservationSchedule Description: Specifies a single date on which market observations take place and specifies optional associated weighting.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: dateAdjustments_id Description: The business day convention and financial business centers used for adjusting the date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business date in the specified business centers.
-- # Class: ObservationTerms Description: Class containing terms that are associated with observing a price/benchmark/index across either single or multiple observations.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: observationTimeType Description: The enumerated values to specify points in the day when option exercise and valuation can occur.
--     * Slot: numberOfObservationDates Description: The number of observation dates between observation start date and observation end date.
--     * Slot: observationTime_id Description: Defines time in respect to a business calendar location that the price/benchmark/index is observed
--     * Slot: informationSource_id Description: The information source where a published or displayed market rate will be obtained, e.g. Telerate Page 3750.
--     * Slot: precision_id Description: Defines rounding rules and precision to be used in the rounding of observations.
--     * Slot: calculationPeriodDates_id Description: Defines parameters used to generate the calculation period dates schedule, including the specification of any initial or final stub calculation periods. A calculation period schedule consists of an optional initial stub calculation period, one or more regular calculation periods and an optional final stub calculation period. In the absence of any initial or final stub calculation periods, the regular part of the calculation period schedule is assumed to be between the effective date and the termination date. No implicit stubs are allowed, i.e. stubs must be explicitly specified using an appropriate combination of firstPeriodStartDate, firstRegularPeriodStartDate and lastRegularPeriodEndDate.
--     * Slot: observationDates_id Description: Describes date details for a set of observation dates in parametric or non-parametric form.
-- # Class: ParametricDates Description: Defines rules for the dates on which the price will be determined.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: dayType Description: Denotes the enumerated values to specify the day type classification used in counting the number of days between two dates.
--     * Slot: dayDistribution Description: Denotes the method by which the pricing days are distributed across the pricing period.
--     * Slot: dayFrequency Description: Defines the occurrence of the dayOfWeek within the pricing period on which pricing will take place, e.g. the 3rd Friday within each Calculation Period. If omitted, every dayOfWeek will be a pricing day.
--     * Slot: lag_id Description: The pricing period per calculation period if the pricing days do not wholly fall within the respective calculation period.
--     * Slot: businessCenters_id Description: The enumerated values to specify the business centers.
-- # Class: PaymentCalculationPeriod Description: A data defining: the adjusted payment date and associated calculation period parameters required to calculate the actual or projected payment amount. This data forms: part of the cashflow representation of a swap stream.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: unadjustedPaymentDate Description: The unadjusted payment date.
--     * Slot: adjustedPaymentDate Description: The adjusted payment date. This date should already be adjusted for any applicable business day convention. This component is not intended for use in trade confirmation but may be specified to allow the fee structure to also serve as a cashflow type component.
--     * Slot: discountFactor Description: A decimal value representing the discount factor used to calculate the present value of cash flow.
--     * Slot: fixedPaymentAmount_id Description: A known fixed payment amount.
--     * Slot: forecastPaymentAmount_id Description: A monetary amount representing the forecast of the future value of the payment.
--     * Slot: presentValueAmount_id Description: A monetary amount representing the present value of the forecast payment.
-- # Class: PaymentDateSchedule Description: The payment dates when specified as relative to a set of dates specified somewhere else in the instance document/transaction, e.g. the valuation dates as typically the case for equity swaps, or when specified as a calculation period schedule.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: finalPaymentDate_id Description: The last payment when specified as an adjustable or relative date, as in the FpML total return construct.
-- # Class: PaymentDates Description: Specifies the parameters to generate the payment date schedule, either through a parametric representation or by reference to specified dates.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: firstPaymentDate Description: The first unadjusted payment date. This day may be subject to adjustment in accordance with any business day convention specified in paymentDatesAdjustments. This element must only be included if there is an initial stub. This date will normally correspond to an unadjusted calculation period start or end date. This is true even if early or delayed payment is specified to be applicable since the actual first payment date will be the specified number of days before or after the applicable adjusted calculation period start or end date with the resulting payment date then being adjusted in accordance with any business day convention specified in paymentDatesAdjustments.
--     * Slot: lastRegularPaymentDate Description: The last regular payment date when specified as a date, as in the FpML interest rate construct. FpML specifies that this date may be subject to adjustment in accordance with any business day convention specified in the paymentDatesAdjustments attribute.
--     * Slot: payRelativeTo Description: Specifies whether the payments occur relative to each adjusted calculation period start date or end date, each reset date, valuation date or the last pricing date. Calculation period start date means relative to the start of the first calculation period contributing to a given payment. Similarly, calculation period end date means the end of the last calculation period contributing to a given payment. The valuation date is applicable for Brazilian-CDI and equity swaps.
--     * Slot: paymentFrequency_id Description: The frequency at which regular payment dates occur. If the payment frequency is equal to the frequency defined in the calculation period dates component then one calculation period contributes to each payment amount. If the payment frequency is less frequent than the frequency defined in the calculation period dates component then more than one calculation period will contribute to the payment amount. A payment frequency more frequent than the calculation period frequency or one that is not a multiple of the calculation period frequency is invalid. If the payment frequency is of value T (term), the period is defined by the effectiveDate and the terminationDate.
--     * Slot: paymentDateSchedule_id Description: The payment dates when specified as relative to a set of dates specified somewhere else in the instance document/transaction, e.g. the valuation dates as typically the case for equity swaps, or when specified as a calculation period schedule.
--     * Slot: paymentDaysOffset_id Description: If early payment or delayed payment is required, specifies the number of days offset that the payment occurs relative to what would otherwise be the unadjusted payment date. The offset can be specified in terms of either calendar or business days. Even in the case of a calendar days offset, the resulting payment date, adjusted for the specified calendar days offset, will still be adjusted in accordance with the specified payment dates adjustments. This element should only be included if early or delayed payment is applicable, i.e. if the periodMultiplier element value is not equal to zero. An early payment would be indicated by a negative periodMultiplier element value and a delayed payment (or payment lag) would be indicated by a positive periodMultiplier element value.
--     * Slot: paymentDatesAdjustments_id Description: The definition of the business day convention and financial business centers used for adjusting the payment date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day in the specified business center.
-- # Class: RateSchedule Description: A class defining a schedule of rates or amounts in terms of an initial value and then a series of step date and value pairs. On each step date the rate or amount changes to the new step value. The series of step date and value pairs are optional. If not specified, this implies that the initial value remains unchanged over time.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: price_id Description: The initial rate. An initial rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05.
-- # Class: ResetDates Description: A data defining: the parameters used to generate the reset dates schedule and associated fixing dates. The reset dates are the dates on which the new index value (which is observed on the fixing date) is applied for each period and on which the interest rate hence begins to accrue.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: resetRelativeTo Description: Specifies whether the reset dates are determined with respect to each adjusted calculation period start date or adjusted calculation period end date. If the reset frequency is specified as daily this element must not be included.
--     * Slot: calculationPeriodDatesReference_id Description: A pointer style reference to the associated calculation period dates component defined elsewhere in the document.
--     * Slot: initialFixingDate_id Description: The initial fixing date.
--     * Slot: fixingDates_id Description: The fixing dates are the dates on which the index values are observed. The fixing dates are specified by reference to the reset date through business days offset and an associated set of financial business centers. Normally these offset calculation rules will be those specified in the ISDA definition for the relevant floating rate index (ISDA's Floating Rate Option). However, non-standard offset calculation rules may apply for a trade if mutually agreed by the principal parties to the transaction.
--     * Slot: finalFixingDate_id Description: This attribute is not part of the FpML ResetDate, and has been added as part of the CDM to support the credit derivatives final fixing date.
--     * Slot: rateCutOffDaysOffset_id Description: Specifies the number of business days before the period end date when the rate cut-off date is assumed to apply. The financial business centers associated with determining the rate cut-off date are those specified in the reset dates adjustments. The rate cut-off number of days must be a negative integer (a value of zero would imply no rate cut off applies in which case the rateCutOffDaysOffset element should not be included). The relevant rate for each reset date in the period from, and including, a rate cut-off date to, but excluding, the next applicable period end date (or, in the case of the last calculation period, the termination date) will (solely for purposes of calculating the floating amount payable on the next applicable payment date) be deemed to be the relevant rate in effect on that rate cut-off date. For example, if rate cut-off days for a daily averaging deal is -2 business days, then the refix rate applied on (period end date - 2 days) will also be applied as the reset on (period end date - 1 day), i.e. the actual number of reset dates remains the same but from the rate cut-off date until the period end date, the same refix rate is applied. Note that in the case of several calculation periods contributing to a single payment, the rate cut-off is assumed only to apply to the final calculation period contributing to that payment. The day type associated with the offset must imply a business days offset.
--     * Slot: resetFrequency_id Description: The frequency at which the reset dates occur. In the case of a weekly reset frequency, also specifies the day of the week that the reset occurs. If the reset frequency is greater than the calculation period frequency then this implies that more than one reset is established for each calculation period and some form of rate averaging is applicable.
--     * Slot: resetDatesAdjustments_id Description: The definition of the business day convention and financial business centers used for adjusting the reset date if it would otherwise fall on a day that is not a business day in the specified business center.
-- # Class: ResetFrequency Description: A class defining the reset frequency. In the case of a weekly reset, also specifies the day of the week that the reset occurs. If the reset frequency is greater than the calculation period frequency the this implies that more or more reset dates is established for each calculation period and some form of rate averaging is applicable. The specific averaging method of calculation is specified in FloatingRateCalculation. In case the reset frequency is of value T (term), the period is defined by the swap/swapStream/calculationPerioDates/effectiveDate and the swap/swapStream/calculationPerioDates/terminationDate.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: weeklyRollConvention Description: The day of the week on which a weekly reset date occurs. This element must be included if the reset frequency is defined as weekly and not otherwise.
--     * Slot: periodMultiplier Description: A time period multiplier, e.g. 1, 2, or 3. If the period value is T (Term) then period multiplier must contain the value 1.
--     * Slot: period Description: A time period, e.g. a day, week, month, year or term of the stream.
-- # Class: StubCalculationPeriodAmount Description: A data defining: how the initial or final stub calculation period amounts is calculated. For example, the rate to be applied to the initial or final stub calculation period may be the linear interpolation of two different tenors for the floating rate index specified in the calculation period amount component, e.g. A two month stub period may used the linear interpolation of a one month and three month floating rate. The different rate tenors would be specified in this component. Note that a maximum of two rate tenors can be specified. If a stub period uses a single index tenor and this is the same as that specified in the calculation period amount component then the initial stub or final stub component, as the case may be, must not be included.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: calculationPeriodDatesReference_id Description: A pointer style reference to the associated calculation period dates component defined elsewhere in the document.
--     * Slot: initialStub_id Description: Specifies how the initial stub amount is calculated. A single floating rate tenor different to that used for the regular part of the calculation periods schedule may be specified, or two floating tenors may be specified. If two floating rate tenors are specified then Linear Interpolation (in accordance with the 2000 ISDA Definitions, Section 8.3. Interpolation) is assumed to apply. Alternatively, an actual known stub rate or stub amount may be specified.
--     * Slot: finalStub_id Description: Specifies how the final stub amount is calculated. A single floating rate tenor different to that used for the regular part of the calculation periods schedule may be specified, or two floating tenors may be specified. If two floating rate tenors are specified then Linear Interpolation (in accordance with the 2000 ISDA Definitions, Section 8.3. Interpolation) is assumed to apply. Alternatively, an actual known stub rate or stub amount may be specified.
-- # Class: StubPeriod Description: A class defining how the initial or final stub calculation period amounts is calculated. For example, the rate to be applied to the initial or final stub calculation period may be the linear interpolation of two different tenors for the floating rate index specified in the calculation period amount component, e.g. A two month stub period may used the linear interpolation of a one month and three month floating rate. The different rate tenors would be specified in this component. Note that a maximum of two rate tenors can be specified. If a stub period uses a single index tenor and this is the same as that specified in the calculation period amount component then the initial stub or final stub component, as the case may be, must not be included.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: calculationPeriodDatesReference_id Description: A pointer style reference to the associated calculation period dates component defined elsewhere in the document.
--     * Slot: initialStub_id Description: Specifies how the initial stub amount is calculated. A single floating rate tenor different to that used for the regular part of the calculation periods schedule may be specified, or two floating tenors may be specified. If two floating rate tenors are specified then Linear Interpolation (in accordance with the 2000 ISDA Definitions, Section 8.3. Interpolation) is assumed to apply. Alternatively, an actual known stub rate or stub amount may be specified.
--     * Slot: finalStub_id Description: Specifies how the final stub amount is calculated. A single floating rate tenor different to that used for the regular part of the calculation periods schedule may be specified, or two floating tenors may be specified. If two floating rate tenors are specified then Linear Interpolation (in accordance with the 2000 ISDA Definitions, Section 8.3. Interpolation) is assumed to apply. Alternatively, an actual known stub rate or stub amount may be specified.
-- # Class: WeightedAveragingObservation Description: A single weighted averaging observation.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: dateTime Description: Observation date time, which should be used when literal observation dates are required. The CDM specifies that the zoned date time is to be expressed in accordance with ISO 8601, either as UTC as an offset to UTC.
--     * Slot: observationNumber Description: Observation number, which should be unique, within a series generated by a date schedule.
--     * Slot: weight Description: Observation weight, which is used as a multiplier for the observation value.
-- # Class: AdjustDateInstruction Description: Instruction that holds the adjusted date.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: adjustedDate
-- # Class: AdjustObservationDatesInstruction Description: Instruction that holds the adjusted observation dates.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: AdjustPeriodInstruction Description: Instruction that holds the adjusted period.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: adjustedPeriod_id
-- # Class: CalculateResetValueInstruction Description: Instruction storing the computed reset value and the calculation method used to derive it.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: calculationMethod
--     * Slot: resetValue_id
-- # Class: CollectFloatingRateOptionInstruction Description: Instruction that identifies the floating rate index and the trade date required for downstream Floating Rate Option Data retrieval.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: floatingRateIndex
--     * Slot: tradeDate
-- # Class: DetermineUnadjustedCalculationPeriodInstruction Description: Instruction that contains the unadjusted calculation period.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: unadjustedResetDate
--     * Slot: unadjustedCalculationPeriod_id
-- # Class: DetermineUnadjustedObservationDatesInstruction Description: Instruction that holds the unadjusted observation dates.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: floatingRateIndexData_id
-- # Class: ResetInstructionState Description: The definitive state object for the Reset process. It acts as a cumulative 'Golden Record,' storing every data point captured from Step 1 (Index Collection) through Step 7 (Final Calculation) to ensure deterministic processing.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: floatingRateIndex Description: The benchmark rate index (e.g., LIBOR, EURIBOR, SOFR) identified for this reset.
--     * Slot: tradeDate Description: The date the underlying trade was executed, used for referencing the relevant holiday calendars.
--     * Slot: unadjustedResetDate Description: The theoretical reset date before applying business day conventions.
--     * Slot: adjustedResetDate Description: The final, legally binding reset date after applying business day conventions.
--     * Slot: calculationMethod Description: The specific compounding or averaging formula used to arrive at the final reset value.
--     * Slot: unadjustedCalculationPeriod_id Description: The raw start and end dates of the period before any business day adjustments are applied.
--     * Slot: adjustedCalculationPeriod_id Description: The calculation period after adjusting for non-business days and relevant financial calendars.
--     * Slot: floatingRateOptionData_id Description: The specific day count fraction, fixings, and lookback parameters associated with the chosen index.
--     * Slot: resetValue_id Description: The final calculated rate or price derived from the observed market data.
-- # Class: ResetInstructionSteps Description: A wrapper that encapsulates the specific ResetInstructionCompositionStepsEnum, allowing the engine to identify the exact phase of the Reset lifecycle currently being processed.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: resetInstructionCompositionSteps
-- # Class: CompositionState Description: A container that holds the cumulative state of an Instruction Composition. It selects the specific history/state schema (e.g., ResetInstructionState) based on the lifecycle process being executed.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: ResetInstructionState_id
-- # Class: CompositionStep Description: Represents a single atomic step in the Instruction Composition lifecycle, including its instructions, status, and optional output. Each CompositionStep is defined by an identifier, a timestamp and a single Instruction.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: timestamp Description: Date and time of the execution of the Instruction Composition step after being executed.
--     * Slot: identifier Description: Identification of the Instruction Composition step.
--     * Slot: compositionStepInstruction_id Description: Set of instructions defining the steps of each Instruction Composition process.
-- # Class: CompositionStepInstruction Description: Set of instructions defining the steps of each Instruction Composition process. The CompositionStepInstruction is defined by a type (as the same instruction can be reused across different Instruction Composition types), and the selection of one of the list of CompositionStepInstructions (where the information for executing the step is held).
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: instructionCompositionType Description: Definition of the Instruction Composition.
--     * Slot: compositionStepInstructions_id Description: List of all Instruction CompositionSteps that can be reusable across Instruction Compositions.
-- # Class: CompositionStepInstructions Description: Container for all instruction steps that can be used within an InstructionComposition.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: collectFloatingRateOption_id Description: Data needed to execute the extraction of the Floating Rate Option index name.
--     * Slot: determineUnadjustedCalculationPeriod_id Description: Data needed to determine the Unadjusted Calculation Period.
--     * Slot: adjustPeriod_id Description: Data needed to adjust the Calculation Period.
--     * Slot: adjustDate_id Description: Data needed to adjust the Reset Date.
--     * Slot: determineUnadjustedObservationDates_id Description: Data needed to determine the Unadjusted Observation Dates.
--     * Slot: adjustObservationDates_id Description: Data needed to adjust the Observation Dates.
--     * Slot: calculateResetValue_id Description: Data needed to calculate the Reset Value.
--     * Slot: resetInstruction_id Description: Data needed to record the Reset Instruction.
-- # Class: InstructionComposition Description: Represents an Instruction Composition orchestration, holding data, shared history, and an ordered sequence of CompositionSteps. Each InstructionComposition will have one or more CompositionStps.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: instructionCompositionType Description: Type of Instruction Composition being orchestrated (e.g. ResetInstruction).
--     * Slot: identifier Description: Unique identifier of this InstructionComposition instance.
--     * Slot: compositionState_id Description: Shared state accumulated across executed steps, capturing intermediate and final outputs of the Instruction Composition process.
--     * Slot: tradeId_id Description: Identifier of the underlying trade to which this InstructionComposition relates.
--     * Slot: instructionCompositionOutput_id Description: Outputs of each Instruction Composition process. The recording of this information will be done in a single step at the end of the process for each Instruction Composition.
-- # Class: InstructionCompositionOutput Description: Records the relevant output of each Instruction Composition. Will be updated while executing the relevant steps of the Instruction Composition so at the end of the process the output should be completed and ready to use in other parts of the system.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: resetInstruction_id Description: Defines the reset value or fixing value produced in cashflow calculations, during the life-cycle of a financial instrument. The reset process defined in Create_Reset function joins product definition details with observations to compute the reset value.
-- # Class: InstructionCompositionSteps Description: A top-level routing object used to specify which process-specific instruction set is currently active within the execution engine.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: ResetInstructionSteps_id
-- # Class: Agreement Description: Specification of the standard set of terms that define a legal agreement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: creditSupportAgreementElections_id Description: Elections to specify a Credit Support Annex or Credit Support Deed for Intial or Variation Margin.
--     * Slot: collateralTransferAgreementElections_id Description: Elections to specify a Collateral Transfer Agreement.
--     * Slot: securityAgreementElections_id Description: Elections to specify a Security agreement.
--     * Slot: clauseLibrarySchedule_id Description: Elections specified through a Clause Library.
--     * Slot: transactionAdditionalTerms_id Description: Any additional terms which mainly intend to specify the extraordinary events that may affect a trade and the related contractual rights and obligation of the parties when this happens
--     * Slot: masterAgreementElections_id Description: A legal representation of the different possible master agreements
-- # Class: AgreementName Description: Specifies the agreement name through an agreement type and optional detailed sub agreement type.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: agreementType Description: Specification of the legal agreement type.
--     * Slot: creditSupportAgreementType Description: Specification of the credit support agreement type.
--     * Slot: creditSupportAgreementMarginType Description: specifies the type of margin for which a legal agreement is named.
--     * Slot: masterAgreementType Description: Specification of the master agreement type.
--     * Slot: masterConfirmationType Description: The type of master confirmation executed between the parties.
--     * Slot: masterConfirmationAnnexType Description: The type of master confirmation annex executed between the parties.
--     * Slot: otherAgreement Description: Definition of an agreement that is not enumerated in the CDM.
--     * Slot: brokerConfirmationType
-- # Class: AgreementTerms Description: Specification of the content of a legal agreement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: clauseLibrary Description: Specification of whether the agreement terms have been negotiated using the clause library methodology.
--     * Slot: agreement_id Description: Specification of the standard set of terms that define a legal agreement.
-- # Class: ContactInformationElection Description: Specifies the party reference and the associated contact information.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: partyReference Description: The party to which the election and details apply.
--     * Slot: primaryContactInformation_id Description: The main notice/address information of the party.
-- # Class: ContractualMatrix
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: matrixType Description: Identifies the form of applicable matrix.
--     * Slot: matrixTerm Description: Defines any applicable key into the relevant matrix. For example, the Transaction Type would be the single term required for the Credit Derivatives Physical Settlement Matrix. This element should be omitted in the case of the 2000 ISDA Definitions Settlement Matrix for Early Termination and Swaptions.
-- # Class: ContractualTermsSupplement Description: A contractual supplement (such as those published by ISDA) and its publication date that will apply to the trade.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: contractualTermsSupplementType Description: Identifies the form of applicable contractual supplement.
--     * Slot: publicationDate Description: Specifies the publication date of the applicable version of the contractual supplement.
-- # Class: LegalAgreement Description: The specification of a legal agreement between two parties, being negotiated or having been executed. This includes the baseline information and the optional specialised elections
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: agreementDate Description: The date on which the legal agreement has been agreed between the parties. This corresponds to the Date of Deed in an English Law document.
--     * Slot: effectiveDate Description: The date on which, or as of which, the agreement is effective, if different from the agreement date. It is expected that it will most often correspond to the agreement date, although there could be situations where the parties will explicitly agree on a distinct effective date.
--     * Slot: agreementTerms_id Description: Specification of the content of the legal agreement.
--     * Slot: umbrellaAgreement_id Description: Specifies a set of legal entities which are part of a legal agreement beyond the two contracting parties to that agreement.
--     * Slot: legalAgreementIdentification_id Description: The type of legal agreement, identified via a set of composable attributes: agreementName, publisher, governing law and version, e.g. ISDA 2013 Standard Credit Support Annex English Law.
-- # Class: LegalAgreementBase Description: Specifies the legal agreement baseline information, being negotiated or having been executed. It excludes specialized elections
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: agreementDate Description: The date on which the legal agreement has been agreed between the parties. This corresponds to the Date of Deed in an English Law document.
--     * Slot: effectiveDate Description: The date on which, or as of which, the agreement is effective, if different from the agreement date. It is expected that it will most often correspond to the agreement date, although there could be situations where the parties will explicitly agree on a distinct effective date.
--     * Slot: legalAgreementIdentification_id Description: The type of legal agreement, identified via a set of composable attributes: agreementName, publisher, governing law and version, e.g. ISDA 2013 Standard Credit Support Annex English Law.
-- # Class: LegalAgreementIdentification Description: Specifies the type of legal agreement, identified via a set of composable attributes: agreementName, publisher, governing law and version, e.g. ISDA 2013 Standard Credit Support Annex English Law.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: publisher Description: The legal agreement publisher, e.g. ISDA.
--     * Slot: governingLaw Description: The law governing the legal agreement, e.g. English Law, New York Law or Japanese Law.
--     * Slot: vintage Description: In the case where successive definitions of the legal agreement have been developed, the vintage identification. This is typically (but not necessarily) done by referencing the year, e.g. 2013 in the case of the ISDA 2013 Standard Credit Support Annex.
--     * Slot: agreementName_id Description: The legal agreement name, e.g. Credit Support Annex for Variation Margin.
-- # Class: NonLegalEntity Description: Specifies a non-legal entity that exists in the agreement with a defined relationship to a Legal entity to the agreement
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: identifier Description: Specifies the unique identifier value for a non-legal entity such as a sleeve, or sub account, that is a party to the agreement and has a relationship with a legal entity defined on the agreement.
--     * Slot: identifierType Description: Specifies the Identifier type for a non-Legal entity to the agreement, for example the use of an alert code to uniquely identify a non-Legal entity.
-- # Class: NoticeContactInformation Description: Specifies notice information including address and, optionally, an associated person. This type also supports the ISDA CSA representation as a single string, through the address attribute in Contact Information.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: additionalInformation Description: Additional information on the recipient.
-- # Class: NoticeInformationElection Description: Specifies the party reference and the associated notice and contact information.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: partyReference Description: The party to which the election and details apply.
--     * Slot: primaryContactInformation_id Description: The main notice/address information of the party.
-- # Class: OtherAgreement Description: A class for defining an agreement executed between parties.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: version Description: The version of the agreement.
--     * Slot: identifier Description: An identifier that has been created to identify the agreement.
--     * Slot: otherAgreementType Description: The agreement executed between the parties and intended to govern product-specific derivatives transactions between those parties.
--     * Slot: date Description: The date on which the agreement was signed.
-- # Class: OtherAgreementTerms Description: A class to specify a related legal agreement. For example, ISDA 2016 Credit Support Annex for Initial Margin, paragraph 13, General Principles, (s): Other CSA and Japanese Law CSA (VM). | ISDA 2016 Credit Support Annex for Variation Margin, paragraph 13, (o): Other CSA.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isSpecified Description: The qualification of whether some other related agreement is specified (True) or not (False).
--     * Slot: legalDocument Description: The specification of this other agreement, when the qualification is True.
-- # Class: Resource Description: Describes the resource that contains the media representation of a business event (i.e used for stating the Publicly Available Information). For example, can describe a file or a URL that represents the event. This type is an extended version of a type defined by RIXML (www.rixml.org). Rosetta restricts the FpML implementation by not providing the ability to associated a document in hexadecimalBinary or base64Binary until such time that actual use cases will come up.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: name Description: The name of the resource. It is specified as a NormalizedString in FpML.
--     * Slot: url Description: Indicates where the resource can be found, as a URL that references the information on a web server accessible to the message recipient.
--     * Slot: resourceId Description: The unique identifier of the resource within the event. FpML specifies this element of type resourceIdScheme but with no specified value.
--     * Slot: resourceType Description: A description of the type of the resource, e.g. a confirmation.
--     * Slot: language Description: Indicates the language of the resource, described using the ISO 639-2/T Code.
--     * Slot: sizeInBytes Description: Indicates the size of the resource in bytes. It could be used by the end user to estimate the download time and storage needs.
--     * Slot: mimeType Description: Indicates the type of media used to store the content. mimeType is used to determine the software product(s) that can read the content. MIME Types are described in RFC 2046.
--     * Slot: comments Description: Any additional comments that are deemed necessary. For example, which software version is required to open the document? Or, how does this resource relate to the others for this event?
--     * Slot: string Description: Provides extra information as string. In case the extra information is in XML format, a CDATA section must be placed around the source message to prevent its interpretation as XML content.
--     * Slot: length_id Description: Indicates the length of the resource. For example, if the resource were a PDF file, the length would be in pages.
-- # Class: ResourceLength Description: A class to indicate the length of the resource.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: lengthUnit Description: The length unit of the resource. For example, pages (pdf, text documents) or time (audio, video files).
--     * Slot: lengthValue Description: The length value of the resource.
-- # Class: TransferContactInformation Description: Specifies transfer information including address and, optionally, an associated account. This type also supports the ISDA CSA representation as a single string, through the address attribute in Contact Information.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: additionalInformation Description: Additional transfer information.
-- # Class: TransferInformationElection Description: Specifies the party reference and the associated transfer & contact information.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: partyReference Description: The party to which the election and details apply.
--     * Slot: primaryContactInformation_id Description: The main notice/address and account information of the party.
-- # Class: UmbrellaAgreement Description: Specifies the set of agreements, the parties of which are set within UmbrellaAgreementSet, beyond the two contracting parties to that agreement.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: UmbrellaAgreementParty Description: Specifies the entities that are part of the umbrella agreement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: actingAs Description: Specifies the CounterpartyRoleEnum, e.g. either Party1 or Party2, that is associated to the party.
--     * Slot: partyRole Description: Represents the legal role that each defined entity to the agreement performs within the structure of that agreement.
--     * Slot: party_id Description: Specifies the party to the umbrella agreement
--     * Slot: nonLegalEntity_id Description: Specifies a non-legal entity that exists in the agreement with a defined relationship to a Legal entity to the agreement.
--     * Slot: parentParty_id Description: Represents the identification of a parent child relationship between two entities in the Umbrella agreement, allowing non-legal entities to be linked to the appropriate legal entity and allowing funds, portfolio or managed accounts to be linked to their applicable Investment Manager or Agent within the agreement.
-- # Class: UmbrellaAgreementSet Description: Represents the groups of agreement term elections that exist within the agreement and to which entities that particular group of elections apply. Where all entities under the umbrella have the same set of elections only one agreement set will exist. At least one agreement set must be defined for an Umbrella agreement
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: additionalLanguage Description: Represents any additional language that may need to be captured regarding the structure or application of terms that may exist for the agreement.
--     * Slot: agreement_id Description: Specification of the standard set of terms that define a legal agreement.
-- # Class: AggregationParameters Description: Parameters to be used to filter events that are relevant to a given portfolio in order to calculate the state of this portfolio. The attributes correspond to all the possible aggregation criteria that can be used and these criteria can be combined. All the attributes are optional.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: dateTime Description: To aggregate as of a particular date
--     * Slot: totalPosition Description: Specifies whether to calculate total position to given date, or only daily position for the given date.
--     * Slot: positionStatus Description: To aggregate based on position status (EXECUTED, SETTLED etc)
-- # Class: AvailableInventory Description: A data type that can be used to describe the inventory of securities that a party holds. The securities are held in the AvailableInventoryRecord, with each item in the array being an individual security and its associated criteria. Criteria can include the quantity available, the rate at which the security is available to borrow at, as well as other details that can affect the decision as to whether a party wants to utilise the securities listed.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: availableInventoryType Description: Defines the purpose of this inventory.
--     * Slot: comment Description: Optional comments for this group of inventory records.
--     * Slot: identifier_id Description: Unique identifier for this group. This can be used to uniquely identify a group of inventory records.
--     * Slot: messageInformation_id Description: Allows details related to the availability messaging use case to be defined
-- # Class: AvailableInventoryRecord Description: An individual piece of available inventory. This represents a single security and its associated criteria. The criteria are used to describe any restrictions on the securities.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: expirationDateTime Description: There may be a set period/time restriction associated to the security.
--     * Slot: comment Description: Optional comment for this specific piece of inventory.
--     * Slot: quantity_id Description: The quantity of the security
--     * Slot: interestRate_id Description: An optional element which can be used to hold a rate associated to this piece of availability.
--     * Slot: dividendTerms_id Description: Specifies the dividend requirements if applicable.
--     * Slot: identifier_id Description: Unique identifier for this record. This can be used to uniquely identify a specific piece of inventory.
--     * Slot: security_id Description: The security details.
-- # Class: ContractBase Description: Encapsulates data features common to trade and position.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: contractDetails_id Description: Represents information specific to trades or positions involving contractual products.
--     * Slot: executionDetails_id Description: Defines specific attributes that relate to trade or position executions.
--     * Slot: collateral_id Description: Represents the collateral obligations of a party.
-- # Class: CounterpartyPosition Description: A Position describes the accumulated effect of a set of securities or financial transactions.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: openDateTime Description: The date and time when the position was opened.
--     * Slot: positionBase_id Description: Encapsulates the core constituents that characterize a position.
--     * Slot: contractDetails_id Description: Represents information specific to trades or positions involving contractual products.
--     * Slot: executionDetails_id Description: Defines specific attributes that relate to trade or position executions.
--     * Slot: collateral_id Description: Represents the collateral obligations of a party.
-- # Class: Inventory Description: A data type that can be used to describe an inventory of securities.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: InventoryRecord Description: An individual piece of inventory. This represents a single security.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: identifier_id Description: Unique identifier for this record. This can be used to uniquely identify a specific piece of inventory.
--     * Slot: security_id Description: The security details.
-- # Class: Portfolio Description: A Portfolio represents an aggregation of multiple Positions, by describing the parameters that this Portfolio should be aggregated based on. The resulting PortfolioState is calculated using these aggregation parameters as inputs, by aggregating all the Events that are relevant to this Portfolio. The concept of Portfolio works at all levels in the model: from the highest for a given LegalEntity for instance, to the lowest to account for security substitutions in a secutity financing transaction. As such, Portfolio can be used either above or below the Contract level.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: aggregationParameters_id Description: Describes the portfolio by describing how to aggregate all its relevant Events.
--     * Slot: portfolioState_id Description: Describes the state of the Portfolio as a list of Positions resulting from the aggregation.
-- # Class: PortfolioState Description: State-full representation of a Portfolio that describes all the positions held at a given time, in various states which can be either traded, settled, etc., with lineage information to the previous state
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: lineage_id Description: Pointer to the previous PortfolioState and new Event(s) leading to the current (new) state. Previous PortfolioState in the Lineage can be Null in case this is the start of the chain of Events.
-- # Class: Position Description: A Position describes how much of a given Product is being held and constitutes the atomic element of a Portfolio.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: product_id Description: The product underlying the position.
--     * Slot: asset_id Description: The asset that underlies the position.
--     * Slot: cashBalance_id Description: The aggregate cost of proceeds.
--     * Slot: tradeReference_id Description: Reference to the Contract, in case product is contractual and the contract has been formed.
-- # Class: PositionBase Description: Base class to describe a Position, which could be a group of products (e.g. trade portfolio) or a group of assets (e.g. collateral portfolio).
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: product_id Description: The product underlying the position.
--     * Slot: asset_id Description: The asset that underlies the position.
--     * Slot: cashBalance_id Description: The aggregate cost of proceeds.
--     * Slot: tradeReference_id Description: Reference to the Contract, in case product is contractual and the contract has been formed.
-- # Class: SecurityLocate Description: A locate is an approval from a broker that needs to be obtained prior to effecting a short sale in an equity security. Similar to security availability, a borrower can request a single or multiple securities, but at least one must be requested.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: availableInventoryType Description: Defines the purpose of this inventory.
--     * Slot: comment Description: Optional comments for this group of inventory records.
--     * Slot: identifier_id Description: Unique identifier for this group. This can be used to uniquely identify a group of inventory records.
--     * Slot: messageInformation_id Description: Allows details related to the availability messaging use case to be defined
-- # Class: CreditLimitInformation Description: A class to represent the credit limit utilisation information.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: CreditLimitUtilisation Description: Credit limit utilisation breakdown by executed trades and pending orders.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: executed_id Description: Credit limit utilisation attributable to executed trades.
--     * Slot: pending_id Description: Credit limit utilisation attributable to pending unexecuted orders.
-- # Class: CreditLimitUtilisationPosition
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: shortPosition Description: Credit limit utilisation attributable to short positions.
--     * Slot: longPosition Description: Credit limit utilisation attributable to long positions.
--     * Slot: global Description: Global credit limit utilisation amount, agnostic of long/short position direction.
-- # Class: CustomisedWorkflow Description: In its initial iteration, this class is meant to support the DTCC TIW workflow information.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: itemName Description: In this initial iteration, this corresponds to the DTCC TIW element name.
--     * Slot: itemValue Description: In this initial iteration, this corresponds to the DTCC value.
-- # Class: EventInstruction Description: Specifies instructions to create a BusinessEvent.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: intent Description: The intent attribute is meant to be specified when the event qualification cannot be programmatically inferred from the event features. As a result it is only associated with those primitives that can give way to such ambiguity, the quantityChange being one of those. An example of such is a reduction in the trade notional, which could be interpreted as either a trade correction (unless a maximum period of time post-event is specified as part of the qualification), a partial termination or a portfolio rebalancing in the case of an equity swap. On the other hand, an event such as the exercise is not expected to have an associated intent as there should not be ambiguity.
--     * Slot: corporateActionIntent
--     * Slot: eventDate Description: Specifies the date on which the event is taking place. This date is equal to the trade date in the case of a simple execution. However it can be different from the trade date, for example in the case of a partial termination.
--     * Slot: effectiveDate Description: The date on which the event contractually takes effect, when different from the event date.
--     * Slot: eventTime_id Description: The time and zone of the date in which the event is taking place.
--     * Slot: effectiveTime_id Description: The time and zone of the date in which the event contractually takes effect.
--     * Slot: packageInformation_id Description: Specifies the package information in case the business event represents several trades executed as a package (hence this attribute is optional). The package information is only instantiated once at the business event level to preserve referential integrity, whereas individual trades make reference to it to identify that they are part of a package.
-- # Class: EventTimestamp Description: A class to represent the various set of timestamps that can be associated with lifecycle events, as a collection of [dateTime, qualifier].
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: dateTime Description: The CDM specifies that the zoned date time is to be expressed in accordance with ISO 8601, either as UTC as an offset to UTC.
--     * Slot: qualification Description: The timestamp qualifier is specified through an enumeration because the experience of integrating the DTCC and CME data representations suggests that a wide set of timestamps are currently utilized among service providers, while there is not at present an objective set of criteria that could help suggest a defined set of timestamps as part of the CDM. At some future point, one possible baseline could be developed from the review of the set of timestamps specified across regulatory regimes and regulations (incl. regulations such as high frequency trading). Also, the integration with a further set of implementations and the specification of business workflows such as clearing as part of the CDM development should help confirm the implementation approach in this respect.
-- # Class: LimitApplicable
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: limitType Description: Standard code to indicate which type of credit line is being referred to - i.e. IM, DV01, PV01, CS01, Notional, Clip Size, Notional, maximumOrderQuantity.
--     * Slot: clipSize Description: This element is required in FpML, optional in CDM for the purpose of accommodating the CME data representation while making reference to the FpML one.
--     * Slot: amountUtilized Description: The limit utilised by all the cleared trades for the limit level and limit type. While the attribute is of type integer in FpML and the CME schema, it has been specified to be of type number in the CDM to take into consideration java size limits as well as for consistency purposes with the way most monetary amounts are expressed.
--     * Slot: amountRemaining Description: The limit remaining for the limit level and limit type. This does not take into account any pending trades. While the attribute is of type integer in FpML and the CME schema, it has been specified to be of type number in the CDM to take into consideration java size limits as well as for consistency purposes with the way most monetary amounts are expressed.
--     * Slot: currency Description: The currency in which the applicable limit is denominated. The list of valid currencies is not presently positioned as an enumeration as part of the CDM because that scope is limited to the values specified by ISDA and FpML. As a result, implementers have to make reference to the relevant standard, such as the ISO 4217 standard for currency codes.
--     * Slot: utilization_id
--     * Slot: velocity_id
-- # Class: LimitApplicableExtended Description: A class to represent the CDM attributes that are not part of the FpML standard. Once broader usage is confirmed, it is expected that those two classes can be collapsed.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: limitLevel Description: The level at which the limit is set: customer business, proprietary business or account level. This attribute is specified as a string as part of the CME clearing confirmation specification.
--     * Slot: limitAmount Description: The total limit available for the limit level and limit type. While the attribute is of type integer in the CME schema, it has been specified to be of type number in the CDM to take into consideration java size limits as well as for consistency purposes with the way most monetary amounts are expressed.
--     * Slot: limitImpactDueToTrade Description: The limit utilized by this specific trade. While the attribute is of type integer in the CME schema, it has been specified to be of type number in the CDM to take into consideration java size limits as well as for consistency purposes with the way most monetary amounts are expressed.
--     * Slot: limitType Description: Standard code to indicate which type of credit line is being referred to - i.e. IM, DV01, PV01, CS01, Notional, Clip Size, Notional, maximumOrderQuantity.
--     * Slot: clipSize Description: This element is required in FpML, optional in CDM for the purpose of accommodating the CME data representation while making reference to the FpML one.
--     * Slot: amountUtilized Description: The limit utilised by all the cleared trades for the limit level and limit type. While the attribute is of type integer in FpML and the CME schema, it has been specified to be of type number in the CDM to take into consideration java size limits as well as for consistency purposes with the way most monetary amounts are expressed.
--     * Slot: amountRemaining Description: The limit remaining for the limit level and limit type. This does not take into account any pending trades. While the attribute is of type integer in FpML and the CME schema, it has been specified to be of type number in the CDM to take into consideration java size limits as well as for consistency purposes with the way most monetary amounts are expressed.
--     * Slot: currency Description: The currency in which the applicable limit is denominated. The list of valid currencies is not presently positioned as an enumeration as part of the CDM because that scope is limited to the values specified by ISDA and FpML. As a result, implementers have to make reference to the relevant standard, such as the ISO 4217 standard for currency codes.
--     * Slot: utilization_id
--     * Slot: velocity_id
-- # Class: MessageInformation Description: This class corresponds to the components of the FpML MessageHeader.model.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: messageId Description: A unique identifier assigned to the message.
--     * Slot: sentBy Description: The identifier for the originator of a message instance.
-- # Class: PartyCustomisedWorkflow Description: A class to specify a party-related, non-standardized data in a generic form.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: partyName Description: The party name to which the workflow pertains to.
--     * Slot: partyReference_id Description: Reference to the party to which the workflow pertains to.
-- # Class: Velocity
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: periodMultiplier
--     * Slot: period
-- # Class: Workflow Description: A collection of workflow steps which together make up an entire workflow sequence.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: WorkflowState Description: A class to specify workflow information, which is conceptually applicable to all lifecycle events.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: workflowStatus Description: The workflow status indicator, e.g. Accepted, Rejected, ...
--     * Slot: comment Description: A comment field to be associated with the workflow, e.g. to specify why a transaction event was rejected by a party.
--     * Slot: warehouseIdentity Description: The identity of the warehouse, if any, that is executing that workflow step.
-- # Class: WorkflowStep Description: A workflow step represents the state of a business event. The workflow step contains a reference to a previous WorkflowStep in order to preserve lineage. A workflow step is accepted if it contains a business event, proposed if proposedEvent is present and is rejected if the rejected flag is set.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: rejected Description: Flags this step as rejected.
--     * Slot: action Description: Specifies whether the event is a new, a correction or a cancellation.
--     * Slot: businessEvent_id Description: Life cycle event for the step.
--     * Slot: counterpartyPositionBusinessEvent_id Description: Documents the life cycle event for a position.
--     * Slot: proposedEvent_id Description: The proposed event for a workflow step.
--     * Slot: previousWorkflowStep_id Description: Optional previous workflow step that provides lineage to workflow steps that precedes it.
--     * Slot: nextEvent_id Description: The intended next event can be specified, even if the instructions are not known yet.
--     * Slot: messageInformation_id Description: Contains all information pertaining the FpML messaging header
--     * Slot: creditLimitInformation_id
--     * Slot: workflowState_id Description: The event workflow information, i.e. the workflow status, the associated comment and the partyCustomisedWorkflow which purpose is to provide the ability to associate custom workflow information to the CDM.
-- # Class: WorkflowStepApproval Description: Party approvals associated to the current WorkflowStep.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: approved Description: Flag denoting whether the workflow step is approved or not
--     * Slot: rejectedReason Description: Optional reason for rejecting the workflow step
--     * Slot: timestamp_id Description: Timestamp of the approval
--     * Slot: party_id Description: Reference to the Party who is approving/rejecting this workflow step
-- # Class: ClauseLibraryClause Description: Defines clauses that make up the Agreement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: name Description: Optional textual description of the clause.
--     * Slot: identifier_id Description: Unique identifier for the clause.
-- # Class: ClauseLibraryClauseVariant Description: Sets the details for a specific variant associated to a clause in the Agreement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: name Description: Optional textual description of the variant.
--     * Slot: identifier_id Description: Unique identifier for this variant.
-- # Class: ClauseLibrarySchedule Description: The set of elections which specify an Agreement.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: ClauseLibraryVariableSet Description: Defines a type where additional variables associated to clauses and their variants can be described.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: name Description: The name of the variable.
--     * Slot: value Description: The value for this variable.
-- # Class: BrokerConfirmation Description: Identifies the market sector in which the trade has been arranged.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: brokerConfirmationType Description: The type of broker confirmation executed between the parties.
-- # Class: EquityMasterConfirmation Description: Specification for General Terms and Elections of an Equity Master Confirmation that is applicable across multiple Equity confirmations and is referenced by each of these confirmations, an example of which being the 2018 ISDA CDM Equity Confirmation for Security Equity Swap.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: EquitySwapMasterConfirmation2018 Description: Specification for the General Terms and Relationship Supplement Elections as provided in the 2018 ISDA CDM Equity Confirmation for Security Equity Swap.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: typeOfSwapElection Description: Per Part 1 Section 4, 'Dividend Obligations', of the 2018 ISDA CDM Equity Confirmation, Para 4.2 'Dividend Returns'.
--     * Slot: linearInterpolationElection Description: Per Part 1 Section 3, 'Floating Obligations', of the 2018 ISDA CDM Equity Confirmation. Para 3.3.
--     * Slot: pricingMethodElection_id Description: Per Part 1 Section 5, 'Pricing', of the 2018 ISDA CDM Equity Confirmation, Para 5.1.
--     * Slot: settlementTerms_id Description: Per Part 1 Section 8, 'Settlement', of the 2018 ISDA CDM Equity Confirmation for Security Equity Swap.
--     * Slot: valuationDates_id Description: The parameters used to generate the 'Equity Valuation Dates' schedule, including the Effective Date and Termination Date for the Swap.
--     * Slot: equityCashSettlementDates_id Description: The parameters used to generate the payment date schedule, relative to the equityCalculationPeriod. Per Part 1 Section 12, 'Definitions', of the 2018 ISDA CDM Equity Confirmation. Para 73.
-- # Class: MasterConfirmationBase Description: Legal agreement specification for General Terms and Elections that are applicable across multiple confirmations and are referenced by these confirmations.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: AdditionalObligations Description: The election of party specific additional obligations applicable to the agreement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: party Description: The party that the additional obligations apply to.
--     * Slot: additionalObligations Description: The party specific additional obligations applicable to the agreement.
-- # Class: AdditionalRepresentation Description: A class to specify the Additional Representation.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: customElection Description: A supplemental custom election that might be specified by the parties for the purpose of specifying the Additional Representation.
-- # Class: AdditionalRepresentationElection Description: A class to specify the parties' Additional Representation(s) election.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: party Description: The elective party.
--     * Slot: isApplicable Description: The Additional Representation is applicable when True, and not applicable when False.
--     * Slot: additionalLanguage Description: Details of any Additional Representations given by the relevant parties in relation to the collateral arrangement.
-- # Class: AdditionalRepresentations Description: A class to specify Additional Representations that may be applicable to an agreement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: regulatoryComplianceRepresentation Description: The qualification of whether Additional Information related to Regulatory Compliance and Concentration Limits is applicable or not.
--     * Slot: additionalRepresentation_id Description: The specification of the Additional Representation that may be applicable to the agreement.
-- # Class: AdditionalRightsEvent Description: A class to specify the Pledgor/Obligor/Chargor Additional Rights Event election.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isApplicable Description: The Pledgor Additional Rights Event election is applicable when True, and not applicable when False.
--     * Slot: qualification Description: The qualification of the Pledgor Additional Rights Event election, when specified.
-- # Class: AdditionalType Description: The specification of the Additional Type of transaction that can require the collection or delivery of initial margin under a given regulatory regime for the purposes of Covered Transactions.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: standardValue Description: The qualification of the Additional Type of transaction that can require the collection or delivery of initial margin when specified as a standard value.
--     * Slot: customValue Description: The qualification of the Additional Type of transaction that can require the collection or delivery of initial margin when specified as a custom value by the parties to the legal agreement.
-- # Class: AddressesForTransfer Description: Specifies the address for transfer as specified by the respective parties to the agreement.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: AllDirectionRating Description: Used to combine two or more Ratings and associated direction using AND logic.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: AllEligibilityToHoldCollateralCriteria Description: Used to combine two or more Criteria using AND logic.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: AmendmentEffectiveDate Description: A class to specify the effective date of the Amendment to Termination Currency. This date can be specified as either an actual date, a specific date (e.g. the annex date) or as a custom provision.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: date Description: The effective date of the Amendment to Termination Currency when specified as an actual date.
--     * Slot: specificDate Description: The effective date of the Amendment to Termination Currency when specified as relative to another date (e.g. the annex date).
--     * Slot: customProvision Description: The effective date of the Amendment to Termination Currency when specified as a non normalized custom provision.
-- # Class: AmountOfNetCapital Description: The amount of net capital.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: amountOfNetCapital_id Description: The amount of net capital.
-- # Class: AnyDirectionRating Description: Used to combine two or more Ratings and associated direction using OR logic.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: AnyEligibilityToHoldCollateralCriteria Description: Used to combine two or more Criteria using OR logic.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: ApplicableRegime Description: A class to specify the applicable regulatory regime(s) that parties to a legal agreement, such as the ISDA 2016 and 2018 CSA for Initial Margin, might be subject to.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: additionalType Description: The CDM's additionalType attribute; each class's slot_usage gives its meaning.
--     * Slot: regime Description: The applicable regulatory regime, as specified through an enumeration.
--     * Slot: additionalRegime Description: The additional regulatory regime as specified by the parties.
--     * Slot: additionalTerms Description: The bespoke Additional Type for the purposes of Covered Transactions (IM).
-- # Class: AppropriatedCollateralValuation Description: A class to specify the Valuation of Appropriated Collateral.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isSpecified Description: The qualification of whether the Valuation of Appropriate Collateral provision is applicable (True) or not applicable (False).
--     * Slot: election Description: The parties' election that qualify the Valuation of Appropriate Collateral in the case where it is deemed applicable.
-- # Class: BaseAndEligibleCurrency Description: The base and eligible currency(ies) for the document as specified by the parties to the agreement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: baseCurrency Description: The common agreed currency into which relevant amounts of all collateral arrangements between the parties are converted, or if not an actual currency, the process through which this is determined. Where hardcoded (e.g. under the 1994 ISDA Credit Support Annex (Security Interest NY Law)), the currency that effectively performs this function.
--     * Slot: baseCurrencyTerminationCurrency Description: A flag detailing whether the Base Currency is set to the Termination Currency as defined in the related Master Agreement.
--     * Slot: baseCurrencyOther Description: Utilised where the clause data structure is not able to capture a material aspect of the clause.
--     * Slot: eligibleCurrencyInclBaseCurrency Description: A flag detailing whether the Base Currency is included as an Eligible Currency.
--     * Slot: eligibleCurrencyOther Description: Utilised where the clause data structure is not able to capture a material aspect of the clause.
-- # Class: BespokeCalculationDate Description: A class to specify bespoke Calculation Date terms for the purposes of Initial Margin.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isApplicable Description: Additional Calculation Date terms are applicable when True and not applicable when False.
--     * Slot: calculationDateImTerms Description: The Additional Calculation Date terms for the purposes of Initial Margin.
-- # Class: BespokeCalculationTime Description: A class to specify additional Calculation Time terms for the purposes of Initial Margin.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: asCalculationAgent Description: If set to True, the Calculation Time for Initial Margin is the time as of which the Calculation Agent (IM) computes its end of day valuations of derivatives transactions.
--     * Slot: bespokeCalculationTimeTerms Description: Additional Terms applicable to Calculation Time for Initial Margin.
-- # Class: BespokeTransferTiming Description: A class to specify any bespoke Transfer Timing language by each party to the agreement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isApplicable Description: A boolean flag to specify whether bespoke transfer terms are applicable or not.
--     * Slot: bespokeTransferTimingTerms Description: The bespoke transfer timing terms applicable to the agreement.
-- # Class: CSADeliveryAmount Description: In respect of a Valuation Date, the amount of collateral which a party is entitled to demand to be transferred to it as a Delivery Amount.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: deliveryAmount Description: Specifies whether the meaning of Delivery Amount follows the pre-print definition or deviates from this (either based on a rating or some other methodology).
--     * Slot: additionalLanguage Description: The additional language that might be specified by the parties to the legal agreement.
-- # Class: CSAIndependentAmount Description: Sets out the additional amount of collateral that is required to be delivered by that party irrespective of the mark-to-market exposure under the related Transactions. It may take the form of a fixed amount, or be determined using credit ratings.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: additionalLanguage Description: The additional language that might be specified by the parties to the legal agreement.
-- # Class: CSAMinimumTransferAmountVariableSet Description: Defines a combination of Rating Agency, Rating Value, amount and Currency code.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: name Description: The name of the Rating Agency.
--     * Slot: value Description: The value assigned to the rating.
--     * Slot: amount Description: The Minimum Transfer Amount (MTA) applicable to the Rating.
--     * Slot: amountIsInfinity Description: A flag that defines the Minimum Transfer Amount (MTA) as Infinity.
-- # Class: CSAReturnAmount Description: In respect of a Valuation Date, the amount of collateral which a party is entitled to demand to be recalled to it as a Return Amount.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: returnAmount Description: Specifies whether the meaning of Return Amount follows the pre-print definition or deviates from this (either based on a rating or some other methodology).
-- # Class: CSAThresholdVariableSet Description: Defines a combination of Rating Agency, Rating Value, Threshold amount and Currency code.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: name Description: The relevant rating agency.
--     * Slot: value Description: Rating applicable to the party from a given rating agency.
--     * Slot: amount Description: The amount value applicable to the Threshold.
-- # Class: CSAValuationDate Description: Specifies the date on which the value of collateral or exposure are calculated in accordance with the agreement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: date Description: Defines whether a date is defined by a certain day of the week or a particular date in the month. If not specified here, then additional language must be used.
--     * Slot: day Description: Specific day(s) or day of the week, if any, specified for Valuation Time.
--     * Slot: calendarDay Description: Defines the day of the calendar if this is specified for in the ValuationDateDateEnum.
--     * Slot: frequency Description: Defines the regularity of the date specified for the Valuation Date.
--     * Slot: additionalLanguage Description: The additional language that might be specified by the parties to the legal agreement.
-- # Class: CalculationAgentTerms Description: Details of the party calculating the value of collateral to be delivered or returned.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: party Description: The party which is specified as Calculation Agent for Initial Margin.
--     * Slot: bespokeCalculationAgentTerms Description: The Calculation Agent (IM) terms when specified.
-- # Class: CalculationAndTimingBase Description: A logical container designed to hold a set of related data. In this case, designed to hold a set of clauses that are common amongst Legacy (1994/95), Variation Margin and Initial Margin Credit Support Documents in regards to Calculation, Valuation and Timing terms.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: notificationTime_id Description: The time by which a demand for the Transfer of Eligible Credit Support (IM) or Posted Credit Support (IM) needs to be made in order for the transfer to take place in accordance with the Transfer Timing provisions.
-- # Class: CalculationAndTimingCollateralTransferAgreement Description: Specification of the Calculation, Valuation and Timing terms specific to the Initial Margin Credit Support Annex.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: cashSettlementDay
--     * Slot: securitiesSettlementDay
--     * Slot: calculationAgentTerms_id Description: Details of the party calculating the value of collateral to be delivered or returned.
--     * Slot: bespokeCalculationDate_id Description: The specification of bespoke Calculation Date terms for the purposes of Initial or Variation Margin by the parties to the agreement.
--     * Slot: bespokeCalculationTime_id Description: Bespoke terms to describe the time as of which such party (or the Calculation Agent (IM) (if applicale)) computes its end of day valuations of derivatives transactions.
--     * Slot: calculationDateLocation_id Description: The specified location where the credit exposure will be calculated by the respective parties.
--     * Slot: notificationTime_id Description: The time by which a demand for the Transfer of Eligible Credit Support (IM) or Posted Credit Support (IM) needs to be made in order for the transfer to take place in accordance with the Transfer Timing provisions.
-- # Class: CalculationAndTimingInitialMargin Description: Specification of the Calculation, Valuation and Timing terms specific to the Initial Margin Credit Support Annex.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: cashSettlementDay
--     * Slot: securitiesSettlementDay
--     * Slot: calculationAgentTerms_id Description: Details of the party calculating the value of collateral to be delivered or returned.
--     * Slot: bespokeCalculationDate_id Description: The specification of bespoke Calculation Date terms for the purposes of Initial or Variation Margin by the parties to the agreement.
--     * Slot: bespokeCalculationTime_id Description: Bespoke terms to describe the time as of which such party (or the Calculation Agent (IM) (if applicale)) computes its end of day valuations of derivatives transactions.
--     * Slot: calculationDateLocation_id Description: The specified location where the credit exposure will be calculated by the respective parties.
--     * Slot: notificationTime_id Description: The time by which a demand for the Transfer of Eligible Credit Support (IM) or Posted Credit Support (IM) needs to be made in order for the transfer to take place in accordance with the Transfer Timing provisions.
-- # Class: CalculationAndTimingLegacy Description: Specification of the Calculation, Valuation and Timing terms specific to the Legacy (1994/95) Credit Support Annex.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: valuationDate_id Description: Details of the days on which calculations are to be made to determine the Delivery Amount and/or Return Amount.
--     * Slot: valuationTime_id Description: Specifies the time on which the value of collateral or exposure are calculated in accordance with the agreement.
--     * Slot: valuationAgent_id Description: Details of the party calculating the value of collateral to be delivered or returned.
--     * Slot: notificationTime_id Description: The time by which a demand for the Transfer of Eligible Credit Support (IM) or Posted Credit Support (IM) needs to be made in order for the transfer to take place in accordance with the Transfer Timing provisions.
-- # Class: CalculationAndTimingVariationMargin Description: Specification of the Calculation, Valuation and Timing terms specific to the Variation Margin Credit Support Annex.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: valuationDate_id Description: Details of the days on which calculations are to be made to determine the Delivery Amount and/or Return Amount.
--     * Slot: valuationTime_id Description: Specifies the time on which the value of collateral or exposure are calculated in accordance with the agreement.
--     * Slot: valuationAgent_id Description: Details of the party valuating the collateral to be delivered or returned.
--     * Slot: valuationDateLocation_id Description: The specified location where the credit exposure will be calculated by the respective parties.
--     * Slot: notificationTime_id Description: The time by which a demand for the Transfer of Eligible Credit Support (IM) or Posted Credit Support (IM) needs to be made in order for the transfer to take place in accordance with the Transfer Timing provisions.
-- # Class: CalculationCurrencyElection Description: A class to specify the ISDA SIMM Calculation Currency.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: party Description: The party which the SIMM Calculation Currency qualification applies to.
--     * Slot: isBaseCurrency Description: The SIMM Calculation Currency (also known as SIMM Reporting Currency) means the Base Currency when True. It means a different currency when False. In that latter case, the SIMM Calculation Currency is specified as part of the currency attribute.
--     * Slot: currency Description: The currency in which the ISDA SIMM Calculation is denominated, when different from the Base Currency. The list of valid currencies is not presently positioned as an enumeration as part of the CDM because that scope is limited to the values specified by ISDA and FpML. As a result, implementers have to make reference to the relevant standard, such as the ISO 4217 standard for currency codes.
-- # Class: CollateralAccessBreach Description: A class to specify Collateral Access Breach language.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isApplicable Description: Collateral Access Breach terms are applicable when True and not applicable when False.
--     * Slot: cabEndDateElection Description: Determination of whether the Collateral Access Breach end date is a number of days (True) or specified (False).
--     * Slot: cabEndDate Description: The business days following the related Collateral Access Breach when the additional terms end.
--     * Slot: cabEndDateTerms Description: Specific terms for when Collateral Access Breach terms end.
-- # Class: CollateralManagementAgreement Description: A class to specify the Collateral Management Agreement election.
--     * Slot: id
-- # Class: CollateralManagementAgreementElection Description: A class to specify the Collateral Management Agreement election.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: party Description: The elective party.
--     * Slot: collateralManagementAgreement Description: The designated Collateral Management Agreement with respect to the elective party as the Obligee.
-- # Class: CollateralRounding Description: A class to specify the rounding methodology applicable to the Delivery Amount and the Return Amount.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: deliveryAmount Description: The nearest integral multiple of Base Currency units to which the Delivery Amount will be rounded in accordance with the specified rounding direction.
--     * Slot: deliveryDirection Description: The rounding rule applicable to the Delivery Amount (which can be (i) up to nearest; (ii) down to nearest).
--     * Slot: returnAmount Description: The nearest integral multiple of Base Currency units to which the Return Amount will be rounded in accordance with the specified rounding direction.
--     * Slot: returnDirection Description: The rounding rule applicable to the Return Amount (which can be (i) up to nearest; (ii) down to nearest).
--     * Slot: currency Description: The currency in which the Delivery Amount and Return Amount rounding amounts are specified.
--     * Slot: other Description: Utilised where the clause data structure is not able to capture a material aspect of the clause.
-- # Class: CollateralTransferAgreementElections Description: The set of elections which specify a Collateral Transfer Agreement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: identifiedCrossCurrencySwap Description: The qualification of whether cross-currency swaps need to be identified in the Confirmation so that the obligations to exchange principal be disregarded for the purpose of determining the Delivery Amount or Return Amount.
--     * Slot: interpretationTerms Description: The bespoke provision that might be specified by the parties to the agreement applicable to Interpretations.
--     * Slot: additionalAmendments Description: Any additional amendments that might be specified by the parties to the agreement.
--     * Slot: additionalBespokeTerms Description: Any additional terms that might be specified applicable.
--     * Slot: regime_id Description: The Regime Table provision , which determines the regulatory regime(s) applicable to each of the parties to the agreement.
--     * Slot: oneWayProvisions_id Description: The determination of whether the One Way Provisions are applicable (true) or not applicable (false).
--     * Slot: generalSimmElections_id Description: The specification of the ISDA SIMM Method for all Covered Transactions with respect to all Regimes.
--     * Slot: sensitivityMethodologies_id Description: The specification of methodologies to compute sensitivities specific to the agreement.
--     * Slot: fxHaircutCurrency_id Description: The reference currency for the purpose of specifying the FX Haircut relating to a posting obligation, as being either the Termination Currency or an FX Designated Currency.
--     * Slot: postingObligations_id Description: The security providers posting obligations.
--     * Slot: substitutedRegime_id Description: The specification of Additional regimes for purposes of determining whether a Regulatory Event has occurred.
--     * Slot: baseAndEligibleCurrency_id Description: The base and eligible currency(ies) for the document as specified by the parties to the agreement.
--     * Slot: creditSupportObligations_id Description: The Credit Support Obligations applicable to the agreement.
--     * Slot: calculationAndTiming_id Description: The set of elections for determining Valuation and Timing terms specific to the agreement.
--     * Slot: conditionsPrecedent_id Description: The set of elections that may overwrite the default Condition Precedent provision, and the set of provisions that are deemed Access Condition.
--     * Slot: substitution_id Description: The conditions under which the Security Provider can substitute posted collateral.
--     * Slot: disputeResolution_id Description: The election terms under which a party disputes (i) the Calculation Agents calculation of a Delivery Amount or a Return Amount, or (ii) the Value of any Transfer of Eligible Credit Support or Posted Credit Support.
--     * Slot: rightsEvents_id Description: The bespoke provisions that might be specified by the parties to the agreement to specify the rights of Security Taker and/or Security Provider when an Early Termination or Access Condition event has occurred.
--     * Slot: custodyArrangements_id Description: The Custodian and Segregated Account details in respect of each party to the agreement.
--     * Slot: additionalRepresentations_id Description: The specification Additional Representations that may be applicable to the agreement.
--     * Slot: demandsAndNotices_id Description: The optional specification of address where the demands, specifications and notices will be communicated to for each of the parties to the agreement.
--     * Slot: addressesForTransfer_id Description: The optional specification of address for transfer as specified by the respective parties to the agreement.
--     * Slot: otherAgreements_id Description: The bespoke definition of other agreement terms as specified by the parties to the agreement.
--     * Slot: terminationCurrencyAmendment_id Description: The bespoke provision that might be specified by the parties to the agreement applicable to Termination Currency. Unless specified the definition of Termination Currency has the meaning specified in the Schedule to the ISDA Master Agreement.
--     * Slot: minimumTransferAmountAmendment_id Description: The bespoke provision that might be specified by the parties to the agreement applicable to Minimum Transfer Amount. Unless specified the definition of Minimum Transfer Amount in any Other Regulatory CSA has the meaning specified in such Other Regulatory CSA.
--     * Slot: processAgent_id Description: The Process Agent that might be appointed by the parties to the agreement.
--     * Slot: jurisdictionRelatedTerms_id Description: The jurisdiction specific terms relevant to the agreement.
--     * Slot: pledgeeRepresentativeRider_id Description: The terms of the Rider for the ISDA Euroclear 2019 Collateral Transfer Agreement with respect to the use of a Pledgee Representative attached to this Agreement.
--     * Slot: masterAgreementDatedAsOfDate_id Description: Defines the date agreed by the parties as the date of the Collateral Transfer Agreement.
--     * Slot: finalReturns_id Description: A clause providing that final return collateral is to be provided without consideration of any Minimum Transfer Amount and collateral haircut.
-- # Class: CollateralTransferTiming Description: Specification of transfer / settlement timing for cash and securities collateral assuming that the notice is provided before the Notification Time (and with a 1LBD lag introduced if the notice is delivered after the Notification Time), and that securities allow for a further Local Business Day for transfer / settlement.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: transferSettlementTiming_id Description: Specification of transfer / settlement timing for cash and securities collateral assuming that the notice is provided before the Notification Time (and with a 1LBD lag introduced if the notice is delivered after the Notification Time), and that securities allow for a further Local Business Day for transfer / settlement.
--     * Slot: collateralTransferTimingDefinition_id Description: Bespoke language removing the pre-print requirement to transfer legal title of securities collateral through written instructions to the relevant depository institution or other securities intermediaries solely for the purposes of the 1994 New York Law Credit Support Annex.
-- # Class: CollateralTransferTimingDefinition Description: Bespoke language removing the pre-print requirement to transfer legal title of securities collateral through written instructions to the relevant depository institution or other securities intermediaries solely for the purposes of the 1994 New York Law Credit Support Annex.
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: isApplicable Description: A boolean flag to represent bespoke amendment to the pre-print definition of Transfer.
--     * Slot: additionalLanguage Description: The additional language that might be specified by the parties to the legal agreement.
-- # Class: CollateralValueMethod Description: Details how particular types of collateral are valued (other than in respect of a default).
--     * Slot: id
--     * Slot: cashCollateral Description: Details of how cash collateral is valued.
--     * Slot: securitiesCollateral Description: Details of how securities collateral is valued.
