-- # Class: QuantityChangeInstruction_change
--     * Slot: QuantityChangeInstruction_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: change_id Description: Quantity by which the trade is being increased, decreased or replaced, and the price at which such quantity change is agreed. The quantity change should always be specified as a positive number, with the direction (increase/decrease/replacement) being specified by the direction enumeration. A fee can also be associated to the quantity change by specifying a Price component of type CashPrice, including the corresponding settlement date and direction.
-- # Class: QuantityChangeInstruction_lotIdentifier
--     * Slot: QuantityChangeInstruction_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
--     * Slot: lotIdentifier_id Description: Identifier for the new lot (in case of increase) or for the existing lot to be changed(in case of decrease or replacement). This optional attribute is mandatory in case of a decrease or replacement if the initial trade state contains multiple trade lots.
-- # Class: Reset_observations
--     * Slot: Reset_id Description: Autocreated FK slot
